    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537070/research-assistant-i-ii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I / II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant I / II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537070 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I / II in the Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing ( BISP Lab — HKU MRI Research Laboratory ) of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.:537070）(to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year full-time basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) About the Position The Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering of Faculty of Engineering is seeking a highly organized, proactive, and detail-oriented individual to join the research team. The successful candidate will assist the laboratory’s principal investigator in managing critical administrative pipelines, from human ethics regulatory compliance to hands-on patient recruitment and laboratory procurement logistics. Key Responsibilites 1. Regulatory & Ethics Administration Assist in the preparation, submission, and management of human research ethics applications, amendments, and annual progress reports to relevant institutional review boards. Maintain meticulous documentation for ongoing studies. 2. Patient Recruitment & Coordination Coordinate and oversee patient/subject recruitment exercises, including managing outreach channels, screening potential participants, and scheduling visits. Act as a primary, professional point of contact for research participants, ensuring a smooth and supportive experience. Maintain accurate, confidential databases of recruitment metrics and participant tracking. 3. Financial Logistics & Procurement Manage day-to-day laboratory procurement, including sourcing quotes, preparing tenders, placing orders, and tracking deliveries of specialized equipment or consumables. Handle lab expense reimbursements and process miscellaneous payment arrangements with external suppliers. Liaise effectively with finance and purchasing departments to resolve budget, invoicing, or supply chain issues. Qualifications & Skills Education: A Bachelor’s degree. No working experience required Skills: Strong financial literacy with experience managing expenses, receipts, and vendor invoices. Exceptional organizational skills and the ability to multitask under tight deadlines. Proficient in MS Office softwares. Communication: Excellent written and spoken communication skills (Cantonese, Putonghua and English) for interacting with patients, institutional administrators, and commercial suppliers. Education: A Bachelor’s degree. No working experience required. Skills: Strong financial literacy with experience managing expenses, receipts, and vendor invoices. Exceptional organizational skills and the ability to multitask under tight deadlines. Proficient in MS Office softwares. Communication: Excellent written and spoken communication skills (Cantonese, Putonghua and English) for interacting with patients, institutional administrators, and commercial suppliers. What We Offer A dynamic, collaborative, and cutting-edge research environment. Opportunities to develop a diverse set of skills in research laboratory management. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until 3O November,2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537070 Research Assistant I / II Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537070 Research Assistant I / II Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
