    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537356/research-assistant-ii-data-analysis-lab-operations": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II (Data Analysis & Lab Operations)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant II (Data Analysis & Lab Operations) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537356 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing ( BISP Lab — HKU MRI Research Laboratory ) of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.:537356）(to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year full-time basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) About the Position The Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing in the Faculty of Engineering is seeking a versatile, proactive, and motivated Research Assistant to join the scientific research team. This position is ideal for an early-career researcher or technical specialist who enjoys a dynamic workload, balancing foundational data analysis with hands-on experimental support. You will work closely with laboratory members, postdocs, and graduate students to facilitate daily research workflows, handle routine signal and image processing pipelines, and ensure experimental logistics run seamlessly. Key Responsibilites 1. Routine Data Analysis & Processing Execute and streamline routine data analysis pipelines, specifically focusing on signal and image processing tasks. Assist lab members in data curation, quality control, and preparing datasets for statistical evaluation. Help maintain code repositories or scripts (e.g., in MATLAB, Python, or specialized imaging software) used for standard laboratory data pipelines. 2. Experimental Logistics & Support Coordinate daily laboratory logistics, including scheduling equipment usage, setting up experimental areas, and managing shared research resources. Assist in the preparation, execution, and breakdown of ongoing scientific experiments alongside senior team members. Maintain clean, organized, and compliant laboratory workstations in accordance with safety protocols. 3. Miscellaneous Team Assistance Provide ad-hoc technical and administrative support to laboratory personnel as unique project needs arise. Help maintain accurate experimental logs, lab notebooks, and internal data documentation. Qualifications & Skills Education: A Bachelor’s degree in Biomedical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Physics, Life Sciences, or a closely related quantitative/scientific discipline. . No working experience required Skills: Technical Skills: Foundational experience with programming languages or software relevant to data analysis and processing ( Python, C++, MATLAB, R, or equivalent ). Familiarity with basic signal processing concepts or digital image manipulation. Core Competencies: Strong organizational habits, a collaborative team-first mindset, and the ability to adapt to varying daily tasks in a fast-paced research environment. What We Offer Hands-on exposure to advanced research methodologies and state-of-the-art laboratory instrumentation. A supportive, mentorship-driven environment ideal for developing technical skills in data science and experimental execution. Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and institutional frameworks. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until 3O November,2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Face