    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537357/research-assistant-ii-artificial-intelligence": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II (Artificial Intelligence)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant II (Artificial Intelligence) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537357 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing ( BISP Lab — HKU MRI Research Laboratory ) of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.:537357）(to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year full-time basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) About the Position The Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing in the Faculty of Engineering is seeking a motivated and technically skilled Research Assistant to join the research team. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and implementation of computational methods for MRI research, including deep learning-based image analysis, data processing pipelines, and research computing infrastructure management. The position provides an excellent opportunity to work in a multidisciplinary environment involving medical imaging scientists, clinicians, engineers, and AI researchers. Key Responsibilites 1. Research Computing & Infrastructure Support Assist in the management and maintenance of laboratory computing resources, including Linux servers, NAS storage systems, and GPU workstations. Support installation, configuration, and maintenance of software environments for AI and medical imaging research. Manage computational workflows, data organization, and storage strategies for large-scale MRI datasets. Provide technical support for researchers using laboratory computing resources. 2. Research Project Support Collaborate with researchers and clinicians on ongoing MRI and AI projects. Assist with preparation of research documentation, technical reports, and publications. Participate in laboratory meetings and contribute to project development. Qualifications & Skills Education: Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Biomedical Engineering, Medical Physics, Electrical Engineering, Data Science, or related disciplines. No working experience required. Skills: Strong programming skills in Python. Experience with deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Familiarity with Linux environments and scientific computing workflows. Experience with Git and software development practices. Excellent communication and teamwork skills. What We Offer A dynamic and interdisciplinary research environment at the interface of MRI and artificial intelligence. Opportunities to develop expertise in medical AI, computational imaging, and research software development. Access to advanced MRI systems and high-performance computing resources. Opportunities to contribute to high-impact research publications and international conferences. Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience, with medical and dental benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until 3O November,2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537357 Research Assistant II (Artificial Intelligence) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537357 Research Assistant II (Artificial Intelligence) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
