    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537358/postdoctoral-fellow-artificial-intelligence-or-hardware-systems": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow (Artificial Intelligence or Hardware Systems)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Post-doctoral Fellow (Artificial Intelligence or Hardware Systems) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537358 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing ( BISP Lab — HKU MRI Research Laboratory ) of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.:537358）(to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year full-time basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) About the Position The Laboratory of Biomedical Imaging and Signal Processing in the Faculty of Engineering is seeking an outstanding and highly motivated Post-doctoral Fellow to join the research team working on advanced MRI technologies, artificial intelligence, computational medical imaging and hardware systems . The successful candidate will lead and contribute to innovative research projects involving AI-driven MRI analysis, deep learning methodology development, and clinical translation. The candidate will work closely with multidisciplinary collaborators, including clinicians, imaging scientists, and engineers, to develop advanced computational solutions for medical imaging applications. Key Responsibilites Research & Method Development Develop novel artificial intelligence and machine learning approaches for MRI image analysis. Design, implement, and validate deep learning algorithms for medical imaging applications. Conduct independent research and contribute to the advancement of computational MRI methods. Analyse large-scale MRI datasets and evaluate algorithm performance. Qualifications & Skills Education: PhD degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Biomedical Engineering, Medical Imaging, Medical Physics, Electrical / Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Research Experience: Strong publication / track record in in the use of artificial intelligence in medical imaging, artificial intelligence, computer vision, or related fields (AI); electrical/mechanical hardware systems (hardware). Demonstrated experience developing deep learning models and computational methods. Ability to conduct independent research and collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams. Skills: Advanced programming skills in Python. Strong experience with deep learning frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow). Excellent communication and teamwork skills. What We Offer A leading research environment focused on next-generation MRI and AI technologies. Opportunities to conduct internationally competitive research with clinical impact. Access to state-of-the-art MRI systems and advanced computing infrastructure. Support for publication, conference participation, and career development. Competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience, with medical and dental benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until 31 December,2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The