    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537396/senior-lecturer-lecturer": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer / Lecturer",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Senior Lecturer / Lecturer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537396 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Data and Systems Engineering (14400) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Lecturer / Lecturer in the Department of Data and Systems Engineering ( Ref.: 537396), to commence as soon as possible on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. The Department of Data and Systems Engineering is one of the five engineering departments in the Faculty of Engineering, offering B.Eng., M.Sc., M.Phil. and Ph.D. programmes in all major fields of data and systems engineering. The Department has strong research programs and excellent facilities for teaching and research. Information about the Department can be obtained at http://www.dase.hku.hk/ . Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in systems engineering, data science, industrial engineering, computer science or a related field, with a strong commitment to quality teaching. They should also have good interpersonal and communication skills in written and spoken English; and should be self-motivated, highly-organized and a good team player. Priority will be given to those who demonstrate strong track record of teaching experiences and skills in experiential learning. Those with more than five years of teaching experience at the tertiary level (or in an equivalent professional setting) who demonstrate outstanding pedagogical skills and leadership in curriculum design may be considered for appointment as Senior Lecturer. The appointee is expected to teach courses in, but not limited to, three subject clusters: (1) systems analytics including computing and programming, operations research, intelligent decision and analytics, industrial optimization; (2) cyber-physical systems including robotics and automation, IoT (Internet of Things), digital twins, cyber-physical systems, and smart industrial systems; and (3) engineering management including project management, quality management, operations management, supply chain and logistics management, and engineering economics. The appointees will be responsible for delivering quality teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Duties include: Delivering high-quality teaching and contributing to course design for undergraduate and postgraduate courses; Supervising student projects; Driving curriculum development and actively participating in knowledge exchange activities; and Contributing to departmental committees and administrative duties. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary Housing benefits will be provided for appointment as Senior Lecturer as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Applicants are highly encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until January 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537396 Senior Lecturer / Lecturer Department of Data and Systems Engineering (14400) Jan 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537396 Senior Lecturer / Lecturer Department of Data and Systems Engineering (14400) Jan 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537593/research-assistant-iii-several-posts": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537593 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in the Cancer Clinical Trials Unit, Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537593) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The Centre of Cancer Medicine is a platform to facilitate the academic development of cancer medicine and oncology, and is created to foster collaboration among the cognate disciplines/(sub)specialities within the Centre of Cancer Medicine/School of Clinical Medicine, and with other Schools/Departments/Institutes/Hospitals/Colleges. The Cancer Clinical Trials Unit is dedicated for the management, organization and conduction of oncology and related clinical research. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Life Sciences or related disciplines. They should also have good coordination and problem-solving skills, as well as good interpersonal and communication skills. Additionally, applicants should be committed to quality and compliance, detail-minded, able to handle multiple concurrent tasks, possess good time management skills, and be self-motivated. A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese) is a must.  Those with less experience may be considered for appointment as Research Assistant II. The selected individual will be responsible for managing and coordinating clinical trials. This includes, but is not limited to, recruiting and screening trial participants, conducting study-related procedures (such as phlebotomy), gathering data, processing samples, managing documentation, overseeing facility operations and ensuring quality control. Additionally, the role involves liaising with clinical trial sponsors, contract research organizations, and both internal and external partners. The appointee may also be tasked with various other responsibilities as needed. The selected individual will receive initial training upon joining, followed by ongoing cancer educational sessions during their employment. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online at the University’s career site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. and one reference letter. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 15 November, 2026, or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537593 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537593 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537603/postdoctoral-fellow-in-ionisable-lipid-chemistry-for-nucleic-acids-delivery": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in Ionisable Lipid Chemistry for Nucleic Acids Delivery",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in Ionisable Lipid Chemistry for Nucleic Acids Delivery The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537603 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in Ionisable Lipid Chemistry for Nucleic Acids Delivery (Ref.: 537603) We now invite applicants to join the JC STEM Lab of Nanomedicine for Advanced Therapy (PI: Professor Khuloud Al-Jamal) at the Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy. The aim of our lab is to use nanotechnology to better understand, diagnose and treat diseases with interests in cancer and neurodegenerative diseases. We are a highly collaborative and multidisciplinary lab eager to create an impact on people's lives taking research a step beyond the lab. Research projects we are looking to pursue are in the areas of extracellular vesicles & cell therapy, immunotherapy, nucleic acids therapeutics for brain cancer and neurodegenerative diseases. Duties and Responsibilities : Design, synthesise and optimise novel ionisable lipids for use in lipid nanoparticle (LNP) formulations, focusing on structure-activity relationships that enhance nucleic acid encapsulation, endosomal escape, and biocompatibility. Develop scale-up protocols for new ionisable lipid candidates, ensuring reproducibility and purity suitable for downstream formulation and in vivo testing. Characterise novel lipids using analytical techniques such as NMR, LC-MS, and HPLC to confirm structural identity, purity, and stability. Formulate and optimise LNPs incorporating newly synthesised ionisable lipids alongside helper lipids, PEG-lipids, and cholesterol, tuning molar ratios and manufacturing parameters to achieve target particle size, encapsulation efficiency, and payload stability. Evaluate the physicochemical properties of LNP formulations, including size, polydispersity, zeta potential, and nucleic acid loading, using dynamic light scattering and related techniques. Assess the stability, biocompatibility, and nucleic acid delivery performance of new lipid-based LNPs through in vitro assays prior to in vivo evaluation. Investigate structure-function relationships between lipid chemistry and LNP delivery efficiency, informing iterative design cycles for next-generation ionisable lipids. Collaborate closely with molecular biology and in vivo research teams to translate novel lipid chemistries into functional LNP-based platform technologies for gene editing and nucleic acid therapeutics. Maintain detailed records of synthetic procedures, characterisation data, and formulation parameters to support intellectual property development and regulatory documentation. Prepare technical reports, protocols, and contribute to manuscript and patent application writing. Collaborate with external partners and vendors on scale-up, custom synthesis, and quality control of lipid materials. Supervise and train junior chemists, postgraduate students, or technical staff on lipid synthesis and characterisation methods. Disseminate findings through peer-reviewed publications, patent filings, and conference presentations. Requirements : Education and Expertise : Ph.D. in Chemistry, Medicinal Chemistry, Pharmaceutical Sciences, or a related field, with a specialisation in lipid or organic synthesis. Proven track record of designing and synthesising novel lipid molecules, demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications or patents. Strong theoretical and practical grounding in lipid chemistry, including structure-activity relationships relevant to ionisable lipids. Research Skills : Hands-on expertise in the design and synthesis of novel ionisable lipids, including multi-step organic synthesis and purification techniques. Proficiency in analytical characterisation methods, including NMR, LC-MS, and HPLC, to confirm lipid structure, purity, and stability. Experience in formulating LNPs incorporating ionisable, helper, PEG, and cholesterol components, with the ability to tune molar ratios and process parameters. Competence in assessing LNP physicochemical properties, including particle size, polydispersity index, zeta potential, and encapsulation efficiency, using dynamic light scattering and related techniques. Experience in evaluating nucleic acid loading efficiency and LNP stability under varying storage and biological conditions. Familiarity with in vitro assays used to assess LNP delivery efficiency, cytotoxicity, and transfection or gene editing performance. Desirable Skills : Experience with high-throughput lipid screening platforms or combinatorial lipid library synthesis. Familiarity with microfluidic or other advanced LNP manufacturing techniques. Knowledge of structure-function modelling or computational tools to predict lipid behaviour and guide rational design. Experience with biophysical assays assessing endosomal escape efficiency or membrane interaction properties of lipids. Familiarity with regulatory or intellectual property considerations relevant to novel lipid excipients. Prior experience contributing to patent applications for proprietary lipid chemistries. Administrative and Collaborative Skills : Ability to manage a research programme financially and administratively under the guidance of the Principal Investigator. Ability to work independently with excellent problem-solving skills, collaborate within a team, and supervise students. High attention to detail in experimental design and execution with a willingness to adapt to new procedures and undergo further training as necessary. Language and Technical Competence : Excellent communication, command of written and spoken English. Capable of contributing to grant writing and funding applications. Proficient in IT skills for efficient data management and communication within the research programme including but not limited to the data management, analysis, and reporting. What We Offer : The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to and funding availability and project progress. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply : The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until January 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537603 Post-doctoral Fellow in Ionisable Lipid Chemistry for Nucleic Acids Delivery Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537603 Post-doctoral Fellow in Ionisable Lipid Chemistry for Nucleic Acids Delivery Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537604/postdoctoral-fellow-in-hydrogelenabled-peptide-brain-delivery": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in Hydrogel-Enabled Peptide Brain Delivery",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in Hydrogel-Enabled Peptide Brain Delivery The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537604 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in Hydrogel-Enabled Peptide Brain Delivery (Ref.: 537604) We now invite applicants to join the JC STEM Lab of Nanomedicine for Advanced Therapy (PI: Professor Khuloud Al-Jamal) at the Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy. We are a highly collaborative research team working on an advanced, nose-to-brain hydrogel delivery platform for the treatment of neurodegenerative diseases (ND), including Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis (ALS), Frontotemporal Dementia (FTD), Alzheimer's disease (AD), and Parkinson's disease (PD). We are looking to recruit highly motivated postdoctoral fellows and/or research staff to design, synthesise and evaluate novel peptide analogues and biodegradable hydrogels capable of bypassing the blood-brain barrier (BBB) for precise, non-invasive brain-targeted therapy. The aim of our lab is to leverage nanomaterials and biocompatible hydrogel platforms to overcome the limited brain bioavailability, rapid degradation, and systemic side effects that currently restrict peptide-based therapeutics for neurodegenerative disease. Our research spans peptide chemistry, nanomaterial/hydrogel engineering, nose-to-brain (N2B) delivery, and translational in vivo disease modelling, aiming to create real-world impact for patients living with ALS, FTD, AD, and PD. Duties and Responsibilities : The candidate should be competent in peptides and hydrogel syntheses and bioconjugation reactions, along with purification and structural characterisation of synthesised compounds. Proficiency is needed in a range of analytical instrumentation, including HPLC, LC-MS, 1H-NMR, gel permeation chromatography, and surface plasmon resonance. The role requires hands-on experience designing, cross-linking, and characterising polymer-based nanomaterials and hydrogels, including evaluating physicochemical properties. Core biological skills include running ELISA, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, and cell-based binding or activity assays, along with general cell culture technique across different cell lines. The candidate should be capable of conducting animal studies, including dosing, biological sample collection, pharmacokinetic sampling, and behavioural assessment, within an ethically approved framework. The candidate should work closely with collaborators on model development, sample sharing, and data analysis. Prepare study protocols, reports, and contribute to manuscript writing. Supervise and mentor undergraduate and postgraduate students. Disseminate findings through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations. Requirements : Education and Expertise : Ph.D. in Pharmaceutical Sciences, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Bioengineering, Molecular Biology, or a related field. Strong biological skills with a proven track record of high-quality research involving peptide or nanomaterial-based therapeutics. Demonstrated experience in scientific writing and publication. Research Skills : Hands-on expertise in nanomaterials and hydrogel formulation, characterisation, and optimisation. Experience in peptide synthesis and bioconjugation chemistry. Strong background in brain delivery strategies, including nose-to-brain (N2B) delivery and blood-brain barrier (BBB) targeting. Familiarity with neurodegenerative disease biology, particularly neuroinflammation, microglial activation, and neuroprotection mechanisms. Proficiency in cell and molecular biology techniques: ELISA, Western blotting, immunohistochemistry, and cell culture (neuronal and nasal epithelial cell lines). Experience with in vivo rodent models, including pharmacokinetic sampling and behavioural testing. Desirable Skills : Experience with radiolabelling and associated detection techniques such as liquid scintillation counting, autoradiography). Experience with analytical instrumentation and analyses software (e.g., HPLC, LC-MS, NMR, and GPC). Familiarity with Design-Expert or similar formulation optimisation software. Administrative and Collaborative Skills : Ability to manage a research programme financially and administratively under the guidance of the Principal Investigator. Ability to work independently with excellent problem-solving skills, collaborate within a team, and supervise students. High attention to detail in experimental design and execution with a willingness to adapt to new procedures and undergo further training as necessary. Language and Technical Competence : Excellent communication, command of written and spoken English. Capable of contributing to grant writing and funding applications. Proficient in IT skills for efficient data management and communication within the research programme including but not limited to the data management, analysis, and reporting. What We Offer : The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and project progress. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply : The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until January 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537604 Post-doctoral Fellow in Hydrogel-Enabled Peptide Brain Delivery Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537604 Post-doctoral Fellow in Hydrogel-Enabled Peptide Brain Delivery Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537605/postdoctoral-fellow-in-lnpassisted-geneediting-for-neurodegeneration": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in LNP-assisted Gene-Editing for Neurodegeneration",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in LNP-assisted Gene-Editing for Neurodegeneration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537605 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in LNP-assisted Gene-Editing for Neurodegeneration (Ref.: 537605) We now invite applicants to join the JC STEM Lab of Nanomedicine for Advanced Therapy (PI: Professor Khuloud Al-Jamal) at the Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy. We are a highly collaborative research team developing an innovative lipid nanoparticle (LNP)-based CRISPR-Cas9 gene editing platform for the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) and frontotemporal dementia (FTD). We are looking for a highly motivated postdoctoral fellow to evaluate single and dual gene knockout strategies targeting two key modifiers of disease pathology, as a novel non-viral therapeutic approach for neurodegenerative diseases. The aim of our lab is to leverage lipid nanoparticle-mediated gene editing to overcome the limitations of current ALS therapies, spanning gene editing technology, nanoparticle-based delivery, in vivo disease modelling, and computational systems analysis to translate a precise, broadly applicable gene therapy strategy toward clinical relevance. Duties and Responsibilities : Design and evaluate CRISPR-Cas9-based gene editing strategies for single and dual gene knockout in disease-relevant models. Formulate, characterise and optimise lipid nanoparticles for the encapsulation and delivery of gene editing payloads. Conduct in vivo animal studies, including administration of LNP-based therapeutics, sample collection, and disease progression monitoring. Perform behavioural studies and phenotypic assessments in disease mouse models to evaluate therapeutic efficacy. Apply immunohistochemistry to determine tissue- and cell-type-specific targeting and delivery precision. Conduct western blot and molecular analyses to quantify target protein knockout and pathological markers. Support transcriptomic studies and contribute to computational modelling of molecular interplay. Collaborate internationally, prepare reports and protocols, and contribute to grant and manuscript writing. Supervise students and disseminate findings through publications and conference presentations. Collaborate with other team member to ensure effective synergy between various projects. Requirements : Education and Expertise : A Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, Pharmacology, Neuroscience, Bioengineering, or a related field is required. Strong biological skills and a proven research track record in gene editing or nanoparticle-based therapeutics. Demonstrated experience in scientific writing and publication. Research Skills : Hands-on expertise in gene editing, particularly CRISPR-Cas systems, including guide RNA design and editing validation. Experience in LNP formulation, characterisation, and nucleic acid payload encapsulation is essential. Familiarity with neurodegenerative disease biology, particularly neuroinflammation, microglial activation, and neuroprotection mechanisms. Proficiency in in vivo experiments including behavioural studies is a plus. Expertise in cellular and molecular biology techniques such as western blotting, immunohistochemistry, and cell culture (mainly motor neurons). Administrative and Collaborative Skills : Ability to manage a research programme financially and administratively under the guidance of the Principal Investigator. Ability to work independently with excellent problem-solving skills, collaborate within a team, and supervise students. High attention to detail in experimental design and execution with a willingness to adapt to new procedures and undergo further training as necessary. Language and Technical Competence : Excellent communication, command of written and spoken English. Capable of contributing to grant writing and funding applications. Proficient in IT skills for efficient data management and communication within the research programme including but not limited to the data management, analysis, and reporting. What We Offer : The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and project progress. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply : The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until January 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537605 Post-doctoral Fellow in LNP-assisted Gene-Editing for Neurodegeneration Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537605 Post-doctoral Fellow in LNP-assisted Gene-Editing for Neurodegeneration Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Jan 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537618/parttime-student-research-assistant-several-posts": {
      "title": "Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537618 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Hourly-paid Department: Department of Sociology (30400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Department of Sociology (Ref.:537618) (to commence in late December 2026 or January 2027 and end on 29 June 2027) Applicants should be current HKU undergraduate students in psychology, early childhood education, or other related social science and education disciplines, preferably in their third or final year of study. They must be highly proficient in written and spoken Chinese (with native-level proficiency in Cantonese required) and possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Applicants should have a strong sense of responsibility, be detailed-minded, dedicated, patient, punctual and be able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment. Experience in working with preschool children and/or exposure to child or psychological assessments would be an advantage. The appointees will be responsible for conducting child assessments under the supervision of the research team and educational psychologists for a large-scale project on early childhood development in Hong Kong. The posts would provide an excellent opportunity for those interested in educational psychology and child assessments, and who would like to gain experience working with children in school-based settings and participate in a large-scale child development research project. Applicants considering further academic/professional pursuits in educational psychology or related fields are particularly welcome. Enquiries about the posts should be sent to the Project Team at hkchild@hku.hk . The applicants should be able to commit to working one to two full weekdays per week during the employment period. The estimated working hours will be approximately 8 - 15 hours per week, and the hourly pay rates will follow the guidelines of the University. Applicants will be required to participate in and successfully pass a mandatory 3-day training program before employment. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 20 November, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 12, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537618 Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) Department of Sociology (30400) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537618 Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) Department of Sociology (30400) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537562/senior-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-i": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537562 Work type: Full-time Department: Technology Transfer Office (99110) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the Technology Transfer Office (Ref.: 537562) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Key Responsibilities: Project Administration & Stakeholder Coordination Support the Business Development (BD) team by independently following up with Principal Investigators (PIs). Serve as a reliable primary point of contact for faculty members, assisting them with administrative follow-ups and tracking project deliverables in collaboration with industry partners. Provide meticulous administrative and operational assistance for the RAISe+ Scheme and contract research projects, ensuring project records are kept up to date and key milestones are strictly monitored against timelines. Business Development & Strategic Support Conduct preliminary market research, gather data, and assist in drafting basic business reports to support the team’s strategic outreach and commercialization efforts. Take ownership of the Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system, ensuring accuracy in tracking the business development pipeline. Operations & Process Optimization Assist the team in drafting and updating Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to document and standardize BD workflows. Execute administrative and operational tasks with a high degree of accuracy and quality control, taking ownership to ensure processes are completed accurately and thoroughly from start to finish. Perform any other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director of the Technology Transfer Office or his/her delegates. Requirements: Qualifications & Industry Experience A Bachelor’s degree or above, with at least 2-3 years’ relevant work experience. Proven versatility in general office administration and project management. Experience in tertiary education institutions or research-intensive environments, specifically in business development, project management, innovation, or technology transfer, is highly preferred. Knowledge of funding schemes (e.g., RAISe+), intellectual property management, or commercialization is an advantage. Technical Skills Hands-on experience with CRM systems (maintenance and data entry) and familiarity with research management systems (e.g., RIMS) is a distinct advantage. Communication & Language Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Excellent interpersonal and communication skills to serve as a reliable liaison among professors, industry partners, and internal stakeholders. Core Competencies: Exceptionally detail-oriented with a strong sense of ownership; capable of consistently delivering highly accurate work independently. Proactive and results-driven, with the ability to document workflows (SOPs) and manage multiple administrative tasks simultaneously in a dynamic environment. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start on October 23, 2026 , and continue until November 8, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Information about the Office can be obtained at https://rise.hku.hk/en . Advertised: Oct 10, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537562 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) Technology Transfer Office (99110) Nov 8, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537562 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) Technology Transfer Office (99110) Nov 8, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537600/senior-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-i": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537600 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537600) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess either (a) 5 passes in HKCEE or min. Level 2 in 5 subjects in HKDSEE, with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience, preferably in tertiary institutions, OR (b) a recognised degree or diploma. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, IT proficiency including MS Office and Chinese Word processing, and excellent organizational and interpersonal skills. They should be a good team player, reliable, self-motivated, attentive to details, and able to work independently and multi-task efficiently. Preference will be given to those with a high level of computer/IT literacy. The appointee will mainly provide day-to-day clerical support to the HKU Health System, the umbrella executive arm overseeing and supporting the LKS Faculty of Medicine's clinical enterprises. Major job duties include: Support HKU Health System improvement projects. Provide clerical support to the Clinical Governance oversight program. Maintain the online library of policies and Standard Operating Procedures. Coordinate the online Clinical Governance reporting system. Perform basic data analysis and provide summary reports. Schedule and coordinate meetings. Provide information desk services on a rotational basis, supporting patients and coordinating medical appointments with HKUMed clinical faculty members. Perform other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 23, 2026 and continue until November 8, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 10, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537600 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Nov 8, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537600 Senior Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Nov 8, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537558/technical-manager": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Technical Manager The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537558 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Technical Manager in the Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537558) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis or one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree in Optometry and be a registered Optometrist (Part I) with The Optometrists Board of Hong Kong SAR under the Supplementary Medical Professions Ordinance, with minimum 10 years’ relevant work experience.  Those with relevant experience in research, large-scale community projects, mentoring and managerial responsibilities would have advantages.  They should have strong sense of responsibility, good interpersonal, organizational and communication skills, with the ability to multi-task and work independently as well as collaboratively as a team. The appointee will be involved in clinical services, research and large-scale community-based screening projects in various districts and in hospitals/clinics.  He/She will manage the day-to-day operations of projects from administration to manpower management; perform ophthalmic examinations and investigations; assist with the procurement and daily maintenance of ophthalmic equipment and devices; prepare reports through data collection and analysis; and supervise junior professionals.  Occasional overtime work may be required. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 22, 2026 and continue until November 4, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 4, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537558 Technical Manager Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Nov 4, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537558 Technical Manager Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Nov 4, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
