    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537585/fulltimeparttime-research-assistant-iii-several-posts": {
      "title": "Full-time/Part-time Research Assistant I/II (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Full-time/Part-time Research Assistant I/II (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537585 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Full-time/Part-time Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537585) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) The appointees will participate in a large-scale multidisciplinary research and community youth mental health project. It is Hong Kong’s first territory-wide initiative to build a youth-specific and youth-friendly mental health platform that provides timely preventive intervention to youth with distress and risk for mental health deterioration. The project will transform current youth services and provide a framework for future developments in youth mental health and youth-focused services both locally and internationally. Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in psychology, social science, or any healthcare-related disciplines. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (fluency in Cantonese is required), the ability to work independently and in collaboration with a multidisciplinary team, and the ability to collaborate with external parties including academics and social service groups. Relevant experience in conducting and managing community research and clinical studies is preferred. The appointee will support the evaluation component of one of the team’s projects.  He/She will perform data collection, analysis and prepare reports, presentations and academic papers; and perform other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will on 26 October 2026 and continue until 12 December 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 12, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537585 Full-time/Part-time Research Assistant I/II (several posts) Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Dec 12, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537585 Full-time/Part-time Research Assistant I/II (several posts) Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Dec 12, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537586/fractional-senior-clinical-practitioner-in-periodontology": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Fractional Senior Clinical Practitioner in Periodontology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537586 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Fractional Senior Clinical Practitioner in Periodontology of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537586), to commence as soon as possible on a fixed-term (50% fractional) basis for two years, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants must possess a dental or medical (Bachelor’s) degree or equivalent and a clinical specialist status or equivalent in Periodontology.  Their clinical expertise should enjoy regional acclaim as evidenced by extensive clinical or teaching experience, regional clinical publications/presentations, and regional recognition of clinical excellence in a clinical specialty. Applicants should also have proven clinical competence in diagnosis and comprehensive treatment planning, and delivery of high-quality periodontal and dental implant treatment in both primary care settings (general dental practice) and referral practice (specialist practice).  They should also be a good team player who is enthusiastic and motivated to make a positive impact on healthcare for Hong Kong citizens through contributions to excellent undergraduate education and beyond, and demonstrate a strong interest in teaching and learning. The appointee will deliver the Periodontology curriculum to undergraduate and postgraduate students, supervise clinical teaching, provide clinical services, and contribute to administrative duties in the Faculty.  Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Professor W.K. Leung, Chief, Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry, at ewkleung@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The successful candidate is required to obtain a valid registration with the Dental Council of Hong Kong.  (Note: Applicants who do not hold a local dental license must fulfil the essential requirements under the laws of a jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, China, to be eligible for Limited Registration.  For details, please refer to the Dental Council of Hong Kong’s website at https://www.dchk.org.hk/en/registration/part_III.html .)  In addition, candidates who do not possess the right of abode or the right to land in Hong Kong are required to obtain a valid visa before taking up employment.  For details of visa applications, please refer to the Immigration Department’s website at https://www.immd.gov.hk/eng/services/index.html . The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 22, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537586 Fractional Senior Clinical Practitioner in Periodontology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 22, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537586 Fractional Senior Clinical Practitioner in Periodontology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 22, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
