    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537596/administrative-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Administrative Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537596 Work type: Full-time Department: HKU Northern Metropolis Office (60120) Categories: Professional & Management, Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Administrative Assistant I/II in the HKU Northern Metropolis Office (Ref.: 537596) About the HKU Northern Metropolis Office With a view to consolidating our efforts in participating in the Northern Metropolis University Town initiative promulgated by the Government, The University of Hong Kong (HKU) has recently established the Northern Metropolis Office (NMO) to provide focused leadership and coordinated support for the University’s strategic developments in the Northern Metropolis University Towns (NMUTs). The NMO is responsible for the planning, development and future operation of these initiatives through engagement with stakeholders within and outside of the University. The Role Reporting to the Executive Director (Academic), the appointee will: support the academic planning associated with the NMUT development ; coordinate projects and initiatives in collaboration with academic and administrative units; provide secretariat support to Committees and Task Forces; conduct research as well as analyse reports and data to inform academic planning and policy development; draft submissions, progress reports, and discussion documents; liaise with various stakeholders to facilitate academic planning initiatives in the NMUTs; manage project timelines and coordinate progress; and undertake other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should have a good university degree with at least 10 years’ solid administrative experience, preferably in higher education, as well as an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), and strong IT and quantitative skills. They should have strong organizational and problem-solving skills and proven ability in data analysis for planning purposes. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, the ability to engage diverse stakeholders, demonstrated capacity to coordinate complex projects and work independently under pressure are required. Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant II. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a full-time fixed-term contract for two years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary for Administrative Assistant I, or at 10% of basic salary for Administrative Assistant II. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 26, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and a written test. Advertised: Oct 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537596 Administrative Assistant I/II HKU Northern Metropolis Office (60120) Oct 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537596 Administrative Assistant I/II HKU Northern Metropolis Office (60120) Oct 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537598/executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537598 Work type: Full-time Department: HKU Northern Metropolis Office (60120) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the HKU Northern Metropolis Office (Ref.: 537598) About the HKU Northern Metropolis Office With a view to consolidating our efforts in participating in the Northern Metropolis University Town initiative promulgated by the Government, The University of Hong Kong (HKU) has recently established the Northern Metropolis Office (NMO) to provide focused leadership and coordinated support for the University’s strategic developments in the Northern Metropolis University Towns (NMUTs). The NMO is responsible for the planning, development and future operation of these initiatives through engagement with stakeholders within and outside of the University. The Role Reporting to the Executive Director (Academic), the appointee will: maintain the administrative and operational instruments of academic planning; provide logistic support for committee and task force meetings, and/or for projects/initiatives relating to the NMUT development; draft submissions, progress reports and discussion documents; collect, compile and prepare data to facilitate academic planning initiatives in the  NMUTs; liaise with academic and administrative units to facilitate communication, consultation, and project implementation; coordinate follow-up actions to ensure timely implementation of initiatives; and undertake office administration and other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should have a good university degree with at least 5 years’ solid administrative experience, preferably in higher education; as well as an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), and sound IT and quantitative skills. They should demonstrate strong organizational, problem-solving, communication and interpersonal skills. The successful candidate should be a good team player with keen attention to details, able to multitask, meet tight deadlines and perform effectively under pressure. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for two years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 26, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and a written test. Advertised: Oct 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537598 Executive Officer HKU Northern Metropolis Office (60120) Oct 26, 202