    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537555/fulltimeparttime-receptionist-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii-in-the-institute-for-advanced-dentistry-multispecialty-clinic-iadmsc-several-posts": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Full-time 1 Hourly-paid 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Full-time/Part-time Receptionist (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Institute for Advanced Dentistry Multi-Specialty Clinic (IAD-MSC) (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537555 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Full-time, Hourly-paid Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Full-time/Part-time Receptionist (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Institute for Advanced Dentistry Multi-Specialty Clinic (IAD-MSC) of the Faculty of Dentistry (several posts) (Ref.: 537555) We are currently looking for enthusiastic and customer-oriented individuals to join the IAD-MSC of the Faculty of Dentistry as Receptionists (at the rank of Clerk II). The Role The appointees will be responsible for: Assisting with patient registration and appointment scheduling; Handling invoicing and payment collection; Answering enquiries via telephone, email, and WhatsApp; Providing administrative support to resident doctors (MDS students); Coordinating with internal and external parties; Maintaining accurate patient records and clinic documentation; and Performing other duties as assigned. On-the-job training will be provided. Qualifications and Qualities A Higher Diploma or above in any disciplines; At least 1 year of relevant work experience; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (proficiency in Putonghua would be an advantage); Good interpersonal and communication skills; Basic proficiency in Microsoft Office applications; A strong customer service mindset with good telephone etiquette; A responsible, proactive, and self-motivated attitude; Ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks efficiently in a fast-paced clinical environment; and Strong organizational skills and attention to details. Fresh graduates with strong customer service skills may also be considered. What We Offer The appointments will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, or temporary part-time contract for up to 1 year, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability.  For full-time appointments, a 5-day work week (with Saturday/ Sunday/ Public Holidays off) and daytime shift duties according to the operational needs of the clinic will be adopted.  For part-time appointments, a flexible working schedule will be arranged based on clinic service demands. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered.  The appointments on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits, if applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 7, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 8, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 7, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537555 Full-time/Part-time Receptionist (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Institute for Advanced Dentistry Multi-Specialty Clinic (IAD-MSC) (several posts) Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Nov 7, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537555 Full-time/Part-time Receptionist (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Institute for Advanced Dentistry Multi-Specialty Clinic (IAD-MSC) (several posts) Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Nov 7, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
