    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537582/senior-technical-officertechnical-officer-in-the-school-of-biomedical-sciences": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer in the School of Biomedical Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537582 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537582) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree, preferably a postgraduate degree in Pathology and/or Physiology. They should have at least 2 years’ solid work experience in developmental biology or a related laboratory science discipline. They should also be highly motivated and able to work independently and as part of a team in a multidisciplinary laboratory environment. Experience with maintaining hematopoietic cultures, managing multiple Drosophila colonies, and advanced imaging techniques will be an asset. Those with less experience will be considered for the post of Technical Officer. The appointee will play a crucial role in supporting student practical classes, demonstrations, laboratory activities, maintaining equipment and facilities, and collaborating with researchers to ensure smooth scientific operations.  His/her responsibilities include, but are not limited to: conducting laboratory experiments and providing technical support to researchers and staff, maintain and calibrate laboratory equipment, troubleshoot technical issues, and ensure their proper functioning, prepare and analyse samples, perform quality control tests, and accurately record experimental data, assisting in the development and implementation of laboratory protocols and standard operating procedures, collaborate with researchers to optimize experimental procedures and provide technical guidance, ensure compliance with safety regulations, maintain a clean and organized laboratory environment. He or she will also need to liaise with commercial parties for purchases, and external contractors and the Estate Office to conduct infrastructure maintenance works. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 20, 2026 and continue until December 6, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 7, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 6, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537490/tenuretrack-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537490 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) (Ref.: 537490) The University of Hong Kong has a highly ranked engineering school and active electrical and computer engineering programmes. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering offers B.Eng., M.Sc., M.Phil. and Ph.D. programmes. Information about the Department can be obtained at http://www.ece.hku.hk The Position We now invite applications for appointment as Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the area of Biomedical Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) . The successful candidate will have a chance to work with an interdisciplinary team to advance ultra-low-field MRI technologies and facilitate their translation into cutting-edge healthcare applications. Requirements We seek a candidate with advanced training in the physical, engineering, and computational foundations of MRI, with a strong focus on deep tech and impact. Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Physics, or a related discipline, alongside a strong track record of high-impact publications. Candidates must demonstrate deep technical expertise in one of the following core domains: (1) MRI Physics & Hardware Design: Experience in magnet configurations, RF/gradient coil engineering, pulse sequence programming, and shielding-free system architectures. (2) Computational Imaging & AI: Deep learning and data-driven image formation to tackle the grand SNR and resolution challenges in ultra-low-field MRI. (3) Translational Research: Developing paradigm-shifting applications for ultra-low-field MRI, such as point-of-care imaging and population health monitoring. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be expected to: Conduct independent research; Develop and secure competitive external research funding; Supervise postgraduate students; Teach undergraduate and postgraduate courses; Contribute to curriculum development and academic administration; Engage in interdisciplinary collaborations. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 3 years initially, to commence as soon as possible thereafter, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract, subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for these positions. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload the following documents: (i) a cover letter, (ii) an up-to-date C.V. (including a full list of publications), (iii) a teaching statement (maximum 2 pages), (iv) a research statement (maximum 2 pages) outlining current and future research plans, and (v) the contact information of at least three referees. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 7, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537490 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537490 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537549/executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537549 Work type: Full-time Department: Joint University Programmes Admissions System Office (99806) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Joint University Programmes Admissions System (JUPAS) Office (Ref: 537549) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year full-time temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) About the Office The JUPAS Office administers the centralised application system for admission to full-time undergraduate programmes offered by participating-institutions in Hong Kong. We are committed to providing accurate, timely, and increasingly user-focused services to eligible applicants, and other key stakeholders, ensuring fairness, transparency, and operational excellence throughout the admissions process. Information about the Office is available at https://www.jupas.edu.hk . About the Role The JUPAS Office is seeking a customer-focused, proactive and detail-oriented individual with an interest in service improvement and user experience.  The appointee will support the delivery of high-quality enquiry services to applicants, parents, schools and the public through various communication channels.  Beyond handling enquiries, the role will contribute to service improvement initiatives by identifying trends, analysing recurring issues and supporting the enhancement of self-service resources and digital communication platforms.  This position supports the enhancement of applicant services through enquiry analysis, service improvements and the development of self-service resources. Major Duties Handle enquiries received through telephone, email, enquiry forms, chatbot and other communication channels. Provide accurate, professional and timely information relating to JUPAS applications, procedures and policies. Investigate and follow up enquiry cases requiring coordination with internal teams and external stakeholders. Monitor enquiry trends, recurring questions and service issues, and recommend improvements to communication materials, FAQs and user journeys. Maintain and update enquiry guides, standard responses, FAQs and chatbot knowledge resources. Categorise and analyse enquiry data, hotline records and feedback to support service enhancement initiatives. Assist in preparing reports, statistics and management information relating to enquiry services and customer experience. Contribute to applicant-facing communications, self-service resources and user experience improvement projects. Support daily website operations, including uploading and updating website content, announcements, and resources via the Content Management System (CMS). Perform administrative and operational duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A recognised bachelor's degree; At least two years of relevant experience in customer service, admissions, education administration, enquiry handling, contact centre operations or other stakeholder-facing functions; Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English and Chinese; Good command of Putonghua would be an advantage; Strong interpersonal and problem-solving skills; A customer-centric mindset and commitment to service excellence; Good analytical ability and confidence working with enquiry statistics and operational data; Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and familiarity with AI-enabled productivity tools will be an advantage; Good numerical sense, attention to detail and IT proficiency; Experience in enquiry management systems, customer services, hotline operations or data reporting would be an advantage. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, along with annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for this position.  Applicants should apply online and upload a covering letter and an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.  Information about the Office is available at https://www.jupas.edu.hk . Advertised: Oct 7, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537549 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Joint University Programmes Admissions System Office (99806) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537549 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Joint University Programmes Admissions System Office (99806) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537568/senior-executive-assistantexecutive-assistant-emba-admissions-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, EMBA Admissions (at the rank of Clerk I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, EMBA Admissions (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537568 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, EMBA Admissions (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537568) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should possess a good bachelor’s degree with at least 2 years of work experience, preferably in student admissions, relationship management, human resources, or related fields. They should have outstanding organisational and communication skills, an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), as well as proficiency in using MS Office applications, particularly Excel and PowerPoint. They should also be mature, meticulous and self-motivated, with a strong sense of responsibility and the ability to handle multiple tasks, work independently and be a good team player. Candidates with strong data management and back-office support skills, client relationship management experience, or familiarity with social media platforms (including proficiency in using WeChat for promotion) would be highly preferred. Those with less experience will be considered for the post of Clerk II. The appointee will assist in various admissions-related areas of the Faculty’s EMBA programme, such as applicant follow-up, database management, academic credential verification, employment background checks, event support, and the processing of invoices and purchase orders. He/She may also perform other duties as assigned. The appointee will work at the Faculty’s Cyberport campus. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 27, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 7, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 27, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537568 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, EMBA Admissions (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 27, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537568 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, EMBA Admissions (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 27, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
