    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537517/manager-assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-administrative-assistant-ii-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Manager/ Assistant Manager (at the rank of Administrative Assistant II /Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Manager/ Assistant Manager (at the rank of Administrative Assistant II /Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537517 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Manager/Assistant Manager (at the rank of Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer) in the Department of Mechanical Engineering (Ref.: 537517) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree and have at least 8 years of relevant work experience, including a minimum of 5 years in a supervisory or management role, preferably within the tertiary education sector. Prior experience in programme administration is highly desirable. Candidates should demonstrate an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua. They should also possess strong organisational, interpersonal, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with keen attention to detail. The successful candidate should have a strong sense of responsibility, demonstrated maturity and professionalism, and the ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. The ability to manage multiple tasks under tight deadlines is essential. Strong leadership capabilities, together with a proactive and self-motivated approach to work, are also expected. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Assistant Manager. The appointee will take a leading operational role in managing the full spectrum of undergraduate programme administration in the Department. Key responsibilities include: Managing day-to-day undergraduate academic programme operations and student affairs; Executing the operational plan, course logistics, and curriculum transitions for the revamped undergraduate programme and academic specializations; Assisting in liaison with external professional bodies, including the HKIE for professional accreditation and quality assurance; Facilitating administrative and logistical workflows between academic leads, teaching staff, and technical teams to support undergraduate laboratory activities and hands-on experiential learning facilities; Planning, organizing, and executing student enrichment initiatives, co-curricular activities, and overseas learning opportunities; Providing executive secretarial and administrative support to departmental teaching committees, working groups, and curriculum task forces; Acting as the primary administrative bridge between internal and external stakeholders, including Faculty officers, Professoriate Leads, teaching staff, and external partner organizations; and Performing any other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 6, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs lik