    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537563/senior-it-managerit-managerit-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior IT Manager/IT Manager/IT Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537563 Work type: Full-time Department: Registry (60300) Categories: Professional & Management, Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong The Registry is seeking a highly skilled Senior IT Manager / IT Manager / IT Officer (several posts) (Ref.: 537563) to join our office. The Roles The appointees will design, implement and support AI-enabled and automation solutions for academic, administrative and student-related services. They will work closely with offices, faculties and departments to deliver secure, scalable and user-oriented solutions. The appointees will be responsible for: Developing and supporting Generative AI, Agentic AI and workflow automation projects; Designing AI chatbots and virtual assistants for enquiries, FAQ handling, response generation, case routing and escalation; Implementing AI solutions for document verification, OCR, intelligent document processing, data extraction and document standardisation; Building AI-powered knowledge bases, repositories and search solutions using retrieval-augmented generation, semantic search and related technologies; Supporting automation of application review, approval workflows, document routing, procurement processes, meeting preparation and case management; Developing data analytics, dashboards and reports to support planning, audit, compliance and decision-making; Integrating AI and automation solutions with University systems, Microsoft 365, Office applications, Teams, APIs and other enterprise platforms using appropriate authentication, authorization and delegated access mechanisms; Using low-code, automation and custom development approaches, where appropriate, to prototype, orchestrate, deploy and support production-ready business workflows, while translating practical user needs into well-governed, maintainable and integrated solutions; Ensuring AI quality assurance, data privacy, cybersecurity, access control and responsible AI compliance; and Preparing documentation, user guides, training materials and management reports. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A Bachelor’s degree or professional qualification in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, Information Systems, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline; For Senior IT Manager, at least 5 to 8 years’ relevant specialist experience at supervisory level in IT, AI, automation, digital transformation or a related sector; Candidates with less experience may be considered as IT Manager or IT Officer; Solid knowledge of Generative AI, Large Language Models, Agentic AI, prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation, vector databases, AI chatbots and workflow automation; Experience in applying AI, automation, data analytics, low-code platforms, Microsoft 365 integration, APIs, secure access delegation, DevOps practices or enterprise workflow solutions in practical business settings; Good understanding of AI governance, cybersecurity, data privacy and responsible AI practices; Strong vendor management, analytical and problem-solving skills, with solid experience in consolidating user needs, managing stakeholder expectations, resolving requirement gaps and translating institutional priorities into practical technical solutions; Meticulous attention to detail while maintaining an overview of the broader context; Demonstrated leadership, strong interpersonal and communication skills; and Excellent command of written and spoken English. Proficiency in Chinese would be an advantage. Preference will be given to applicants with relevant certifications or practical training in areas such as AI, cloud platforms, cybersecurity, data analytics, Microsoft Azure AI, AWS AI/ML, Google Cloud AI, Power Platform, ITIL or equivalent qualifications. Project management-related certifications such as PRINCE2 or PMP would be an additional advantage but are not essential. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits   The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% or 10% of basic salary based on the level of appointment. Appointment as Senior IT Manager or IT Manager or IT Officer will depend on qualifications, experience and level of responsibility. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site at https://jobs.hku.hk and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 6, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537563 Senior IT Manager/IT Manager/IT Officer Registry (60300) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537563 Senior IT Manager/IT Manager/IT Officer Registry (60300) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537571/senior-executive-assistant-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant / Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Senior Executive Assistant / Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537571 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.: 537571） The Role The appointee(s) will be responsible for providing administrative support to our new taught postgraduate programmes, including assisting with the preparation of marketing materials and publicity, managing student admissions, coordinating curriculum and course selection, collecting and compiling data, and handling inquiries and other student-related matters. Additionally, he/she will assist with departmental events, new initiatives, and perform any other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics, OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience; OR a Bachelor’s degree with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Self-motivated, attentive to details, and able to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently; Strong sense of responsibility, positive attitude, and ability to work independently under pressure to meet tight deadlines; Effective communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills; Proficiency in IT skills, especially in MS Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Knowledge of management of database and website an advantage; Preference will be given to those with work experience in tertiary education, especially experience in handling taught postgraduate student matters. Those with less experience and/or lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Executive Assistant. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a fixed-term full-time basis for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to funding ability and satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 6, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 6, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 6, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537571 Senior Executive Assistant / Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 6, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537571 Senior Executive Assistant / Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Nov 6, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
