    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537572/administrative-assistant-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-programme-manager": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of Senior Programme Manager)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of Senior Programme Manager) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537572 Work type: Full-time Department: Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (60380) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of Senior Programme Manager) in the Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (Ref: 537572) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, and with the possibility of renewal) The Academic Liaison Office, which includes International Affairs Office, Mainland Affairs Office and HKU Summer Institute, is dedicated to promoting academic exchanges and fostering collaboration with Mainland and overseas institutions. Applicants should have a good University degree and at least 6 years’ work experience, of which at least 3 years should be at supervisory or management level.  They should have excellent communication skills, including a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); outstanding leadership, interpersonal and organisational skills; a strong sense of responsibility; and the ability to work under pressure.  Commitment to quality and accountability, and readiness for new challenges are essential.  Solid experience in programme development and management or in fostering partnerships in the higher education sector is an advantage. The appointee will oversee the design, planning and implementation of programmes of HKU Summer 