    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537579/senior-research-assistant-holding-the-functional-title-of-project-officer": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Project Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Project Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537579 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Chemistry (25200) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Project Officer for AI-assisted Research Publicity (at the Rank of Senior Research Assistant) in the Department of Chemistry (Ref.:537579) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a B.Sc. degree in Chemistry with at least 3 years of relevant work experience, or an M.Sc. degree in Chemistry with at least 1 year of relevant work experience.  They should have a solid scientific background and sufficient knowledge to understand and communicate chemistry-related research and teaching materials effectively.  They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, strong communication and organizational skills, and the ability to work independently and meet deadlines. Applicants should be proficient in using generative AI tools and AI-assisted workflows, including coding agents such as OpenAI Codex or equivalent tools, to improve presentations, troubleshoot webpages, produce videos and develop publicity materials.  Experience in PowerPoint design, video editing, website maintenance and scientific communication is required.  They should also be able to verify AI-generated content and properly handle scientific accuracy, confidentiality, copyright and data-protection issues. The appointee will use AI and other digital tools to support the research, teaching and publicity activities for the group of Prof. Chi-Ming Che.  Duties include editing and improving research and teaching PowerPoint presentations; maintaining and troubleshooting webpages; producing promotional and explanatory videos; and preparing bilingual publicity materials for research achievements, conferences, seminars, visits and other academic activities. Applicants with an outstanding record and relevant experience in AI-assisted database and e-notebook management would be an advantage and may be considered for appointment at a higher rank.  The appointee may also be required to perform other duties as assigned. Interested applicants may contact Dr. Lihui Zhu at zhulihui@hku.hk with a CV and a brief description of their background and skills. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until March 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 6, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537579 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Project Officer) Department of Chemistry (25200) Mar 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537579 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Project Officer) Department of Chemistry (25200) Mar 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537528/parttime-fulltime-pharmacist": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Part-time / Full-time Pharmacist The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537528 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Full-time Department: Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (21300) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Part-time/ Full-time Pharmacist in the Department of Pharmacology and Pharmacy (Ref.: 537528), to commence on a six-month temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Pharmacy or a healthcare-related post-graduate degree, and be a registered pharmacist in Hong Kong, with at least 5 years’ work experience in pharmacy practice. Relevant experience in pharmacy teaching or research would be an advantage.  Applicants with less than 5 years of experience, but with solid experience in pharmacy, may also be considered. The appointee is expected to contribute to community pharmacy service development, capacity building, as well as to participate in teaching or research initiatives. He/She is expected to possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits, if applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 5, 2026 (H