    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537537/parttime-research-nurse": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Part-Time Research Nurse The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537537 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Part-Time Research Nurse in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 537537) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies.  HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession. HKU-CTC’s Phase 1 Clinical Trials Unit (Phase 1 Unit) is a professional clinical trials facility located at the Queen Mary Hospital and dedicated to conducting phase 1 and early phase clinical trials.  We are seeking a high calibre talent who have the passion in promoting healthcare advancement through practising clinical research to join our Phase 1 Unit as a Part-Time Research Nurse. Main Responsibilities: Be responsible for clinical trial coordination and operations; Recruit trial volunteers; Execute study procedures, data collection and documents management, medical emergency management, facilities management and quality management; Communicate with research teams and internal/external collaborators; and Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Nursing; Registered with the Nursing Council of Hong Kong; A minimum of 1 year’s nursing experience is preferred; Good interpersonal, communication, coordination and problem-solving skills, and commitment to quality and compliance; Detail-minded, self-motivated, and able to multitask; and Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Both Cantonese & Mandarin); Candidates with the following qualifications will have an advantage: Basic Life Support (BLS) and/or Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support (ACLS) certification, and a venipuncture certificate; Experience in clinical trial operations and knowledge of Good Clinical Practice (GCP); Experience in using electronic devices (e.g., tablets and computers) for efficient and accurate clinical data capture. The appointment will be made on a part-time temporary basis on a six-month contract, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University's career site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 17, 2026 and continue until November 2, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 3, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 2, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537537 Part-Time Research Nurse Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 2, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537537 Part-Time Research Nurse Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 2, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
