    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537557/exercise-and-wellness-trainer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Exercise and Wellness Trainer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537557 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre for Sports and Exercise (46800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Exercise and Wellness Trainer (at the rank of Senior Technical Assistant) in the Centre for Sports and Exercise (Ref.:  537557) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should possess a recognized degree, preferably in Sports Science, Exercise Science or equivalent, with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience in exercise prescription and testing.  They should have an excellent command of both spoken and written English and Chinese.  They should also demonstrate good interpersonal, organizational and communication skills; proficiency in IT; the ability to interact positively and professionally with users; and the capability to work independently, as well as collaboratively within a team.  Possession of a valid certifications and qualifications in fitness training (e.g NSCA Certified Strength & Conditioning Specialist, ASCA Strength & Conditioning Coach (Level 2), ACSM Certified Clinical Exercise Physiologist) will be considered an advantage. The appointee will provide health and fitness services for programs and projects conducted at the Active Health Clinic; deliver evidence-based, quality training advice; develop tailored fitness programs for diverse populations; conduct health and fitness assessments in both on-site and clinical settings; assist in fitness and wellness projects; prepare presentations, reports and educational materials; and undertake other duties as assigned.  Working on shift duties will be required. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536945) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start on October 17, 2026 and continue until November 2, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 3, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 2, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537557 Exercise and Wellness Trainer Centre for Sports and Exercise (46800) Nov 2, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537557 Exercise and Wellness Trainer Centre for Sports and Exercise (46800) Nov 2, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
