    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537554/research-assistant-iii-in-the-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537554 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537554) (to commence as soon as possible for 12 months, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should preferably possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in nursing, psychology, public health, social sciences, statistics, data science, or other healthcare- or research-related disciplines. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and/or Putonghua), as well as good interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. They should be responsible, detail-oriented, and able to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research team. Relevant experience in maternal and child health, sleep research, longitudinal or cohort studies, participant recruitment and follow-up, behavioral or video-based research, wearable or digital health technologies, and/or quantitative data analysis would be an advantage. Proficiency in statistical software or programming languages such as R, Python, SPSS, or Stata would also be desirable. Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for the post of Research Assistant II. The appointee will work under the supervision of Dr. Ying Dai on research projects in maternal and child sleep health supported by funding schemes including the National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC), the Research Grants Council General Research Fund (GRF), and other local and institutional funding schemes. Duties include participant recruitment and follow-up, data and sample collection, data management and analysis, behavioral/video coding, literature review, preparation of reports and manuscripts, coordination with research partners, and other research-related tasks as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31 , 202 6 , or until the post is filled, whichever is the earlier Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537554 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537554 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537529/executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537529 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537529) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years’ administrative experience, preferably in a tertiary institution, or a healthcare related field. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; strong communication, interpersonal, organizational and problem-solving skills; the ability to work independently and under pressure to meet tight deadlines; as well as an appropriate level of IT skills. Knowledge of design software would be an advantage. Applicants should also be self-motivated with a strong sense of responsibility, a good team player, capable of multitasking, and attentive to detail. The appointee will be responsible for the day-to-day operations and management, including but not limited to human resources, finance, research administration, managing social media platforms and marketing materials. They may also be assigned other duties as necessary. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from 9 October 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537177/professor-in-the-school-of-future-media": {
      "title": "Professor in the School of Future Media",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Professor in the School of Future Media Ref.: 537177 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Future Media (31200) Categories: Professoriate Staff Applications and nominations are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Professor in the School of Future Media (Ref.: 537177), to commence in Summer 2027 or from as soon as possible thereafter. School of Future Media The School of Future Media (SFM) at The University of Hong Kong (HKU) is a newly established interdisciplinary school dedicated to advancing education, research and creative practice at the intersection of journalism, documentary filmmaking, artificial intelligence and the global creative industries. Established in October 2025, the School brings together HKU’s Journalism and Media Studies Centre (JMSC), the Division of Documentary and AI Filmmaking, and the Division of Global Creative Industries, creating a distinctive platform for innovation across factual storytelling, screen-based media and emerging creative technologies. Building on the longstanding strengths of JMSC in journalism education and multimedia storytelling, SFM promotes an integrated approach spanning the humanities, creative arts and technology. It aims to prepare the next generation of storytellers, scholars and creators through interdisciplinary collaboration, ethical inquiry and engagement with the evolving media landscape in Hong Kong, the region and internationally. SFM offers undergraduate, taught postgraduate and research postgraduate programmes for a new generation of media professionals, creative practitioners and scholars. Current offerings include Bachelor of Journalism, Media and Artificial Intelligence, Bachelor of Arts in Global Creative Industries, Master of Journalism, Master of Journalism (Documentary Filmmaking Specialisation), Master of Arts in Creative Artificial Intelligence Film and Media, and a rigorous and interdisciplinary MPhil/PhD programme designed for aspiring scholars in journalism, media and communication studies. For more information about the School, please visit https://hkums.hku.hk/ . The Position The position is open to all areas in one or more of the following or related fields, including but not limited to: AI and generative AI in filmmaking Animation and game design Immersive and interactive media Computer vision Data journalism, data analytics, & technologies Business and finance journalism Digital humanities AI applications in journalism practices Entrepreneurship and innovation Global creative industries with expertise in one or more of the following areas: gaming and digital humanities, visual arts, heritage and museum studies, cultural industries, performing arts, visual communications. Duties and Responsibilities The appointees are expected to contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching and curriculum development, supervise postgraduate students, conduct high-quality research, and undertake administrative duties at SFM. Requirements A Ph.D. degree in film production and film studies, journalism and media studies, computer science, artificial intelligence, data science, and related fields; A strong commitment to excellence in research, teaching and mentoring; A proven track record in academic leadership and university-level administration; A distinguished and sustained record of conducting high-quality impactful research from publications, competitive grants and international recognition for scholarship; Strong connections and exposure in media industry or partners in China and/or Asia-Pacific region; Ability to establish strategic partnerships with industry and international academic institutions for fundraising, resource development and School’s advancement. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. Nomination, Expression of Interest and Application Applications from, and nominations of, individuals from diverse backgrounds are welcome, particularly those who are interested in contributing to the diversity and growth of the School of Future Media. Nominations, expressions of interest and applications should be directed in confidence to Heidrick & Struggles via email at hkusfm@heidrick.com . Review of nominations and applications will begin immediately and continue until the post is filled. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537462/research-assistant-professor-postdoctoral-fellow-in-mechanical-engineering": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537462 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Professional & Management Hong Kong Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering (Ref:537462 ) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities Carrying out research works under supervision for projects ranging from fundamental fluid dynamics and interfacial phenomena to biomedical and other applications Driving research activities towards defined goals in specified timeline Translating research to users through commercialization activities Processing in data analysis and management Drafting proposals, reports and presentations relevant to the projects Liaising with project collaborators and partners Performing various laboratory administrative duties Handling other relevant tasks as assigned by the supervisor(s) Requirements A PhD degree in Chemical Engineering / Biomedical Engineering / Mechanical Engineering / Chemistry or related engineering fields Relevant hands-on experience in microfluidics and diagnostic tool design is highly preferred Fresh graduates with outstanding academic achievement and strong passion in applied research of biomedical instrumentation will also be considered as Research Assistant Fluent in English in both writing and verbal communications; clear and concise writing skills Good time management with a strong sense of responsibility and research ethics Self-motivated team player who can be assertive to achieve results, and able to work under pressure What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 30, 2026 the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537462 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537462 Research Assistant Professor / Postdoctoral fellow in Mechanical Engineering Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
