    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537526/postdoctoral-fellow-several-posts-in-the-division-of-public-health-laboratory-sciences": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537526 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointments as Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537526), to commence as soon as possible, on a one- to three-year temporary term contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Bioinformatics or related disciplines, demonstrating a solid foundation in both biological science and computer science. They should have a strong background in virology research, with preference given to those with expertise in virus transmission, phylogenetic analysis and genomic sequence embedding. Proven experience in studying the patterns, drivers and mechanisms of the emergence of pathogens at human-animal interface including influenza and tick-borne viruses, and advanced bioinformatic data analysis—specifically involving microbiome, virome, and environmental metagenomics—is highly preferred. Applicants should be highly logical, detail-oriented, and self-motivated. An excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese is essential. The appointees will lead a research team to conduct comprehensive data analysis across diverse datasets, including genomic/ metagenomic sequencing data and ecological surveillance data, as well as spearhead the development of analysis pipelines. Working off-campus and outside of office hours may be required occasionally. Enquiries about the duties of this post should be sent to Mr. Eric Yip at yiperic@hku.hk . To learn more about the School's academic and research environment, please visit https://sph.hku.hk/ . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV, together with a cover letter and a list of relevant research publications.  Review of applications will start on October 12, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537526 Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences School of Public Health (22400) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537526 Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences School of Public Health (22400) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537533/executive-officerclerk-i-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-executive-assistant": {
      "title": "Executive Officer/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Officer/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537533 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537533) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis or one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above with at least 5 years’ full-time work experience, preferably in tertiary education institutions.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken Chinese and English; a strong sense of responsibility; and excellent organizational, interpersonal and communication skills.  They should also be self-motivated, attentive to details, able to handle multiple tasks, and work independently and in a team to meet tight deadlines.  Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience will be considered for appointment as Clerk I. The appointee will assist the Chief Department Administrator in providing comprehensive administrative support to the Department.  Key areas of responsibility may include: Human Resources Management Programme Administration Research Administration Finance and Budgeting He/She will also perform any other duties as assigned.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 537079) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible, and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537533 Executive Officer/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537533 Executive Officer/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
