    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537089/assistant-director-senior-manager-translational-research-and-commercialisation-at-the-rank-of-assistant-registrar-administrative-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537089 Work type: Full-time Department: Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) in the Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (RISE) (Ref.: 537089) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The University seeks a high-calibre, experienced professional to join us as Assistant Director/ Senior Manager, supporting translational research and commercialisation initiatives for the University and its subsidiaries, including R&D centres and partnership programmes, both locally and internationally. The appointee will develop strategic initiatives to advance translational research and commercialisation, leveraging the University’s strengths in life sciences to develop valuable IP assets, formulate commercialisation strategies, and build key partnerships and new ventures. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Vice-President (Research and Innovation) or their delegate and work collaboratively with faculties, units and subsidiaries across the University to foster a vibrant culture of innovation and entrepreneurship. Key Responsibility Develop and implement strategic initiatives to advance translational research, innovation, and commercialisation across the University and its subsidiaries, including R&D centres and partnership programmes. Identify, assess, and support high-potential technologies and research outcomes, providing guidance on intellectual property protection, development pathways, and commercialisation opportunities. Collaborate closely with academic faculties, researchers, innovators, and industry partners to accelerate the translation of research into societal and economic impact. Establish and strengthen strategic partnerships with industry, investors, regulators, government agencies, and international collaborators to create new opportunities for research translation and innovation. Negotiate and manage complex agreements related to research collaborations, intellectual property, licensing, venture creation, and strategic partnerships. Foster a vibrant innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystem by supporting incubation, acceleration, mentorship, and innovation programmes across the University. Promote the University's technology portfolio, innovation capabilities, and research strengths to industry leaders, investors, venture capital firms, and strategic partners globally. Qualifications and Qualities Possess a postgraduate degree, preferably a PhD, in a STEM, biomedical, healthcare, engineering, or related discipline; additional qualifications in business, innovation management, entrepreneurship, or intellectual property would be an advantage. Have at least 10 years of relevant experience in translational research, technology transfer, research commercialisation, business development, entrepreneurship, and venture investment, particularly within the life sciences or related fields. Demonstrate a successful track record of translating research outcomes into commercial or societal impact through licensing, startup formation, industry partnerships, or investment activities. Possess strong knowledge of intellectual property management, technology transfer, innovation ecosystems, and commercialisation practices. Have substantial experience in developing and managing collaborations with researchers, industry partners, investors, government agencies, and international stakeholders. Possess excellent communication, negotiation, stakeholder management, and relationship-building skills. Have experience working in Chinese Mainland and international markets, with an understanding of global innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems. Be highly self-motivated, proactive, results-oriented, and capable of managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Possess an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua Applicants with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for appointment as Senior Manager. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided, where applicable, for the position of Assistant Director. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's career site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ), and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 14, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537089 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537089 Assistant Director/ Senior Manager (Translational Research and Commercialisation) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/ Administrative Assistant I) Research, Innovation, Strategic Partnerships and Entrepreneurship (49500) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537376/fellowship-in-the-society-of-fellows-in-the-humanities": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537376 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Arts (04000) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Society of Fellows in the Humanities, Faculty of Arts The Society of Fellows in the Humanities aims to attract exceptional early-career postdoctoral scholars from around the world to Asia's global university. Located in one of the world's most dynamic cities and on Mainland China's doorstep, the University of Hong Kong offers unique opportunities to engage in cutting-edge research through its commitment to innovation and interdisciplinarity. The Faculty of Arts is one of HKU’s oldest and largest faculties and is consistently recognized as first in Asia for the Arts and Humanities. Its international outlook is reflected in the incredible diversity of its staff and students and its collaborations with other top universities around the globe. Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities (Ref.: 537376 ) The Society seeks outstanding applicants (appointed at the rank of Research Assistant Professor), with a flexible commencement date between June and August 2027 for a period of three years. The Society aims to establish a vibrant research community where Fellows interact with each other and other members of the Faculty.  Fellows will be expected to teach two courses during the term of their appointment and are required to submit a brief annual summary of their activities and accomplishments. The University of Hong Kong is an English-medium university. A host department within the Faculty of Arts will be selected on the basis of a Fellow’s proposed area of research. Applicants must have a PhD conferred after January 1, 2025, but not later than June 30, 2027. They will not be currently employed in tenure-track positions. A highly competitive package including medical benefits, annual leave, and conference and research support will be offered to the successful applicants. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. Applicants should apply online through the University’s careers website ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV, cover letter (not exceeding 300 words), research proposal (not exceeding 1500 words), and writing sample. They should arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent directly by the referees to the Society at sofhku@hku.hk . Please refer to the Society of Fellows website ( https://www.sof.arts.hku.hk ) for the requirements for application documents and other details. Application will be reviewed by a panel of scholars from across the spectrum of the arts and the humanities. The application process closes on December 15, 2026 . Successful applicants will be notified by the end of February 2027. The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expresslyencourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537376 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities Faculty of Arts (04000) Dec 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537376 Fellowship in the Society of Fellows in the Humanities Faculty of Arts (04000) Dec 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537481/senior-clinical-practitionerclinical-practitioner-in-oral-and-maxillofacial-radiology": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537481 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537481), to commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for up to nine months. For appointment as Senior Clinical Practitioner , applicants must possess a dental or medical (Bachelor’s) degree or equivalent and a clinical specialist status in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology or equivalent.  Their clinical expertise should enjoy regional acclaim as evidenced by extensive clinical or teaching experience, regional clinical publications/presentations, and regional recognition of clinical excellence in a clinical specialty. For appointment as Clinical Practitioner , applicants must possess a dental or medical (Bachelor’s) degree or equivalent, demonstrate sound clinical experience and have a good track record of continuing professional education or formal advanced education such as an MDS degree or equivalent. The appointee will deliver clinical teaching to undergraduate students, provide clinical service, and manage patients.  He/She may be considered for appointment as a Senior Clinical Practitioner if registered as a specialist and may also provide clinical training to postgraduate students.  Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Professor C. McGrath at mcgrathc@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The successful candidate is required to obtain a valid registration with the Dental Council of Hong Kong.  (Note: Applicants who do not hold a local dental license must fulfil the essential requirements under the laws of a jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, China, in order to be eligible for Limited Registration.  For details, please refer to the Dental Council of Hong Kong’s website at https://www.dchk.org.hk/en/registration/part_III.html .) The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  They should also indicate clearly which post (i.e. Senior Clinical Practitioner or Clinical Practitioner) they wish to be considered for and please note that the final decision will be made by the University.  Closes October 29, 2026 . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537481 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537481 Senior Clinical Practitioner/Clinical Practitioner in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537482/tenuretrack-clinical-associate-professorclinical-assistant-professor-in-oral-and-maxillofacial-radiology": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537482 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537482), to commence as soon as possible, on a four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure prior to the expiry of a second four-year fixed-term contract, subject to satisfactory performance. The Faculty of Dentistry is the only dental school in Hong Kong, China and the only one in China that uses English as the medium of instruction.  The high quality of the Faculty’s undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, research excellence, knowledge exchange (KE) and clinical/professional services have attained global recognition, as evidenced by the Faculty’s global rankings among the top three by the QS World University Rankings by Subject for ten out of the past twelve years (2015-2026).  The Faculty’s strategic research themes include AI+ & Precision Dentistry, Regenerative Dentistry, Global Oral Health, and Oral Ecosystem & One Health.  The Faculty also plays important roles in public and professional education through its KE activities and Global Education Hub for Oral Healthcare Professionals (GEHOHP), translational research & innovation via its Global Hub for Future Dentistry (GHFD) in collaboration with HKU Techno-Entrepreneurship Core and Hong Kong Science & Technology Parks Corporation, and enhancement of its global impacts through proactive engagement, networking and partnership. For appointment as Clinical Associate Professor , applicants should possess a dental or medical Bachelor's degree or equivalent, a clinical specialist qualification or equivalent status in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology, and a Ph.D. degree or equivalent.  They should also have: (i) proven evidence of quality research, publications in high quality international journals, and local and regional recognition for scholarship and professional expertise; (ii) demonstrated ability in undergraduate and postgraduate education, clinical practice and research; (iii) demonstrated participation in Faculty and University affairs; and (iv) demonstrated ability in knowledge exchange (KE) activities, and leadership in professional education programmes or community engagement. For appointment as Clinical Assistant Professor , applicants should possess a dental or medical Bachelor's degree or equivalent, and a Master of Dental Surgery degree or equivalent in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology.  They should also have (i) ability in undergraduate and postgraduate clinical teaching and practice; (ii) potential for and interest in research; (iii) ability and willingness to participate in Faculty affairs; and (iv) active participation in KE activities. Possession of good administrative and academic leadership skills will be an advantage.  Interest in artificial intelligence (AI) and big data applications in dentistry is a great merit. The appointee will be responsible for providing clinical training to dental undergraduates, teaching taught postgraduates, supervising research postgraduates, providing consultative service, and conducting research in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology. Information about the Faculty can be obtained at http://facdent.hku.hk/ .  For general enquiries, please contact Professor L.J. Jin, Dean of the Faculty of Dentistry at ljjin@hku.hk .  For information about the post, please contact Professor C. McGrath at mcgrathc@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The successful candidate is required to obtain a valid registration with the Dental Council of Hong Kong.  (Note: Applicants who do not hold a local dental license must fulfil the essential requirements under the laws of a jurisdiction outside Hong Kong, China, to be eligible for Limited Registration.  For details, please refer to the Dental Council of Hong Kong’s website at https://www.dchk.org.hk/en/registration/part_III.html .) The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ), and upload a cover letter, an up-to-date C.V., a research statement and a teaching statement.  They should also indicate clearly which post (i.e. Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Assistant Professor) they wish to be considered for and please note that the final decision will be made by the University.  Closes October 29, 2026 . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537482 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537482 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Assistant Professor in Oral and Maxillofacial Radiology Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 29, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
