    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537494/assistant-lecturer-several-posts": {
      "title": "Assistant Lecturer (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant Lecturer (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537494 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Assistant Lecturer (several posts) in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537494) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Nursing or a healthcare-related discipline, and be a holder of the Certificate of Registration (Part I) and valid Practising Certificate issued by the Nursing Council of Hong Kong, with a minimum of 3 years’ post-registration local clinical experience.  Preference will be given to those with higher academic qualifications and clinical teaching experience, particularly in general medical, surgical, or geriatric nursing. Applicants should have strong communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; the ability to work independently and as a team; and the capacity to work under pressure and multitask.  Those who are qualified as Advanced Practice Nurse (APN) will be offered the title of Advanced Practice Nurse. The appointees will report to the Chairman of the Teaching and Learning Committee.  They will be responsible for teaching, conducting tutorials, and providing practical and clinical supervision in Nursing.  Candidates with substantial clinical experience may also be assigned lecture teaching duties. They may be required to perform duties outside normal office hours. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536859) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. and at least 2 reference letters with specific comments on their competence.  Review of applications will start on October 14, 2026 and continue until December 9, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 9, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537494 Assistant Lecturer (several posts) School of Nursing (20800) Dec 9, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537494 Assistant Lecturer (several posts) School of Nursing (20800) Dec 9, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
