    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537515/senior-finance-manager-finance-manager": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior Finance Manager/ Finance Manager The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537515 Work type: Full-time Department: Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Senior Finance Manager/Finance Manager, Subsidiaries and Initiatives Team in the Finance and Enterprises Office (Ref.: 537515) The Role The appointee will be assigned to the Subsidiaries and Initiatives Team in performing the following duties: Oversee the team in executing routine or special financial tasks, including but not limited to preparation of statutory and management financial reports, budgets, and interim/year-end consolidation packages; Steer the timely submission of financial statements, reports, and schedules for university-owned subsidiaries located in Hong Kong, Chinese Mainland and international locations; Stay abreast of prevailing accounting standards, group policies, and local legislation; advise senior management on implications and ensure consistent implementation across all regions; Serve as the major contactpoint with auditors and tax consultants for compliance with all financial, tax, and regulatory requirements, including transfer pricing documentation and audit engagements; Lead the review of existing policies and procedures with proposed recommendations and implementation plans to enhance internal controls over the university’s subsidiary operations; Lead the establishment and execution of new initiatives, collaborating with cross-functional stakeholders on strategic budgeting, policy formulation, workflow design, approval processes, accounting treatments and reporting standards, etc.; Oversee administrative duties, including company secretarial matters of subsidiaries; Drive process optimization and automation initiatives to streamline and standardize financial operations and reporting workflows; Manage and develop a high-performing team, fostering professional growth and ensuring capability alignment with the management’s direction and expectation; Perform ad hoc tasks as assigned; and Occasional travel to Chinese Mainland may be required. Qualifications and Qualities A recognized Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related discipline; A professional qualification (e.g., HKICPA, ACCA, etc) is a must; Minimum of 10 years of relevant experience in financial management, with at least 5 years in a senior supervisory or managerial role overseeing multi-regional operations, ideally within universities or sizable non-profit making organizations; Proven experience in managing accounting, auditing, and financial reporting for subsidiaries in Hong Kong, Chinese Mainland, and international location; Extensive knowledge of Chinese Mainland accounting standards, tax regulations, and auditing practices; familiarity with cross-border financial compliance is essential; Strong understanding of international financial reporting standards and group consolidation processes; Demonstrated leadership skills, with the ability to lead and develop a diverse finance team and manage complex stakeholder relationships; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); ability to communicate effectively across cultures and regions; Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications (such as Excel, Word, PowerPoint) and experience with business intelligence tools such as QlikView or similar systems; Hands-on experience with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems, particularly Oracle Financials or equivalent, is highly an advantage; Strong sense of responsibility, strategic thinking, and the ability to work independently and under pressure to meet deadlines; and High level of integrity, professionalism, and commitment to organizational excellence. What We Offer Appointments will be made on fixed-term full-time contracts for 3 years for the Senior Finance Manager, or 2 years for the Finance Manager, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary for Senior Finance Manager and 10% of basic salary for Finance Manager. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test.  Candidates with less experience may be considered as Finance Manager. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 29, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537515 Senior Finance Manager/ Finance Manager Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Oct 29, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537515 Senior Finance Manager/ Finance Manager Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Oct 29, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
