    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537530/research-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Research Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537530 Work type: Full-time Department: Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant l/ll in the Sau Po Centre on Ageing within the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537530), to commence as soon as possible , on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. The Sau Po Centre on Ageing at HKU is dedicated to advancing research in the field of ageing and caregiving. Our mission is to improve the quality of life for older adults through innovative research and community engagement. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Social Sciences, Psychology, Public Health, Information Technology or related disciplinary studies, preferably with at least 1-year relevant work experience or further studies in healthcare, technology, gerontology. Relevant work experience in big data analysis, managing large databases of multiple research projects relating to family caregivers of older adults and/or geron-technology, and with related track records of academic publication should be advantageous. They should have a good command of written and spoken Chinese (fluency in Cantonese is required) and English, advanced knowledge and experience with statistical software (e.g., SPSS, R, Stata) and MS Office applications (including Word, Excel, PowerPoint etc.), and strong team work and communication skills. The applicants should be self-motivated, able to work independently and in a multidisciplinary team with collaboration with local and international experts to conduct high-impact and cutting-edge research related to family caregivers of older adults and/or geron-technology, and will be responsible for engaging in managing and executing projects, engaging with the community and stakeholders including project partners and collaborators to translate research into practice, and performing other duties as assigned. Shortlisted applicants will be invited to attend a data and written test, and an interview. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered in addition to University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity, and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537530 Research Assistant I/II Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537530 Research Assistant I/II Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537531/it-officer-it-technician-holding-functional-title-of-assistant-it-manager-it-system-specialist": {
      "title": "IT Officer / IT Technician (holding functional title of Assistant IT Manager / IT System Specialist)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 IT Officer / IT Technician (holding functional title of Assistant IT Manager / IT System Specialist) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537531 Work type: Full-time Department: Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as IT Officer / IT Technician (holding the functional title of Assistant IT Manager / IT System Specialist) in the Sau Po Centre on Ageing within the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537531), to commence as soon as possible, on a up to/ more than 1-year temporary term basis with University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. The Sau Po Centre on Ageing at HKU is dedicated to advancing research in the field of ageing and caregiving, aiming to become a leading research centre on gerontology in Greater China and the Asia Pacific region. Our mission is to improve the quality of life for older adults through innovative research and community engagement. We are committed to the enhancement of the well-being and quality of life of older adults and their caregivers through research, education, and knowledge exchange activities. Information about the Centre can be obtained at https://ageing.hku.hk/. We are looking for a highly dynamic and proactive IT professional who excels in project management, execution, and quality assurance, with a solid background on vender management. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science, Information Technology, or other related disciplines, at least 5 years’ relevant work experience in managing vendor for IT system development, enhancement and maintenance, and handling stakeholder engagement. Relevant experience in community projects is preferred. Applicants should also be a good team leader with strong sense of responsibility, effective communication, analytical and problem – solving skills, and willingness to learn. Proficiency in English and Chinese (including Cantonese) is required. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as IT Technician. Relevant experience in the following areas will be an advantage: Full-Stack & API Development: Built dynamic web applications and microservices using modern web programming languages, JSON data interchange, and robust RESTful API development. Database & Data Management: Managed relational databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, MS SQL Server) and NoSQL systems, writing advanced SQL scripts, handling data migrations, and leveraging data analysis tools. DevOps & Infrastructure: Deployed containerized environments using Docker and configured automated CI/CD pipelines for secure server management. AI & Project Management: Integrated AI models and automation tools into workflows, applying Agile/SDLC principles and light project management experience. The appointee will support the development of mission-critical online platform for our community project to service the home-bound carers. He/She will: solicit, analyze, and convert user requirements into system specification and prioritize user requirements according to the operational impact; perform quality assurance test before user acceptance test; support the development of communication and training strategy for solution delivery by coordinating with involved stakeholders (including University IT Services and vendors, our community partners); and perform any other duties as assigned by Centre Director Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and attend an interview. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity, and transparency. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537531 IT Officer / IT Technician (holding functional title of Assistant IT Manager / IT System Specialist) Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537531 IT Officer / IT Technician (holding functional title of Assistant IT Manager / IT System Specialist) Sau Po Centre on Ageing (30302) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537532/finance-manager-assistant-finance-manager": {
      "title": "Finance Manager/ Assistant Finance Manager",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Finance Manager/ Assistant Finance Manager The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537532 Work type: Full-time Department: Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Finance Manager/Assistant Finance Manager in Faculty Partnership & Solutions Team in the Finance and Enterprises Office (Ref.: 537532) The Role The appointee will be assigned to the Faculty Partnership and Solution Team in performing the following duties: Supervise a team to perform the financial control and management for the assigned faculties, including budgetary control, resource allocations, research projects vetting, and regular review of financial position; Handle and resolve inquiries on budget and financial matters in accordance with the established policies and procedures; Manage project accounts to ensure the accuracy of financial reports and timely submission; Support year-end closing procedures and liaise with auditors during the annual audit; Prepare finance reports and analysis in accordance with relevant accounting standards and regulatory requirements; Assist in updating and reviewing the University's financial policies and procedures, as well as other manuals related to financial operations; and Perform any ad hoc duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities A recognized Bachelor's degree in Accounting/Finance or related disciplines with at least 6 years’ relevant experience preferably in universities or sizable organisations with a minimum of 3 years at the supervisory level; A qualified accountant and/or member of recognised professional accounting bodies; A strong sense of responsibility and commitment, good supervisory skills, and ability to work independently; Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications (including Excel, Word and PowerPoint) and QlikView or other business intelligent systems; and Hands-on experience in Oracle Financials would be an advantage. What We Offer Appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Candidates with less experience may be considered as Assistant Finance Manager. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 29, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to prompting equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537532 Finance Manager/ Assistant Finance Manager Finance and Ent