    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537535/executive-assistant-mba-programme-operations": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant, MBA Programme Operations",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Executive Assistant, MBA Programme Operations The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537535 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant, MBA Programme Operations (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537535) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a bachelor’s degree with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience, preferably in a tertiary institution.  They should have an excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Mandarin), good organisational, interpersonal and communication skills, with cultural awareness and strong computer literacy.  They should be good team players who are detail-oriented and self-motivated, and able to work independently, also with a customer service orientation, and the ability to handle crises gracefully.  Experience in handling Student Information System (SIS) would be an advantage. The appointee will provide support to the MBA Programme. Major duties include course administration, handling student enquiries and grievance cases from Greater Bay Area (GBA), liaising with professors about classroom logistics and course materials, staffing student events, producing office documentation and reports; and perform other duties as assigned.  The appointee will be required to work on weekday evenings, weekends and public holidays. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview.  He/She will work at the Cyberport campus. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537535 Executive Assistant, MBA Programme Operations Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537535 Executive Assistant, MBA Programme Operations Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
