    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537423/project-manager-alumni-affairs": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Project Manager (Alumni Affairs) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537423 Work type: Full-time Department: Development & Alumni Affairs Office (60800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Project Manager (Alumni Affairs) (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Development & Alumni Affairs Office (DAAO) (Ref.: 537423) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance). The appointee will be joining a dynamic and collaborative team dedicated to engaging HKU’s alumni community through a wide range of events, donation campaigns and outreach initiatives. We are looking for a motivated and creative team player who is excited to embrace fun and meaningful challenges, try new ideas, and contribute to meaningful alumni engagement work. He/she will be reporting to the Assistant Director (Alumni Affairs) in handling the execution of a range of tasks, including but not limited to alumni engagement and relationship management, event and project management, social media communications and administrative support. Key Responsibilities He/She will: assist in the planning, organisation and execution of alumni events and activities, including campus reunions, alumni tours, networking events and other engagement programmes; support annual congregation-related events and preparation work, including planning, coordination of logistics, materials preparation, on-site arrangements and liaison with relevant parties; assist in managing the Office’s social media content and channels, including content planning, drafting, scheduling, coordination of creative assets, and monitoring of audience engagement; support content development for platforms such as Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, LinkedIn, WeChat, and others; assist in maintaining alumni relationships, handling alumni enquiries, updating alumni-related records and supporting alumni outreach initiatives; coordinate with internal departments and external vendors on operational matters, including procurement, payment processing, logistics, venue arrangements, moving-related matters and other administrative duties; perform any other duties as assigned. Some evening, weekend or public holiday work may be required occasionally for alumni events and University activities. Compensation leave will be offered. Requirements Applicants should possess the following qualifications: a good university degree, with at least 3 years of relevant experience; relevant experience in event management, alumni relations, external communications, marketing and social media management would be an advantage; work experience in university alumni relations and / or familiarity with HKU culture and structure would be highly preferred; an excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese, including fluency in Cantonese and Putonghua; strong communication, organisational and problem-solving skills; a dedicated team player who is attentive to details, service-oriented, able to multi-task, and able to work independently with initiative and under pressure to meet tight deadlines; familiarity with major social media platforms, including Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, LinkedIn, WeChat and Xiaohongshu; and experience in creating creative content for social media would be preferred. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Project Executive. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V., together with samples of past social media, marketing, creative or relevant communications work, and/or samples of past HKU-related project work. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537433/tenuretrack-professor-associate-professor-assistant-professor-several-posts-in-the-school-of-computing-and-data-science": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (several posts) in the School of Computing and Data Science",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (several posts) in the School of Computing and Data Science The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537433 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for joint appointments as Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (several posts ) in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537433), to commence in September 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. The appointment rank will be determined based on the qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. For Assistant Professors, the appointment will initially be made on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and with consideration for tenure before the expiry of the second three-year fixed-term contract, subject to satisfactory performance. Exceptionally outstanding candidates at Professor/Associate Professor level may be considered for appointment on tenure terms, subject to the University’s approval. The School of Computing and Data Science (CDS) strives to advance education and research across artificial intelligence, computer science, data science, and statistics and actuarial science. It aims to take an integrated approach to reform these academic disciplines and foster multidisciplinary research collaboration within the University and beyond. For more information about the School, please visit www.cds.hku.hk . The Positions 1. Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor These positions are open to all research areas in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or a related field, including but not limited to: AI for Social Good BioAI Computer Graphics and Vision Database Systems Embodied AI and Robotics FinTech Human-AI Interaction Machine Learning Natural Language Processing Programming Languages and Verification Quantum Information and Computation Scalable Data Analytics and AI Security Software Engineering Systems and Architecture Theoretical Computer Science The appointment rank will be determined based on the qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. Appointees will be expected to contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, supervise graduate students, conduct high-quality research, and participate in administrative duties at CDS. 2. Tenure-track Assistant Professor (under AI+X initiative) We are seeking outstanding interdisciplinary scholars in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Data Science, or a related field who can develop creative and innovative research and teaching programmes that bridge artificial intelligence with other disciplines. Appointees will be hosted by CDS and will be co-hosted by another Faculty / School / Department at the University, as appropriate, depending on their expertise and research profile. The appointees are expected to contribute to research and teaching activities that strengthen sustained collaboration between CDS and the co-host unit. Requirements A Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or another relevant field; A solid research track record commensurate with the rank sought; A strong commitment to excellence in research and teaching, together with demonstrated or potential academic leadership; For joint appointments under AI+X, a strong cross-disciplinary research profile and a clear agenda for building research and teaching programmes that connect AI with another discipline; and For appointment at Professor level, outstanding and internationally recognised research achievements. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave, professional leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salary tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. A start-up package commensurate with the needs and experience of the appointee will be provided. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload a cover letter, an up-to-date curriculum vitae, a research statement outlining current and future research plans and interests, a teaching statement, relevant teaching evaluations where available, three representative recent or significant research publications, and the contact information of three referees. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and will be conducted on a rolling basis, continuing until May 31, 2027 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: May 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537433 Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (several posts) in the School of Computing and Data Science School of Computing and Data Science (14700) May 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537433 Tenure-track Professor / Associate Professor / Assistant Professor (several posts) in the School of Computing and Data Science School of Computing and Data Science (14700) May 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537479/assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537479 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Engineering (24000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the School of Biomedical Engineering (Ref.: 537479) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The School of Biomedical Engineering (SBME) is a newly established school at HKU which brings together talents from the Faculties of Engineering, Medicine, Science and Dentistry to train the next generation of biomedical engineers. We are seeking an experienced administrator to help build and run the School's academic programmes during this formative period. Information about the School can be obtained at https://sbme.hku.hk/ . Applicants should possess a good university degree and preferably have at least 5 years’ work experience in the higher education sector or a related field. They should be excellent communicators with a strong sense of responsibility and the ability to motivate team members to deliver quality work under tight deadlines, as well as to lead and inspire a team. They should have an excellent command of English and Chinese (Cantonese and/or Putonghua); a high level of interpersonal, organisational, time management and problem-solving skills; and an appropriate level of IT knowledge are essential. Experience in programme management, marketing, social media, and event coordination would be desirable. The appointee will provide administrative support in undergraduate programme, including admissions, registration, timetabling, assessment, student affairs, curriculum revisions, quality assurance and enhancement, and committee support. He/ She will also support postgraduate programmes, student recruitment, outreach events and other School initiatives. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 13, 2026 and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537479 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) School of Biomedical Engineering (24000) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537479 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) School of Biomedical Engineering (24000) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537485/administrative-assistant-i-to-be-seconded-to-gbaicti-as-its-director-global-communications-engagement": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Director (Global Communications & Engagement))",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Administrative Assistant I (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Director (Global Communications & Engagement)) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537485 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant I (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Director (Global Communications & Engagement)) (Ref.: 537485) The Greater Bay Area International Clinical Trial Institute (GBAICTI) is a wholly-owned entity of the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, positioning as a centralized clinical research facilitation platform with the mission and vision of creating and sustaining a thriving clinical research ecosystem and energizing the development of a healthy and wealthy society through biomedical innovation, research, translation and development in Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area (GBA). The University of Hong Kong Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) is appointed as the operator of GBAICTI. We are seeking a high calibre talent to join the operation team as Director (Global Communications & Engagement). Main Responsibilities: Report to the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) and supervise the Office of Global Communications & Engagement (OGCE); Formulate and direct the implementation of strategies on global communication with professional communities in clinical research and biomedical development and on involvement and engagement of the local public; Facilitate partnership and collaboration with the biomedical industry; Build and maintain professional networks in various clinical specialty areas to enhance collaboration in clinical research; Develop and manage a clinical research portal, corporate websites and social media channels to facilitate communication with stakeholders including investigators and clinical research professionals, the biomedical industry and the public; Organize professional conferences, symposia, forums, seminars and exhibitions to facilitate professional knowledge exchange; Support the CEO in exercising corporate governance and compliance; Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Holder of a bachelor’s degree; A minimum of 10 aggregate years of supervisory experience, acquired in the last 20 years; Solid experience in corporate communications, new media and/or event management, preferably in the clinical research industry; Knowledge in clinical research (including research ethics and good clinical practice) is an added advantage; Proficiency in common office applications (e.g. MS Office including Word, Excel and PowerPoint); Hands-on experience in project management, database, graphic design and multimedia applications (e.g. MS Project, Access, Visio, Photoshop, Illustrator and VSDC) is an added advantage; Commitment to quality, integrity, confidentiality and compliance; Excellent leadership, organizational, project management and problem-solving skills; Strong interpersonal, communication and stakeholders management skills; Detail-minded, able to handle multiple concurrent tasks and self-motivated; A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including both Cantonese and Putonghua). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 13, 2026 and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537485 Administrative Assistant I (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Director (Global Communications & Engagement)) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537485 Administrative Assistant I (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Director (Global Communications & Engagement)) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537488/teaching-assistant": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Teaching Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537488 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Teaching Assistant in the Faculty of Social Sciences (2 posts) (Ref.: 537488), to commence in January 2027 or as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Social Sciences, Computer Science, Computational Social Science, or a related discipline, with at least one year of teaching and/or research experience. They should have excellent analytical, problem-solving and communication skills, a high level of proficiency in written and spoken English, and a good command of Chinese. Knowledge of mainstream Large Language Models (LLMs), such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek, Muse Spark and Kimi, and working experience with Agentic AI is preferred.  Preference will be given to those with teaching and/or research experience in computational social science, relevant programming and data analysis skills, and familiarity with computational tools such as machine learning, text analytics, and social network analysis. The appointees will provide teaching support to the undergraduate courses offered by the Faculty of Social Sciences.  They will assist the course instructor(s) in preparing teaching materials, conducting small-group tutorial classes, marking assignments and offering feedback, supervising student work, invigilating examinations, and undertaking other duties as assigned by the course instructor. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 23, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537488 Teaching Assistant Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 23, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537488 Teaching Assistant Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 23, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537492/town-planning-manager-assistant-town-planning-manager-at-the-rank-of-technical-manager-i-ii": {
      "title": "Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537492 Work type: Full-time Department: Estates Office (66061) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II) in the Estates Office (Ref.: 537492) We are looking for a Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II) to join the Estates Office. The Role Reporting to the Assistant Director of Estates, the appointee will be responsible for town planning, land administration and development, and campus planning matters of the University. The appointee will support the University’s strategic development objectives by identifying and evaluating development opportunities; undertaking land-use research, feasibility assessments and planning studies; securing relevant statutory planning and land approvals; and coordinating consultants, professional advisers, Government departments and other stakeholders on land, planning, urban design and related technical matters.  The appointee will provide professional advice to senior management on the strategic, optimal and sustainable use of the University’s land and property assets and perform other assigned duties. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A recognised university degree in Town Planning, Urban Planning / Design or related disciplines; Corporate Membership of the Hong Kong Institute of Planners (HKIP), or an equivalent professional qualification with relevant work experience in Hong Kong planning practice; At least 5 years’ relevant post-qualification experience, preferably with experience in a supervisory, managerial or project leadership capacity; Sound knowledge of Hong Kong’s statutory planning system (in particular master planning, planning applications, rezoning applications and related technical assessments) and land administration matters; Proven experience in liaising with Government departments, statutory authorities, consultants and other stakeholders; Good stakeholder management, communication, analytical, presentation and report writing skills; The ability to work independently, exercise professional judgement, solve complex problems and manage multiple assignments proactively; Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications; An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; and Working knowledge of Geographic Information Systems (GIS) (e.g. ArcGIS) and Graphic Design Software (e.g. AutoCAD, Photoshop and SketchUp) would be an advantage. Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager II). What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.   A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 26, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537492 Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II) Estates Office (66061) Oct 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537492 Town Planning Manager / Assistant Town Planning Manager (at the rank of Technical Manager I / II) Estates Office (66061) Oct 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537495/technical-manager-to-be-seconded-to-gbaicti-as-its-manager-process-innovation-optimization": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Technical Manager (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Manager (Process Innovation & Optimization)) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537495 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Technical Manager (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Manager (Process Innovation & Optimization)) (Ref.: 537495) The Greater Bay Area International Clinical Trial Institute (GBAICTI) is a wholly-owned entity of the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, positioning as a centralized clinical research facilitation platform with the mission and vision of creating and sustaining a thriving clinical research ecosystem and energizing the development of a healthy and wealthy society through biomedical innovation, research, translation and development in Hong Kong and the Greater Bay Area (GBA). The University of Hong Kong Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) is appointed as the operator of GBAICTI. We are seeking a high calibre talent to join the operation team as Manager (Process Innovation & Optimization). Main Responsibilities: Report to the Vice-President (Process Innovation & Optimization) and support the management and operation of the Office of Research Process Innovation & Optimization (OPIO); Connect and engage with industry partners, regulators, public and private hospitals/medical institutions, clinical trials centres to advance clinical trial capability and efficiency in Hong Kong; Support continuing evaluation of the operational efficiency of clinical trial end-to-end processes (such as in the domains of research ethics review and oversight, regulatory review, research project contracting and financial management, informed consent, clinical trial operations, audit and inspection readiness), and recommend strategies and initiatives to key stakeholders to accelerate clinical trial initiation, enhance overall operational efficiency and enhance quality of delivery; Support to drive clinical trial innovation and technology adoption to enhance overall operations and compliance of trial conduct; Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Holder of a bachelor’s degree in medicine, pharmacy, biotechnology, life sciences or related subjects; A minimum of 5 years of experience in the clinical research profession; Good knowledge and experience in local clinical research operations, processes and regulations, ICH GCP, industrial standards and digital health technologies (DHT); Experience in SOP management, process optimization in biomedical enterprises, contract research organizations or clinical research institutions is a definite advantage; Proficient in common office applications (e.g. MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Teams); hands-on experience with project management and database tools (e.g. Power BI and Visio), as well as process mapping and root cause analysis tools, would be an added advantage; Commitment to quality, integrity, confidentiality and compliance; Good organizational, project management and problem-solving skills; Good interpersonal and communication skills; Detail-minded, able to handle multiple concurrent tasks and self-motivated; A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese; Proficiency in Putonghua is an added advantage. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 13, 2026 and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537495 Technical Manager (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Manager (Process Innovation & Optimization)) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537495 Technical Manager (to be seconded to GBAICTI as its Manager (Process Innovation & Optimization)) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
