    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537496/head-strategy-and-operations-at-the-rank-of-assistant-registraradministrative-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Head (Strategy and Operations) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Head (Strategy and Operations) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537496 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Engineering (14000) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Head (Strategy and Operations) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I) in the Faculty of Engineering (Ref.:537496), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a good Bachelor’s degree with at least 10 years of relevant full-time administrative and management experience, preferably gained in the tertiary education sector. A higher degree would be an advantage. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Cantonese and Putonghua. Applicants should be mature, meticulous, self-motivated, and collaborative team players with strong organisational, leadership, and communication skills. They should possess the ability to think strategically, drive initiatives, build effective stakeholder relationships, and manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment. They should exercise sound judgment and demonstrate initiative in handling a wide range of responsibilities. A strong commitment to service excellence and results, coupled with excellent interpersonal, time-management, problem-solving, and multitasking abilities, is essential. Experience in leading teams, managing complex operations, and working across Hong Kong and Mainland China would be an advantage. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant I. The appointee will play a key role in advancing the Faculty’s strategic priorities and its operations in Hong Kong and Shanghai. Working closely with the Faculty’s leadership, the appointee will contribute to the formulation and implementation of strategic initiatives aligned with the Faculty’s long-term goals, and ensure effective coordination and operational integration across Hong Kong and other locations. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to: Facilitating the strategic development and operations of the Faculty of Engineering at the HKU Zhangjiang Base in Shanghai, with oversight of key functional areas, including human resources, accounting and financial management, site administration, academic programme administration, event coordination, external engagement, and general office administration; Driving the planning and implementation of strategic initiatives, policies, and procedures, while fostering close coordination between the Faculty’s Hong Kong and Shanghai operations; Advising and supporting the Faculty’s management, including the Dean, Associate Deans, and the Faculty Secretary, on strategic, operational, and administrative matters, and contributing to the effective governance and management of the Faculty; Leading a team of staff to deliver high-quality services; address complex operational issues; and promote continuous improvement in systems, processes, and service standards; Acting for the Faculty Secretary, as and when required; and Representing the Faculty and cultivating effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders in Shanghai, Hong Kong, and other locations, as necessary. The role may require periodic travel to Mainland China to spearhead the Faculty’s strategic initiatives. It requires a proactive and adaptable individual with strategic vision, sound judgment, and the ability to lead complex operations and manage multiple priorities in a dynamic academic environment. The appointee will also perform other duties as assigned by the Dean and the Faculty Secretary in support of the Faculty’s mission and objectives. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Housing benefits will be provided for the Assistant Registrar rank. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537496 Head (Strategy and Operations) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I) Faculty of Engineering (14000) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537496 Head (Strategy and Operations) (at the rank of Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I) Faculty of Engineering (14000) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
