    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537498/senior-research-assistant-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537498 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health (Ref. no.: 537498), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. HKU has partnered with the International Vaccine Institute (IVI) and The University of Cambridge to establish the HKJCGHI, with funding support from The Hong Kong Jockey Club Charities Trust. IVI is a non-profit international organization dedicated to vaccines and vaccination for global health. The Epidemiology, Public Health and Impact (EPIC) Unit coordinates HKJCGHI’s work streams in epidemiology, pandemic preparedness and capacity building. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Epidemiology, Public Health, Biostatistics, or a related field. A PhD degree in a relevant discipline is an advantage but not required. Applicants should have 1–3 years of experience in epidemiological research, preferably in the fields of infectious diseases, vaccines, pandemic preparedness or antimicrobial resistance. Applicants should demonstrate strong quantitative skills, including experience with statistical software such as R, SAS, or Stata, and the ability to manage and analyze large epidemiological datasets. Familiarity with the design and implementation of epidemiological studies is highly desirable. They should have excellent written and spoken English skills. Preference will be given to candidates with prior work experience in global health, international organizations, or low- and middle-income country (LMIC) settings. The appointee will work closely with the Research Scientist to support research activities on epidemiology and pandemic preparedness under HKJCGHI, and report to the HKJCGHI Programme Director in Hong Kong. Key responsibilities include contributing to the design, implementation and monitoring of epidemiological studies related to infectious disease surveillance and pandemic preparedness; managing and analyzing related data to support research objectives; assisting in the development of research protocols, data collection tools, and ethic applications for studies; contributing to the preparation of research reports, manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals, and presentations for scientific meetings; collaborating with internal and relevant external stakeholders; and supporting capacity-building activities and knowledge translation efforts in LMICs. The appointee may also be required to assist in organizing meetings and facilitate procurement activities related to laboratory diagnostics. He/She is expected to undertake regular international travel to field sites in Africa and Asia to monitor project implementation and progress. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will receive a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme totaling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start from October 13, 2026 and continue until December 10, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 10, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537498 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 10, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537498 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 10, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537499/senior-research-assistant-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537499 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health (Ref. no.: 537499), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. HKU has partnered with the International Vaccine Institute (IVI) and The University of Cambridge to establish the HKJCGHI, with funding support from The Hong Kong Jockey Club Charities Trust. IVI is a non-profit international organization dedicated to vaccines and vaccination for global health. The Epidemiology, Public Health and Impact (EPIC) Unit of IVI coordinates HKJCGHI’s work streams in epidemiology, pandemic preparedness and capacity building. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Epidemiology, Biostatistics, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Public Health or a related discipline with a strong quantitative focus. A PhD degree in a relevant discipline would be an advantage but is not required. Applicants should have 3–4 years of experience in mathematical modelling and/or statistical inference relevant to epidemiological studies of infectious diseases, with a proven track record of leading research projects and publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Applicants should have expertise in study design, as well as in the formulation and implementation of mathematical or computational models of infectious diseases. They should also have an interest in, or experience with, integrating climate change variables, sociodemographic factors, and other area-level covariates into disease modelling. Experience working with diverse datasets, including epidemiological, surveillance, demographic, and climate data, is essential. Proficiency in programming languages such as R, Python, MATLAB, or C++ for modelling and analysis is required. Familiarity with statistical methods, machine learning techniques, and tools for data visualization would be an advantage. Experience in using agentic artificial intelligence to facilitate analysis workflows is an additional advantage, but is not required. The appointee will work closely with Research Scientists and the biostatistics team at IVI. IVI has an extensive global network of field sites and databases spanning 20 years of vaccine-related field studies. Drawing on existing IVI EPIC databases from IVI projects and field sites, the appointee will contribute to the design, development, and implementation of mathematical and computational models to simulate infectious disease transmission dynamics, progression, and intervention strategies, with a particular focus on the intersection of infectious diseases and climate change. The appointee will work closely with the Data Scientist to incorporate climate change variables, such as extreme weather events, temperature, precipitation, and environmental factors, into models to explore the impacts of climate variability on disease dynamics. He/She will be expected to integrate epidemiological, demographic, health systems, and climate data into modelling frameworks to inform public health policies and intervention planning. He/She will lead research projects, define research objectives, manage project timelines, coordinate internal and external collaborators, publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals, and present findings at conferences and stakeholder meetings. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed-term contract will receive a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start from October 6, 2026 and continue until December 10, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 10, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537499 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 10, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537499 Senior Research Assistant in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 10, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537502/administrative-assistant-iiexecutive-officer-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-managermanager-in-the-asia-case-research-centre-several-posts": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Manager/Manager) in the Asia Case Research Centre (Several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Manager/Manager) in the Asia Case Research Centre (Several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537502 Work type: Full-time Department: Asia Case Research Centre (07005) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Manager/Manager) in the Asia Case Research Centre, Faculty of Business and Economics (several posts) (Ref.: 537502) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and mutual agreement.) The Asia Case Research Centre (ACRC) is a research centre affiliated with the Faculty of Business and Economics at The University of Hong Kong.  The ACRC is committed to the advancement of learning and teaching in business education and strives to promote leading management thinking through research on the latest practices in the Asian business environment.  We work with scholars from universities and institutions within and outside the region, and enjoy close ties with the business community. Applicants should hold a master’s or higher degree in Business Administration, Finance, Economics, or a closely related discipline, along with at least three to nine years of proven experience in a position involving staff supervision.  Familiarity with the Case Teaching Method in business education, as well as strong research, writing, and organizational skills are required.  An excellent command of written English is essential, and native-level written Chinese is an advantage.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and interviews. Applicants with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered as Executive Officer. This role is built around reading, writing, and editorial judgment. The appointees will spend a majority of their time working through case study drafts, shaping them into polished, curriculum-aligned teaching materials for the Faculty of Business and Economics and beyond, while working closely with faculty, case writers, and business leaders to (i) source and develop compelling case studies, and (ii) build trusted senior-level relationships that underpin sustained collaboration. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience shall be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 533661 and 536149) need not to reapply. The University only accepts online application for the above posts  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537502 Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Manager/Manager) in the Asia Case Research Centre (Several posts) Asia Case Research Centre (07005) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537502 Administrative Assistant II/Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Manager/Manager) in the Asia Case Research Centre (Several posts) Asia Case Research Centre (07005) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
