    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537503/scientific-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Scientific Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537503 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Scientific Officer in the Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537503), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree preferably in Mechanical Engineering, Ophthalmology, or related disciplines, with at least 10 years' solid experience in clinical research.  Those with expertise in the development and design of virtual reality platform for the evaluation of visual disability would be preferred.  Applicants should also have good interpersonal and organizational skills, a strong sense of responsibility and self-motivation, an excellent command of written and spoken English, good interpersonal and communication skills, and the ability to multi-task and work independently and collaboratively as a team. The appointee will be involved in research projects related to the development of novel pharmacological treatments for ocular diseases and investigations in neuroregeneration and neuroprotection. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload the following documents: A cover letter describing your most significant scientific accomplishment, the qualifications that make you particularly well suited for this job, and your future work plan; A curriculum vitae and publication list highlighting the most important papers with detailed bibliometric information on each publication listed, including (i) the impact factor of the journal; (ii) journal rank in category in the format of ‘the rank out of total number of journals in that specific category’, with reference to Journal Citation Reports (JCR); and (iii) authorship role ((co-)first author, (co-)corresponding author or last author); and Two reference letters Review of applications will start on 12 October 2026 and continue until 26 October 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537503 Scientific Officer Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Oct 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537503 Scientific Officer Department of Ophthalmology, School of Clinical Medicine (22300) Oct 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537504/manager-career-development-training-mba-programmes-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Manager, Career Development & Training (MBA Programmes) (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537504 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Manager, Career Development & Training (MBA Programmes) (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537504) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) We are seeking a dynamic and experienced Career Manager to join our team. The ideal candidate should hold a bachelor’s degree with at least 10 years of relevant experience in corporate business development, strategic partnerships, relationship management, recruitment or related fields. We are looking for someone who is proactive, resourceful and commercially minded, with strong communication, interpersonal, organizational and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate should be passionate about helping students grow and succeed, offering patient support while guiding, motivating and challenging them when appropriate. They should confidently engage corporate partners; understand their talent needs and proactively identify suitable career opportunities for MBA students. Strong business acumen, sound judgement and a willingness to go the extra mile are essential. Based at the Faculty’s Cyberport campus, the Career Manager will support MBA career development and training. Responsibilities include developing and maintaining corporate and recruiting partnerships, promoting MBA talent to employers, organizing recruitment talks, international career treks, leadership and industry forums, and managing career resources. The role also involves hands-on project management, event logistics, administration and internal reporting. We are looking for a committed and accountable team player who takes ownership and sees projects through from start to finish, while being equally comfortable working independently. Excellent written and spoken English is required, with proficiency in Mandarin and/or Cantonese highly preferred. If you enjoy building relationships, creating opportunities and making a meaningful difference in students’ career journeys, we would love to hear from you. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and a presentation session. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue for October 19, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 19, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537504 Manager, Career Development & Training (MBA Programmes) (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 19, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537504 Manager, Career Development & Training (MBA Programmes) (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Oct 19, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537507/senior-executive-assistant-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537507 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537507) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above with 5 years’ work experience, preferably in tertiary institutions.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; IT proﬁciency; good communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; and the ability to work independently.  Those with less experience may be considered for appointment as Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II). The appointee will provide executive and administrative support to the Administration Office in one or more of the following areas, including Finance, Research, Event Coordination, Taught Postgraduate Programmes, and Human Resources.  He/She will support day-to-day operations of the Office, and perform other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 12, 2026 and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537507 Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537507 Senior Executive Assistant/ Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
