    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537538/research-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537538 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Pathology, School of Clinical Medicine (21200) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Department of Pathology, School of Clinical Medicine and the State Key Laboratory of Liver Research (Ref.: 537538)  (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and availability of funding) Position Description: The Department of Pathology is seeking a highly self-motivated and dedicated Research Assistant II to support cutting-edge translational research in using extracellular vesicles (EVs) for diagnosis and therapy of liver cancer. The successful candidate will work closely with Dr. Lucy Tian (From Prof. Irene Ng’s research team) on projects involving clinical-relevant projects and molecular mechanisms of immunotherapy resistant in liver cancer. Our research aims to develop novel EV-based strategies for biomarker detection and to engineer EVs as targeted drug-delivery vehicles. Key Responsibilities: Cell Biology: Conduct standard cell culture, cell manipulation and functional assays. Molecular Biology: Perform routine laboratory assays including bacteria culture, cloning , plasmid preparation , qPCR, Western blotting, flow cytometry. Animal Work: Handle mouse work, including husbandry, xenograft allocation, drug administration, tumor monitor and measurement, tissue dissociation. Data record: Use logbook to record experiments, analyze the data using scientific software, including GraphPad Prism, SPSS, flow jo, ZEN, image J, etc Qualifications and Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree or Master/M.Phil. degree in Medicine, Biomedical Sciences, Biochemistry, Biotechnology, Molecular Biology, Pharmacy or a related discipline. Hands-on experience with basic molecular biology techniques (Western blot, qPCR, cloning) and animal work is preferred. Strong organizational and communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work collaboratively in a team environment. Good command of written and spoken English and Mandarin. Skills in bioinformatic analysis is preferred, but not mandatory. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Enquiries about the post should be sent to Dr. Lucy Tian at lucytian@hku.hk. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until Oct 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University thanks applicants for their interest but advises that only candidates shortlisted for interviews will be notified of the application result. Advertised: Sep 29, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537538 Research Assistant II Department of Pathology, School of Clinical Medicine (21200) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537538 Research Assistant II Department of Pathology, School of Clinical Medicine (21200) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537470/office-attendant": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories General Support Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Office Attendant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537470 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: General Support Staff Hong Kong Office Attendant in the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537470) We are looking for an Office Attendant to join the Faculty of Dentistry to handle general office administrative work. The Role The appointee will handle general office administrative tasks and assist with office operations.  Duties include replenishing pantry supplies, assisting with the arrangement of maintenance work for office facilities and equipment, keeping office areas tidy and clean, acting as a backup for the receptionist, preparing tea, delivering documents outdoors, assisting with examinations, and performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities Form 3 or equivalent, with at least 1 year’s solid work experience; Good interpersonal and communication skills; Ability to communicate in Cantonese and write simple Chinese and English; Ability to work independently; and Fluency in Putonghua would be an advantage. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 18, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 18, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537470 Office Attendant Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 18, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537470 Office Attendant Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 18, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
