    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537468/nurse": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Nurse The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537468 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Nurse in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537468) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The SToP Research Program under Professor K.K.A. Chung is now recruiting full-time Nurse. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or equivalent, and be registered with the Nursing Council of Hong Kong. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese); good communication skills; and the ability to work independently and as a team. Research experience and/or experiences in conducting repetitive transcranial magnetic stimulation (rTMS) would be an advantage. Preference will be given to candidates who plan to pursue postgraduate studies. The appointee will provide basic nursing care, conduct on-site interviews with subjects, perform phlebotomy and research interventions, implement assessment programmes, perform data entry and analysis, prepare manuscripts, and conduct other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The university only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ), and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start on October 12, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537468 Nurse Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537468 Nurse Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537440/research-assistant-iii-in-the-division-of-neurology": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Neurology",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Neurology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537440 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Nephrology, Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537440) Our team focuses on studying the genotype-phenotype correlation in various monogenic kidney diseases including Autosomal Dominant Polycystic Kidney Disease and Alport Syndrome. We investigate the clinical utility of genetic testing in nephrology (including diagnosis, prognosis, precision therapy and transplant optimization). We also investigate the applicability of polygenic risk score in ethnically Chinese patients with kidney disease. We now invite applications for the captioned post, Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will work with a multidisciplinary team including health care professionals and statisticians. Scope of duties include (but not limited to): Recruitment of and liaison with patients regarding research projects and clinical trials Administration of questionnaires Data collection, entry, organization and analysis Preparation of reports, presentation files and manuscripts Training opportunities relating to medical statistics, genetic testing and interpretation, techniques etc. will be provided where necessary. Perform other duties as assigned Requirements A bachelor’s degree in Health Sciences, Medical Statistics or a related discipline A good command of English and Chinese (Candidates who are proficient in Cantonese would be given priority in consideration) A strong sense of responsibility, good interpersonal, organisational and communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively as a team Prior experience in health sciences research would be strongly preferred Applicants with lower qualifications may be considered for the rank of Research Assistant II What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 28, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537440 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537440 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
