    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537472/associate-professor-research": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Research)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Associate Professor (Research) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537472 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Associate Professor (Research) in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) (Ref.: 537472), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. The University of Hong Kong has a highly ranked engineering school and active electrical and computer engineering programmes. The ECE Department offers B.Eng., M.Sc., M.Phil. and Ph.D. programmes. Information about the Department can be obtained at http://www.ece.hku.hk/. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Electrical and Computer Engineering or a closely related field, with a strong commitment to research and teaching. A solid track record in research is essential, preferably in neuroscience and biomedical applications utilizing novel optical tools. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will be entitled to a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for these positions. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload the following documents: (i) a cover letter, (ii) an up-to-date C.V. (including a full list of publications), (iii) a teaching statement (maximum 2 pages), (iv) a research statement (maximum 2 pages) outlining current and future research plans, and (v) the contact information of at least three referees. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537472 Associate Professor (Research) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537472 Associate Professor (Research) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537478/postdoctoral-fellow-research-assistant-professor-in-the-department-of-social-work-and-social-administration-multiple-posts": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (multiple posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (multiple posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537478 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-Doctoral Fellow / Research Assistant Professor (multiple posts) in the Department of Social Work and Social Administratio n (Ref.: 537478), to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary to two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Candidates should possess a PhD or equivalent in Social Work, Social Sciences, Business, or a related field, and have at least two year’s post-qualification experience. They should also have competency in qualitative and quantitative data analysis; strong proficiency in written and spoken English and Cantonese. Knowledge and experience in conducting research in social welfare and private sectors are highly preferred.  Those with substantial and relevant experience in research project management and strong track record of publications may be considered for the appointment of Research Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in examining how partnerships between NGOs, the corporate sector, and government agencies facilitate workplace inclusion for marginalised populations (e.g., individuals with disabilities or special needs). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for these positions. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload the following documents: (i) a cover letter, (ii) an up-to-date curriculum vitae (including a full list of publications), and (iii) the contact information of at least three referees. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 30 November 2026, or the positions are filled. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537478 Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (multiple posts) Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537478 Postdoctoral Fellow / Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (multiple posts) Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537510/coordinator-communication-and-public-engagement-at-the-rank-of-technical-officer-research-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Communication and Public Engagement (at the rank of Technical Officer/ Research Assistant I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Coordinator, Communication and Public Engagement (at the rank of Technical Officer/ Research Assistant I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537510 Work type: Full-time Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Coordinator, Communication and Public Engagement (at the rank of Technical Officer/ Research Assistant I/II) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 537510) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies.  HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who pursue career advancement and success.  We are seeking a high calibre candidate to join our Communication and Public Engagement Unit. Main Responsibilities: Support the team in implementing corporate branding and recruitment plans; Provide logistical support for corporate events, recruitment campaigns and public education activities; Design promotional materials, such as publications, social media posts, short videos, and animations; Maintain and update digital channels including websites and social media platforms; Maintain the volunteer database, process new registrations, and handle operational tasks related to volunteer management; Handle public enquiries regarding clinical research activities and volunteer participation; Assist in sourcing quotations from external partners and service providers; Provide on-site assistance during visits for delegations and guests. Requirements : Bachelor’s degree or above, preferably in Sciences, Social Sciences, Marketing, Public Relations, or related disciplines; Proficiency in design and video-editing tools, and experience in social media management, customer service or public relations are definite advantages; Excellent communication and interpersonal skills; Detail-minded, self-motivated and independent; Strong sense of responsibility and positive service attitude; Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview.  Those who have responded to the previous advertisements (Ref.: 537254) need not re-apply. The appointment will commence as soon as possible for a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed terms basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Appointment on 2-year fixed term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 12, 2026 and continue until October 27, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 27, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537510 Coordinator, Communication and Public Engagement (at the rank of Technical Officer/ Research Assistant I/II) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Oct 27, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537510 Coordinator, Communication and Public Engagement (at the rank of Technical Officer/ Research Assistant I/II) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Oct 27, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537514/postdoctoral-fellow-in-the-department-of-social-work-and-social-administration": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537514 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as P ostdoctoral Fellow in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (Ref:.537514), to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a PhD in Mental Health, Psychology, Clinical Psychology, Social Work or other related disciplines. They should have (i) a track record of publications; (ii) excellent written and oral communication skills in both English and Chinese, including Cantonese; (iii) strong problem-solving, organisational and administrative abilities; and (iv) attend to detail, with the ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team. Prior experience in postdoctoral research, project management, coordinating and delivering and professional training within the field of mental health-related research would be an advantage. The appointee will work in the HKJC-funded project mental health project. The position offers an excellent opportunity for academic publications, building research partnerships with international researchers and local mental health service providers, and learning the implementation of amental health research project. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV with supporting documents, a cover letter stating their background, and three references for the post applied.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537514 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537514 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
