    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537441/hall-executive-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Hall Executive (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537441 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Hall Executive (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref: 537441), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal. The Role Assist with the administration and operations of a cluster of residences, responsible for general office administration. Handle inquiries and student matters in a timely manner. Coordinate residence meetings, events and service projects. Maintain inventory of office supplies, handle procurement, and ensure stock availability. Record income and expenses, process invoices and payments, and assist with various financial tasks. Offer support to student residents by addressing their inquiries and concerns. Coordinate residents’ move in, move out and room relocation. The Dean of Student Affairs holds the authority to deploy the appointee to various clusters of student residences based on operational needs during the appointment period. Qualifications and Qualities Preferably with a recognized University degree. At least Form 5 or above, with 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics; OR a min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE, including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics. With 2-3 years of relevant work experience. A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Good organizational and communication skills, with the ability to work independently. Attention to detail and a good team player. Genuine interest in student welfare and student development. Proficiency in PC applications such as MS Office Suite, knowledge of Adobe Photoshop or Canva, would be an advantage. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537441 Hall Executive (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537441 Hall Executive (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
