    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537449/student-advising-officer-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537449 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Careers and Employability of the Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref.: 537449) (to commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefit scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary). We are seeking a motivated and resourceful professional to spearhead the expansion of HKU’s employer network in the Greater Bay Area (GBA) and drive targeted career engagement initiatives that connect students with job opportunities in this rapidly growing economic region. The role is ideal for a proactive individual who is passionate about employer relations, partnership building, and event management in the Chinese Mainland. The appointee will be responsible for the below duties: Develop GBA employer network by establishing and maintaining long-term partnerships with key employer partners in the region, spanning a wide range of industries and sectors. Plan and organise a series of GBA-specific career events throughout the year, including company tours, career talks, industry seminars, experience sharing sessions, networking events, training workshops, job fairs, and on-site interviews. Coordinate and manage all event logistics such as venue booking, transportation arrangements, event equipment, and publicity. Conduct regular engagement meetings with employers to gather market intelligence, share insights on student capabilities, and identify collaboration opportunities that align with employers’ recruitment cycles and hiring needs. Drive student participation across all career events, equipping them with up-to-date information on industry developments, job opportunities, recruitment processes, workplace culture, and living conditions in the GBA. Collaborate closely with internal stakeholders to ensure the GBA initiatives complement broader career development strategies and institutional goals. Monitor and report on key performance indicators to demonstrate programme impact and support continuous improvement. Applicants should possess: A recognised university degree with at least five years of relevant work experience in employer relations, business development, career services, or talent acquisition, preferably with exposure to the GBA or Chinese Mainland market. Proven experience in building and maintaining corporate relationships, ideally with companies or organisations in the Chinese Mainland. Strong project management and event coordination skills, with a track record of delivering programmes or events from end to end. A proactive, self-motivated, and detail-oriented mindset, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and work independently in a fast-paced environment. Sound understanding of the GBA economic landscape, industry developments, and graduate employment trends in the region. An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese and Putonghua are essential). Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications; experience with CRM systems or stakeholder management tools is an advantage. Willingness to travel frequently. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 3, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 3, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537449 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 3, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537449 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 3, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537477/research-assistant-iii-in-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-of-the-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537477 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health (Ref.: 537477), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in molecular biology, biomedical science, biochemistry, virology, immunology or a related discipline. Prior experience in animal work, viral propagation, computational analysis and vaccine/drug development is considered as an advantage. Applicants with the following qualifications are highly desirable: Self-motivated, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team Proficiency in standard molecular biology techniques (molecular cloning, PCR, western blot) and tissue culture techniques, with at least two years of hands-on wet-lab experience Well-organized, with the ability to maintain accurate and detailed experimental records Excellent communication skills in both English and Chinese, with strong academic writing skills in English Those with higher academic qualifications or more extensive relevant wet-lab experience may be considered for appointment as Research Assistant I. The appointee will contribute to the development of new vaccines against emerging and re-emerging zoonotic viruses, and to gain mechanistic insights of virus-host interactions. He/She will assist ongoing projects in the lab and help with general lab managements. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Dr Jade Yao at jade2026@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start on October 8, 2026 and continue until December 24, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 24, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537477 Research Assistant I/II in Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 24, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537477 Research Assistant I/II in Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 24, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537497/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537497 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537497), to commence as soon as possible for two to three years, with the possibility of renewal and promotion subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. This position is primarily computational/dry-lab. The successful candidate will work closely with our wet-lab team to address key questions of the field. Candidates with a hybrid background (strong computational skills plus hands-on molecular/virology experience) are particularly encouraged to apply, but pure computational biologists are also welcome. Requirements Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Virology, Immunology, Microbiology, Pathogen Biology, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related discipline. They should be responsible, self-motivated, attentive to detail, and a strong command of English. The candidate must possess a strong publication record that demonstrate their capacity of using bioinformatic platforms in life science research. The candidate should be proficient in at least one programming language (e.g., R, Python, C, or C++). They should also have a strong publication record demonstrating expertise in multi-omics analysis, particularly single-cell and spatial transcriptomics. This includes the processing and interpretation of multi-omics, single-cell (e.g., scRNA-seq), and spatial datasets to investigate cellular heterogeneity, host–pathogen interactions, and immune responses. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will join a vibrant multidisciplinary team focusing on emerging infectious diseases. He/She will be working on studies focusing on virus-host interaction, pathogenic determinants, and/or virus evolution. He/She will be expected to independently lead research projects in the aforementioned areas, write manuscripts, assist in grant applications, and co-supervise junior researchers and graduate students. Recent representative works of the group include Nat Commun, 2025, PMID:41381428; Nat Commun, 2025, PMID: 40670362; PNAS, 2025, PMID: 40402245; Nat Commun, 2024, PMID: 39379369; Sci Adv, 2023, PMID: 36662861; Nature, 2022, PMID: 35062016; Nature, 2022, PMID: 35922005. For enquiries about the duties of the post, please contact Prof. Hin Chu (https://hkumicro.hku.hk/university-staff/dr-chu-hin/) at hinchu@hku.hk . What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications. Applicants should apply online and upload: An up-to-date CV; Two reference letters from academic supervisors (preferably including one from the Ph.D. supervisor); and Relevant supporting documents (academic transcripts, publication list, research experience, and representative outputs). Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 31, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 25, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537497 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Mar 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537497 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Mar 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537427/postdoctoral-fellow-in-photonics-in-the-department-of-physics": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in Photonics in the Department of Physics",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in Photonics in the Department of Physics The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537427 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Physics (25600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Three positions are available as Post-doctoral Fellows in Photonics in the Department of Physics (Ref.: 537427) , to commence as soon as possible for 12 months, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Physics, or relevant areas. Those with experience in optoelectronic devices, topological photonics, non-Hermtian physics are welcome to apply. The appointees will work with Prof. Shuang Zhang to pursue research in active photonic devices.  Prof. Zhang’s research interests cover a wide range of topics in photonics, including, but not limited to, topological metamaterials, metasurfaces, non-linear optics, etc.  The current publications of Prof. Zhang group’s can be found at: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=sepjZ3sAAAAJ&hl=en A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V., a cover letter and a list of publications.  They should also arrange 2 referees to send reference letters to Prof. Zhang by e-mail (shuzhang@hku.hk) directly.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until March 18, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 24, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 18, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537427 Post-doctoral Fellow in Photonics in the Department of Physics Department of Physics (25600) Mar 18, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537427 Post-doctoral Fellow in Photonics in the Department of Physics Department of Physics (25600) Mar 18, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
