      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Project Officer/Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537453 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Project Officer/ Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/ II) in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537453) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a good university degree, preferably in Communications, Public Relations, Business Administration, or Marketing Research, with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience; OR 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience; OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience. They should have a good command of written and spoken Chinese and English; excellent communication, interpersonal and organisational skills; IT proficiency in MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and database management; and be detail-oriented, independent and self-motivated. Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for the position as Project Officer. The appointee will provide clerical, administrative and logistics support for event and database management, marketing communications and/or office administration. He/She may also perform other duties in support of the Faculty's mission, core values and goals. Work outside office hours and on weekends may be required occasionally. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 8, 2026 and continue until October 23, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 24, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537453 Senior Project Officer/Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 23, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537453 Senior Project Officer/Project Officer (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 23, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
