    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537467/executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537467 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537467) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a good Bachelor’s degree, with at least 5 years’ solid administrative work experience. A good understanding of the education sector is preferred. Applicants should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; strong communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; as well as an appropriate level of IT skills. They are also expected to have experience in managing a small team, the ability to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently to meet strict deadlines with minimal supervision, and a good sense of tact in dealing with sensitive and confidential issues, including discreet handling of personal and confidential files. The appointee will perform a wide range of duties including managing different processes, liaising with both internal and external stakeholders for resources acquisition, and IT procurement. Other duties include execution of strategic projects, team administration, and preparation of reports and presentation. He/She shall directly report to the Faculty Information Officer. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536675) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 23, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 24, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537467 Executive Officer Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 23, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537467 Executive Officer Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Oct 23, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537469/executive-assistant": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Executive Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537469 Work type: Full-time Department: Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Executive Assistant in the Social Sciences Research Centre (SSRC) (Ref.:537469) within the Faculty of Social Sciences. The appointment is on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. The Social Sciences Research Centre is looking for a highly organised, proactive and responsible Executive Assistant to support the planning, coordination and delivery of training programmes, seminars, workshops, conferences and other Centre activities. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will provide administrative and operational support to the Centre, with a primary focus on training and event organisation. Major duties include: Work on the planning, coordination and implementation of training programmes, workshops, seminars, conferences, public lectures, study tours and other SSRC activities; liaising with internal units, external partners, speakers, participants, vendors and service providers; handling event logistics, including venue booking, scheduling, registration, invitation, hospitality arrangements, on-site support and post-event follow-up; preparing event materials, publicity content, programme rundowns, briefing notes, reports, summaries and other documentation; operating and maintaining the Centre’s social media platforms, including Xiaohongshu (RedNote), WeChat and Instagram; supporting participant communication, enrolment management, attendance records, feedback collection and basic data compilation; assisting in procurement, quotation collection, payment processing, reimbursement and other financial/administrative procedures related to Centre activities; providing general secretarial and administrative support to the Centre; and performing other duties as assigned. Requirements Applicants should possess: a Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Social Sciences, Education, Communication, Hospitality, Public Administration, Business Administration, Marketing, or a related discipline at least 1 year of relevant work experience, preferably in administration, training, event management, programme coordination, executive education, public engagement or project support; an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, with fluency in Cantonese and Putonghua; strong organisational, communication, interpersonal and problem-solving skills; the ability to manage multiple tasks, work under tight timelines and provide reliable on-site support for events; proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and common online communication/event management tools; experience in organising academic, professional training, executive education, public engagement, conferences, seminars or study tour activities would be an advantage; knowledge of design tools such as Canva and generative AI image tools, and experience in managing social media platforms, would be an advantage; a strong sense of responsibility, attention to detail, service orientation and willingness to work as part of a team; and maturity, self-motivation and the ability to work independently with people from diverse backgrounds. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 26, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates may be invited to attend a written test and an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 24, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537469 Executive Assistant Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Oct 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537469 Executive Assistant Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Oct 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537385/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Administrative Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537385 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Family Medicine and Primary Care, School of Clinical Medicine (22500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applicants are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant II in the Department of Family Medicine and Primary Care, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537385) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree with at least 6 years’ senior administrative experience, including a minimum of 3 years’ experience supervising a large administrative team, preferably in a tertiary institution.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; strong communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; the ability to work independently and under pressure to meet tight deadlines; and a good level of IT proficiency.  They should also be a good team leader with the ability to multitask and maintain close attention to detail. The appointee will oversee the operation of the Department's general office and be responsible for a wide range of administrative functions relating to the Department’s human resources and finance matters, academic programmes, event organization, report writing, student affairs and team supervision; and perform any other duties as assigned.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 9, 2026 and continue until October 23, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537385 Administrative Assistant II Department of Family Medicine and Primary Care, School of Clinical Medicine (22500) Oct 23, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537385 Administrative Assistant II Department of Family Medicine and Primary Care, School of Clinical Medicine (22500) Oct 23, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
