    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537395/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537395 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537395)  (to commence as soon as possible for three years, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Postdoctoral Fellowship in Nutritional Epidemiology We are seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Fellow to join our research team in nutritional epidemiology, with a focus on dietary patterns, lifestyle monitoring, and health outcomes in large populations. Applicants must hold a doctoral degree (Ph.D.) in Nutritional Epidemiology or a related field, with substantial experience in dietary analysis, epidemiologic study design, big data handling, and dietary pattern deduction. They must demonstrate proven expertise in nutritional epidemiology, particularly in linking dietary pattern identification to health outcomes, and preference will be given to those with specialized experience in diet and health research in large population cohorts. The appointee is expected to demonstrate both independent research capabilities and effective team collaboration, manage ongoing research projects on lifestyle monitoring and intervention, publish original research articles in high-impact journals, assist PIs in writing external competitive grants, and develop their own SEED funding applications. This position offers excellent mentorship and access to large-scale cohort data in a collaborative research environment. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536197) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V., with the contact information of at least 2 referees.  Review of applications will start from October 15, 2026 and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537395 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537395 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537387/clerk-iii-several-posts": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerk I/II (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537387 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, School of Clinical Medicine (21000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerk I/II (several posts) in the Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537387) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Higher Diploma or above, with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience; OR 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics, OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience.  They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua), strong computer literacy, as well as excellent communication, interpersonal and organizational skills.  They should also be self-motivated, a good team player, attentive to details and able to multitask, and work independently to meet tight deadlines.  Solid work experience in tertiary institutions or in the education sector would be an advantage.  Those with lower qualifications or less experience will be considered for appointment as Clerk II. The appointees will provide administrative and clerical support for undergraduate and postgraduate degree programmes.  They will assist in finance, HR and research management, events coordination including trainings, workshops, seminars and conferences, and perform other duties as assigned.  Working outside normal office hours and on weekends may be required.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited for a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 4, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537387 Clerk I/II (several posts) Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, School of Clinical Medicine (21000) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537387 Clerk I/II (several posts) Department of Orthopaedics and Traumatology, School of Clinical Medicine (21000) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
