    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537403/senior-executive-assistant-executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii-office-administration-team": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant /Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II), Office Administration Team",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior Executive Assistant /Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II), Office Administration Team The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537403 Work type: Full-time Department: Information Technology Services (40000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant /Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II), Office Administration Team, CIO and Librarian Office, Information Technology Services (Ref.: 537403) Information Technology Services (ITS) provides central IT services that support the University’s teaching, learning, research and administration. As ITS continues to transform and adopt new technologies, we are strengthening our administrative support to enhance service delivery and operational excellence. Further information about ITS is available at https://www.its.hku.hk/ . We are seeking an experienced, proactive and tech-savvy administrator to join the Office Administration Team and provide high-quality support for ITS. The appointee will work with colleagues at all levels, use digital and AI-assisted tools to streamline daily operations, and strengthen collaboration across the CIO and Librarian Office. With exposure to human resources, finance, procurement, facilities and event management, this role offers a valuable opportunity to develop as a well-rounded administrator within a supportive team. The Role Handle HR administration, including recruitment, appointments, contract matters, training coordination and general staff-related support; Support procurement and finance work, including purchase orders, payments, reimbursements, budget monitoring, documentation and reporting; Coordinate administrative and logistical support for facilities, departmental events and office activities; Use digital and AI-assisted tools to prepare reports, analyse data and streamline routine workflows; Collaborate with the Library Administration Team to support events and other day-to-day administrative work; and Perform other duties as assigned. *Work outside normal office hours may be required for duty-related events. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years of relevant full-time work experience; A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; Strong communication, organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work effectively with diverse stakeholders; Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel and PowerPoint; Practical experience in using AI tools, such as Microsoft Copilot or similar applications, for drafting, data analysis or workflow improvement, and an openness to adopting new technologies; Self-motivated, detail-oriented and responsible, with good time management skills and the ability to handle multiple tasks independently; and Knowledge of advanced digital tools, such as Power Platform, Visio, Photoshop or Adobe Illustrator, and experience in the tertiary education sector would be advantages. Candidates with less experience but strong potential may be considered for appointment as Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II). What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, and commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537403 Senior Executive Assistant /Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II), Office Administration Team Information Technology Services (40000) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537403 Senior Executive Assistant /Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk I/II), Office Administration Team Information Technology Services (40000) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537405/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537405 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-Doctoral Fellow in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537405), to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Doctoral degree in statistics, biostatistics, computer science, psychiatry, psychology or a related discipline. They should be familiar with programming languages such as R or Python and have a good command of written and spoken English. Those with expertise in MRI imaging analysis and neuroscience in clinical population, especially in psychiatry research will be preferred. The appointee will work on multiple projects on psychiatry research particularly focusing on MRI imaging and neuroscience. The appointee will work in a flexible environment, and have a chance to collaborate with health science, computer science and neuroscience experts.  For further enquiries about the duties of the post and/or the project, please contact Prof. Sherry Chan (kwsherry@hku.hk) A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start on October 02, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 17, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537405 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537405 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
