    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537322/senior-research-assistant-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-project-assistant": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Senior Project Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Senior Project Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537322 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Senior Project Assistant) in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537322) (to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary basis or two-year fixed term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Nursing, Public Health, Social Work or other healthcare-related disciplines, with at least 2 years’ of post-qualification work experience. They should have an excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese (including fluency in Cantonese).  They should also demonstrate strong skills in statistical analysis, data management, and project coordination, with good leadership, excellent organizational, interpersonally and communication skills, and the ability to collaborate closely with a multidisciplinary team and external parties, including project funder, academic and research staff members, community stakeholders, social service groups, and other supporting teams. Experience in working with non-governmental organisations (NGOs), or working with individuals with disabilities, is highly preferred. The appointee will work for the “Jockey Club Health Programme for Adult Persons with Disabilities” under the supervision of Professor Kelvin Wang. He/she will assist in coordinating research projects, designing and implementing research activities, analysing data, preparing scientific reports, supervising junior research-support staff, liaising with community partners and institutions, general administration, and perform other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537322 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Senior Project Assistant) School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537322 Senior Research Assistant (holding the functional title of Senior Project Assistant) School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
