    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537221/assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537221 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Department of Mechanical Engineering (Ref.: 537221) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year/three-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree, with at least 4 years’ work experience, preferably in staffing/finance administration. They should have a strong command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua and Cantonese), along with high levels of communication, organizational, time management and problem-solving skills, as well as a good level of IT knowledge and the ability to work independently.  They should also be good team players and fast learners with the ability to handle multi-tasks under tight deadlines. Attention to detail, accuracy in their work, and leadership ability are also expected. The appointee will provide executive support and coordination for the Department’s staffing and finance administration, and manage a range of related responsibilities. He/She will be responsible for handling staffing and human resources matters, including recruitment, appointments, personnel reviews, and leave administration. The role also involves overseeing the financial operations, including purchase requisitions, procurement, payroll, staff claims, and resource management. In addition, the appointee will coordinate the preparation of various reports and provide secretarial support to committees, and coordinate academic and delegation visits for the Department as required. He/She will be required to supervise clerical staff to ensure the delivery of quality services, and to perform ad-hoc anad non-routine tasks as assigned. Occasional work outside normal office hours may be required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536991) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 30, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537221 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537221 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) Department of Mechanical Engineering (14500) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
