    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537375/postdoctoral-fellow-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-the-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537375 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health (Ref.: 537375), to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year or two-year temporary term contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should have a Ph.D. degree in biological/medical sciences or related disciplines, with research experience in virology, microbiology and/or immunology. Strong communication skills and a good command of spoken and written English are essential. Applicants should be organised, attentive to details, responsible, self-motivated, and able to work independently and collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team. Prior experience in conducting flow cytometry, together with experience in measuring neutralising antibody responses following infection or vaccination, would be an advantage. The appointee will deliver collaborative projects on immunological responses triggered by vaccination and viral infection. He/she will support the management and oversight of the research activities and assist in the supervision of junior research staff. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Miss Ingrid Lam at ilht@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537375 Post-doctoral Fellow in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537375 Post-doctoral Fellow in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
