    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537392/research-assistant-professor-postdoctoral-fellow-in-the-faculty-of-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537392 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences We now invite applications for the captioned post, who will involve in the Jockey Club End-of-Life Community Care Project ( www.JCECC.hk ). Duties and Responsibilities Involve in the research team of the Project to work on research and evaluation studies in end-of-life care (EoLC). Duties and responsibilities include: Supervise a team of research staff on research and evaluation tasks in EoLC Perform advanced level of data analysis (quantitative and qualitative) Advance knowledge based on the data and disseminate it through peer-review journals, press conference or other means Draft reports and presentations relevant to the project Liaise with project collaborators and partners Mentor junior research staff Support and perform other duties as assigned Requirements Ph.D. degree in Social Work, Gerontology, Nursing, Counseling, Public Health, Psychology, Behavioral Health, Mental Health or a related discipline, preferably with clinical experiences in EoLC or gerontology care Good command of written and spoken Chinese (Cantonese) and English Ability to multi-task and work on a tight schedule to meet project deadlines Ability to work well independently and collaboratively as a team Ability to develop a body of high-quality publications in scholarly journals with global impact Proficiency in statistical software packages, including SPSS and R, for large and complex data analysis Proven knowledge and experience in undertaking research related to EoLC is advantageous Relevant post-doctoral work experience and an excellent track record of publications will be advantages Applicants with less experience or qualifications may be considered for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow What We Offer The appointment will commence from as soon as possible on temporary basis until June 30, 2027. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online, upload a covering letter and an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537392 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537392 Research Assistant Professor / Post-doctoral Fellow in the Faculty of Social Sciences Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537258/tenuretrack-assistant-professor-in-the-department-of-psychiatry-and-school-of-biomedical-sciences": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry and School of Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry and School of Biomedical Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537258 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for joint appointment as Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine and the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537258), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract. We are seeking scholars whose work advance the understanding of the biological mechanisms underlying mental disorders and neuropsychiatric diseases. We welcome applicants from psychiatry and related fields, in particular genomics, epigenetics, neurobiology, biostatistics and big data analytics. Applicants who adopt multidisciplinary approaches to address key challenges in psychiatry and neuroscience, and with research of high translational potential are particularly encouraged to apply. Applicants should possess: (i) a Ph.D. degree or equivalent in a related discipline; (ii) evidence of international recognition and a strong record of scholarship with a demonstrated ability to work across disciplines towards new research initiatives; (iii) a strong commitment to engaging students at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels; and (iv) a strong track record of high-quality research as indicated by publication record and external grants. The appointee is expected to conduct independent and collaborative scholarly research, publish research articles in high-impact journals, and attract competitive grants to maintain active research programmes; take part in teaching undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, and supervise research postgraduate students; and perform administrative duties. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of the basic salary. Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. including contact details of three referees, a one-paragraph biosketch and a summary of four most significant publications highlighting specific contributions to each on a single A4 page, and statements of research and teaching interests. Review of applications will start from November 16, 2026 and continue until January 1, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 1, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537258 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry and School of Biomedical Sciences Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Jan 1, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537258 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry and School of Biomedical Sciences Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Jan 1, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537261/executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537261 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) in Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (Ref.: 537261) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Higher Diploma or an equivalent qualification, or 5 passes in HKCEE, including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, plus at least 4 years of full-time work experience, preferably in the tertiary education sector. They should have a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); good organisational, interpersonal, communication and problem-solving skills; proficiency in IT and familiarity with office applications; and ability to work independently and under pressure to meet tight deadlines. They should also have a strong sense of responsibility, attention to detail and the ability to multitask.  Immediately available is preferred. The appointee will assist in financial and administrative matters of the Department, including handling payments and processing receipts, preparing accountment statements and reimbursement claims, maintaining database for finance records, and managing office inventory. He/She will also provide support for tasks as assigned by supervisor(s) and perform other duties as assigned by the Head of the Department or his/her delegates. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537261 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537261 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (14300) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
