    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537340/research-assistant-professor-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-the-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537340 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health (Ref.: 537340), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should have a Ph.D. degree in biological/medical sciences or related disciplines, with post-doctoral research experience in virology, microbiology and/or immunology. Applicants should have substantial experience in both flow cytometry and the measurement of neutralising antibody responses following infection or vaccination. They should also have a strong quantitative and qualitative background, a proven track record of research, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team. The appointee will lead studies on immunological responses triggered by vaccination and viral infection. He/she will take a leading role in overseeing research projects and supervising junior research staff. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Miss Ingrid Lam (ilht@hku.hk). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. together with at least three reference letters. Review of applications will start from 28 September 2026 and continue until 14 December 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 14, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537340 Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 14, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537340 Research Assistant Professor in The Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI), the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Dec 14, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537350/tenuretrack-clinical-professor-clinical-associate-professor-clinical-assistant-professor-several-posts": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Clinical Professor/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537350 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign We are pleased to invite outstanding scholars to join HKUMed and contribute to our expanding research, teaching, and clinical innovation programmes through the ‘140 for 140’ Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign . This is an open-discipline call.  Recruitment areas include Anaesthesiology; Cancer Medicine; Clinical Oncology; Community Medicine; Critical Care Medicine; Diagnostic Radiology; Emergency Medicine; Family Medicine and Primary Care; Medical Oncology; Medicine; Microbiology; Obstetrics and Gynaecology; Ophthalmology; Orthopaedics and Traumatology; Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine; Pathology; Psychiatry and Surgery. The Position Applications are invited for appointments as Tenure-Track Clinical Professor/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537350), to commence as soon as possible, on a four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second four-year fixed-term contract. Exceptionally outstanding candidate for Clinical Professor may be considered for appointment on tenure terms. Clinical Professor Appointees shall be mapped to the relevant departments and take up a key role in achieving the highest standard of quality in all aspects of its teaching, research and clinical programmes; fostering academic collaboration within and outside the Faculty/University; as well as pursuing new strategic directions for the further development of their respective departments. They may be assigned to discharge duties at hospital(s) and clinic(s) affiliated with HKU Health System. Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor Appointees shall be mapped to the relevant departments with a strategic role to play in growing the clinical services. They shall also focus on the education of medical students, postgraduate teaching and supervision, as well as academic research. They may be assigned to discharge duties at hospital(s) and clinic(s) affiliated with HKU Health System. Information about respective teaching departments can be obtained at https://www.med.hku.hk/en/depts/teaching . The Person Clinical Professor Applicants should possess a specialist registration with the Hong Kong Medical Council (or be eligible to apply to the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine for the Certification of Specialist Registration), and preferably other relevant higher academic qualification (e.g. MD, MS, PhD). They should have a distinguished and sustained record of high-quality impactful research, as indicated by publications and competitive grants, with demonstrated clinical excellence. They should also have achieved international recognition for scholarship and professional expertise. In addition, applicants should demonstrate a strong commitment to, and evidence of, excellence in teaching, curriculum development, capacity building, mentoring early career researchers and supervision at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Preference will be given to those with demonstrated administrative leadership in universities or healthcare settings. Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor Applicants should possess a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong, with the attainment of the status as Fellow of the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine or equivalent. They should display strong clinical acumen and skills in the relevant specialty, with demonstrated experience in teaching medical students, interns and trainees. Proven capacity to initiate and contribute to basic, clinical and/or translational research is essential. It is also advantageous to have a higher academic qualification (e.g. MD, MS, PhD). Those with less qualifications and experiences may be considered for appointment as Clinical Assistant Professor. There will be opportunities for academic growth, career development and mentorship, with protected time for educational and clinical research activities, depending on the appointees’ interests and accomplishments. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534597) need not re-apply. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointments will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. A start-up package that is commensurate with the needs and experience of the appointee will be provided. A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidates. Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online at the University's career site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ), with (a) an executive summary describing their most outstanding accomplishments and qualifications; (b) an up-to-date C.V. highlighting their best publications in recent years; and (c) a 1-page description of their future research and career plan. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 14, 2027 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 14, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537350 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Mar 14, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537350 Tenure-Track Clinical Professor/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Mar 14, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537351/clinical-professor-of-practice-clinical-associate-professor-of-practice-clinical-assistant-professor-of-practice-several-posts": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Practice/ Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clinical Professor of Practice/ Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537351 Work type: Full-time Department: Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign We are pleased to invite outstanding scholars to join HKUMed and contribute to our expanding research, teaching, and clinical innovation programmes through the ‘140 for 140’ Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign . This is an open-discipline call. Recruitment areas include Anaesthesiology; Cancer Medicine; Clinical Oncology; Community Medicine; Critical Care Medicine; Diagnostic Radiology; Emergency Medicine; Family Medicine and Primary Care; Medical Oncology; Medicine; Microbiology; Obstetrics and Gynaecology; Ophthalmology; Orthopaedics and Traumatology; Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine; Pathology; Psychiatry and Surgery. The Position Applications are invited for appointments as Non­-Tenure Track Clinical Professor of Practice/ Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) in the LKS Faculty of Medicine (Ref.: 537351), to commence as soon as possible, on a three- to four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Fractional appointments may be considered for the suitable candidates. Clinical Professor of Practice Appointees shall be mapped to the relevant departments/units and take up a key role in achieving the highest standard of quality in all aspects of its clinically driven activities. They will foster academic collaboration within and outside the Faculty/University, and pursue new strategic directions for the further development of the Faculty and/or the respective departments/units. Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice Appointees shall be mapped to the relevant departments/units with a strategic role to play in growing the clinical services. They shall also focus on the education of medical students with support to academic research. Those with less experience may be considered for appointments as Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice. There will be opportunities for academic growth, career development and mentorship, depending on the appointees’ interests and accomplishments. The Person Applicants should possess a specialist registration with the Medical Council of Hong Kong (or be eligible to apply to the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine for the Certification of Specialist Registration). They should have achieved international recognition for professional expertise, in addition to a good and sustained record of excellence in one or more of the following areas: Clinical Services Teaching and Learning Knowledge Exchange and Services Research (basic science, translational and/or clinical research) Preference will be given to those with demonstrated administrative contributions and management experience in universities or healthcare settings. Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534595) need not re-apply. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointments will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidate. Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online at the University's career site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V., and contact information of 3 referees should be provided in the application form. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 14, 2027 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 14, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537351 Clinical Professor of Practice/ Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Mar 14, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537351 Clinical Professor of Practice/ Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/ Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine (20000) Mar 14, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537360/senior-technical-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Technical Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537360 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537360) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, and with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should hold a Master’s degree or above, preferably in Microbiology, Biological Sciences, Biotechnology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related discipline, with a minimum of 5 years of practical laboratory experience in biological, microbiological, biomedical, or biosafety level 2 and 3 (BSL-2 & BSL-3) laboratories. Familiarity with core laboratory equipment, such as flow cytometry, imaging systems, and next-generation sequencing (NGS) platforms, as well as standard biological techniques and common laboratory instruments, is essential. They should possess good interpersonal and organizational skills, proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese, and a strong sense of responsibility and self-motivation. They should also be able to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team, and be eager to learn new techniques. Applicants with a strong publication record will have an advantage. The appointee will assist in conducting routine and advanced experiments, managing core equipment, and developing and implementing standard operating procedures. He/She will also be responsible for ensuring compliance with laboratory safety regulations and biosafety guidelines, and performing general administrative and ad hoc tasks as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from September 24, 2026 and continue until October 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537360 Senior Technical Officer Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537360 Senior Technical Officer Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537391/executive-officer-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-communications-executive": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Communications Executive) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537391 Work type: Full-time Department: Asia Global Institute (31120) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Communications Executive) in the Asia Global Institute (Ref: 537391) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-ended gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should have a good university degree and at least 5 years’ solid working experience in event management with strong communications and administrative skills, preferably in the higher education or public/quasi-public sectors. Additional experience in handling finances and expenses matters and an appropriate level of IT skills would be an advantage. They should have an excellent command of spoken and written English and Chinese, be self-motivated, attentive to details, able to multi-task independently and a good team player. Applicants should be flexible enough to cope with different tasks as assigned and to work outside of normal office hours occasionally. The appointee will be assisting the implementation of various kinds of events, marketing and branding initiatives. He/She will also be responsible for providing accounting and administrative support; office documentation and data verification and other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Information about the Institute can be obtained at https://www.asiaglobalinstitute.hku.hk/ . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until December 18, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 18, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537391 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Communications Executive) Asia Global Institute (31120) Dec 18, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537391 Executive Officer (holding the functional title of Senior Communications Executive) Asia Global Institute (31120) Dec 18, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
