    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537316/clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-executive-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537316 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537316) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis or one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability) The Centre of Cancer Medicine is a platform to facilitate the academic development of cancer medicine and oncology, and is created to foster collaboration among the cognate disciplines/(sub)specialities within the Centre of Cancer Medicine/ School of Clinical Medicine, and with other Schools/ Departments/ Institutes/ Hospitals/ Colleges. The Cancer Clinical Trials Unit is dedicated for the management, organization and conduction of oncology and related clinical research. Applicants should possess a recognized degree, or 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics; OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics with at least 2 years’ work experience. A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese. Excellent organizational and communication skills, strong computer literacy, and the ability to handle multiple tasks efficiently. The appointee will handle the day-to-day clerical work for the Cancer Clinical Trials Unit, Centre of Cancer Medicine. This includes general office tasks such as answering phones, handling incoming and outgoing mail, and keeping the office filing system organized and up to date. The role also involves helping with basic office chores, such as checking stationery stocks, ordering new supplies, and ensuring that the workspace and meeting rooms are tidy and ready for use. The role will also support the research team with simple document tasks and record-keeping. This includes photocopying and scanning study documents, preparing folders for patient visits, and helping data entry of study documents into an electronic data capture system. The appointee will help update simple logs and lists, such as staff contact lists or attendance records, and ensure that all documents are filed safely to protect patient privacy. Additionally, the appointee will also handle basic financial and data tasks to keep the unit running smoothly. This includes collecting and organizing receipts for research expenses, fill out reimbursement forms for travel, and performing accurate data entry into the department’s computer systems and performing any other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be required to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contact-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s career site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. and one reference letter. Review of applications will start from as soon as possible and continue until October 25, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 25, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537316 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Oct 25, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537316 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) Centre of Cancer Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22900) Oct 25, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
