    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537288/clerk-iii-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-executive-assistantexecutive-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537288 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537288) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should have 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics; or minimum Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, preferably with a recognized degree plus at least 2 years’ work experience. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; good communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; IT proficiency; the ability to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently to meet tight deadlines; and competence in performing administrative duties and collaborating with different stakeholders. They should also be attentive to details, a good team player with self-motivation and a strong sense of responsibility. Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience will be considered for the post of Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant). The appointees will provide administrative support to the financial matters of the School, including handling procurement processes such as Request for Quotation (RFQ), processing of payments, purchase orders, invoices and reimbursement claims etc. They may assist in budgetary control matters, and undertake other duties as assigned by the supervisor. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 10, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 10, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537288 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Nov 10, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537288 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Nov 10, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
