    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537338/tenuretrack-assistant-professor-in-international-governance-of-frontier-technologies-in-the-school-of-governance-and-policy": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant Professor in International Governance of Frontier Technologies in the School of Governance and Policy",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Tenure-track Assistant Professor in International Governance of Frontier Technologies in the School of Governance and Policy The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537338 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Governance and Policy (31100) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for an appointment as Tenure-track Assistant Professor in International Governance of Frontier Technologies in the School of Governance and Policy (Ref.: 537338), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract. The School of Governance and Policy (SGP) Established in 2025, SGP aspires to be the leading global hub for governance and policy scholarship and education, rooted in Hong Kong’s unique role as a bridge between China and the world, empowering leaders across Asia and beyond with strategic insight, analytical rigor, and cross-sector collaboration.  By fostering multidisciplinary knowledge, we aim to strengthen governance systems, enrich multilateral understanding, and drive transformative policy impact. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be expected to teach courses offered in postgraduate programmes related to international relations, global governance, and/or public policy.  He/She will also contribute actively to research and knowledge exchange, programme development at postgraduate level, and assume service and administrative responsibilities as appropriate. Requirements Applicants should possess Ph.D. degree in economics, public policy, politics, or a closely related field, such as JD in international or administrative law.  They should be accomplished scholars who conduct rigorous empirical research on the dynamics of governance, law, and geopolitics that shape frontier technologies globally and have teaching and research experience in one or more of the following areas: the  comparative design, governance, and implementation of AI or other frontier technologies, current and future algorithmic threats, accountability and innovation, international legal risk, and conflict resolution on global or regional disputes, among others.  They should also have a proven track record, or strong potential for research excellence, scholarly publications and securing competitive external funding. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salary tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload the following documents: (1) an up-to-date CV, (2) a research statement of no more than 2 pages, (3) a teaching statement of no more than 2 pages, (4) two samples of representative research output, and (5) the contact information of three referees.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 6, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Enquiries may be directed to the School Office at sgpinfo@hku.hk . Advertised: Sep 10, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 6, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537338 Tenure-track Assistant Professor in International Governance of Frontier Technologies in the School of Governance and Policy School of Governance and Policy (31100) Nov 6, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537338 Tenure-track Assistant Professor in International Governance of Frontier Technologies in the School of Governance and Policy School of Governance and Policy (31100) Nov 6, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537287/senior-clerkclerk-i-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-executive-assistant-in-the-division-of-public-health-laboratory-sciences-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Senior Clerk/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Clerk/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537287 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Clerk/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537287), to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a good university degree with at least 1 year of relevant work experience, preferably in the higher education sector. They should have knowledge of and experience in project management, office administration, financial management, human resource management, and external communications. Proficiency in English and Chinese (including Cantonese and Mandarin) is required. Applicants should also possess strong organizational, problem-solving, communication and interpersonal skills, and demonstrate a high level of proficiency in computer applications and document processing. They should be able to work effectively both independently and as part of a team, manage multiple tasks, and take initiative in a fast-paced environment. The appointee will provide research management and administrative support to Principal Investigators and contribute to the R&D initiative and implementation of the research team. Duties include liaising with a wide range of stakeholders and collaborators across finance, HR, PR, research, educational, corporate and government sectors; monitoring project progress and preparing reports; managing financial and HR matters; facilitating regulatory approvals; drafting and negotiating agreements; preparing patent-related documentation; coordinating events and meetings; and performing other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written assessments. Information about the School can be obtained at https://sph.hku.hk . Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Mr. Eric Yip at yiperic@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits, if applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537287 Senior Clerk/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537287 Senior Clerk/Clerk I (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
