    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537309/senior-technical-officertechnical-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537309 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer in the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine and the State Key Laboratory of Pharmaceutical Biotechnology (Ref.:537309) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis or one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Master’s degree or above in Biology, Molecular Biology, Immunology, Biochemistry or a related discipline; preferably with experience in laboratory management and knowledge of animal studies.  They should have good communication and collaboration skills; be able to work independently and meet tight schedules; pay attention to efficiency.  Those with lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Technical Officer. The appointee will coordinate an eight-year inter-institutional project on “metabolic medicine” supported by RGC “Areas of Excellence Scheme”, manage research platforms in the State Key Laboratory, and perform other duties as assigned.  5.5 working days per week is required. For more information about our research directions, please visit our lab website: https://www.sklpb.hku.hk A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536451) need not re-apply. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from September 22, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537309 Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537309 Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537314/administrative-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Administrative Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537314 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant I/II in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537314) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary for Administrative Assistant I and 10% for Administrative Assistant II, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a good university degree, preferably a Master’s degree with at least 10 years' relevant administrative, management or team leadership experience, preferably gained in a tertiary institution or public-sector organisation. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua. They should be mature, meticulous, self-motivated, and collaborative team players with strong organisational, interpersonal, and communication skills. They should also be able to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and demonstrate initiative in handling a wide range of responsibilities. A strong commitment to service excellence and team goals, together with excellent inter-personal, time-management, problem-solving, and multitasking abilities, is essential. They should also possess a professional work ethic and a high level of computer literacy. A good understanding of the business field in the higher education sector, along with the ability to build partnerships will definitely be an advantage. Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant II. The appointee will play a versatile role to support the administration and execution of the Faculty's initiatives, undertake special projects and perform any duties as assigned by the Dean or his delegate(s). Work outside office hours and on weekends may be required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 9, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537314 Administrative Assistant I/II Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537314 Administrative Assistant I/II Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537277/research-assistant-professor-in-the-division-of-rheumatology-clinical-immunology": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant Professor in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537277 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant Professor in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology in the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537277) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities Participate in research program of PID modelling using stem cell platforms conducted in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology. Supervise junior research staff and postgraduate students, and prepare reports and papers. Perform other duties as assigned. The appointee will be given an opportunity to develop their own research programme in the wider fields of PID and autoimmunity. Requirements A PhD degree with at least 5 years’ post-doctoral work experience in the area of primary immunodeficiencies (PID) and autoimmunity. What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 3-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 8, 2026 , and continue until November 8, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 8, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537277 Research Assistant Professor in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 8, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537277 Research Assistant Professor in the Division of Rheumatology & Clinical Immunology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 8, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
