    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537298/parttime-student-affairs-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Part-time Student Affairs Assistant I",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Part-time Student Affairs Assistant I The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537298 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Part-time Student Affairs Assistant I (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Careers and Employability of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (several posts) (Ref.: 537298) (to commence as soon as possible for up to 12 months, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability). Applicants should possess a Higher Diploma or Associate Degree preferably in Statistics, Mathematics, Social Sciences or related disciplines. They should be well-organised, responsible, flexible, attentive to detail, able to adapt to a fast-paced environment and work under tight deadlines. A strong numerical sense, proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, and good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) are essential. Experience in survey research support, database management, statistical software, or statistical report production would be an advantage. The appointee will support the implementation of survey research projects, including the Graduate Employment Survey and Employer Survey. He/She will assist in the survey system testing and administration, publicity and promotion activities, data collection, data verification and cleansing, report preparation, and statistics updates. The appointee will also engage in graduate employment support and outreach initiatives, communicate with recent graduates to collect and update employment information and maintain accurate records in the graduate employment database, assist with daily office operations, and perform other duties as assigned. Occasional work outside normal office hours may be required to support operational and project needs. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits, where applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until Novem ber 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 8, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537298 Part-time Student Affairs Assistant I Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537298 Part-time Student Affairs Assistant I Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
