    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537300/internal-audit-manager": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Internal Audit Manager The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537300 Work type: Full-time Department: Internal Audit Office (61000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Internal Audit Manager in the Internal Audit Office (Ref.: 537300) The Role The appointee will report to the Director of Internal Audit. Job responsibilities include: Lead the planning, execution, and supervision of assigned audits aligned with the Annual Audit Plan and other ad hoc assignments. Conduct risk-based audits in accordance with Global Internal Audit Standards, and in compliance with governing laws and regulations applicable to the University. Review findings, ensure quality audit reporting, and provide actionable recommendations to address identified risks. Monitor implementation of audit recommendations and progress reporting. Support enhancement of audit processes effectiveness and efficiency using technology, analytics and market best practices. Coach Internal Audit Officers to support team and individual’s professional growth. Qualifications and Qualities Degree holder (master’s degree holder preferred) in relevant discipline(s) 8 to 12 years’ relevant work experience in internal audit, governance, risk management and / or compliance. Experience in universities or educational institutions preferred Internal audit-related qualifications required (e.g. CIA, CISA, CFE etc.) Integrity, leadership, strong interpersonal skills, decision-making, stakeholder influence, mentoring capability, and ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Data analytics (e.g. Power BI, Tableau, ACL etc.) skills and effective command 