    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537226/research-assistant-ii-in-community-child-health-unit-in-the-department-of-paediatrics-and-adolescent-medicine-school-of-clinical-medicine": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II in Community Child Health Unit in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant II in Community Child Health Unit in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537226 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in Community Child Health Unit in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine  (Ref.: 537226 ) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should hold a Bachelor’s degree or higher in Biomedical Sciences, Biochemistry, or a related discipline. Hands-on laboratory research experience (e.g., cell culture, assay execution, sample processing) is strongly preferred. Fresh graduates with strong hands-on laboratory training are welcome. Candidates should be self-motivated team players with high integrity, strong communication skills, and a genuine passion for biomedical research. Proficiency in written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese) is required. Appointees will join large-scale biomarker cohort, molecular, and genetics projects across community child health and clinical studies. Responsibilities include conducting various lab research experiments, data collection, report drafting, maintaining protocols, and supporting daily lab operations with collaborators. Candidates with less experience may be considered for Senior Laboratory Assistant. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until Nov 30, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 3, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537226 Research Assistant II in Community Child Health Unit in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537226 Research Assistant II in Community Child Health Unit in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
