    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537278/postdoctoral-fellow-senior-research-assistant-or-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow/ Senior Research Assistant or Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Post-doctoral Fellow/ Senior Research Assistant or Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537278 Work type: Full-time Department: HKU Institute for Climate and Carbon Neutrality (47100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the HKU Institute for Climate and Carbon Neutrality (Ref.: 537278) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will collaborate closely with the supervisor and core research team to advance AI-enabled Earth observation initiatives. A primary focus will be driving the research and technical development of iEarth , an HKU-incubated Earth intelligence platform. Core responsibilities include: Conducting innovative research in remote sensing, geospatial AI, spatiotemporal data analytics, and related applications in climate and sustainability. Designing and evaluating research methodologies, AI/ML models, robust data workflows, and functional prototypes. Bridging research and application by working alongside technical teams to translate academic outputs into integrated platform features and practical demonstrations. Authoring and preparing high-impact academic papers, grant proposals, comprehensive project reports, and technical documentation. Supporting the laboratory by performing other related research duties as assigned. Requirements Candidates must possess a degree in Remote Sensing, Geographic Information Science (GIS), Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Earth System Science, or a closely related discipline. Appointment levels will be determined by the following qualifications: Post-doctoral Fellow: Requires a Ph.D. along with a proven ability to conduct independent research and generate high-quality academic outputs. Senior Research Assistant: Requires a relevant Master's degree, postgraduate qualifications, or substantial equivalent research experience. Research Assistant: Requires a relevant Bachelor’s degree. Core Competencies: Technical Proficiency: Strong programming skills with advanced proficiency in Python. Domain Expertise: Hands-on experience in remote sensing, geospatial data analysis, machine learning, or adjacent fields. Communication: Excellent written and spoken English, paired with strong interpersonal skills. Teamwork: Proven ability to collaborate effectively within a dynamic, interdisciplinary research environment. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in large-scale geospatial data processing, AI model deployment, or the development of research software and scalable platforms will be considered a strong advantage. What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post(s). Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until [30 December, 2026], or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 3, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537278 Post-doctoral Fellow/ Senior Research Assistant or Research Assistant HKU Institute for Climate and Carbon Neutrality (47100) Dec 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537278 Post-doctoral Fellow/ Senior Research Assistant or Research Assistant HKU Institute for Climate and Carbon Neutrality (47100) Dec 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537290/part-time-student-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Part Time Student Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Education 1 Part Time Student Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537290 Work type: Hourly-paid Department: Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part Time Student Research Assistant in the Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (Ref.: 537290). To commence as soon as possible until 31 August 2027. Requirements: Candidates should be undergraduate students of HKU. Candidates who study Chinese or English Language/ Literature as their major or minor subject or who are interested in STEAM education, digital literacy, learning design and analytics are preferred. Candidates should have excellent command of written Chinese and English, and preferably knowledge of the local education context. Duties: To help organize project activities like workshops, transcribe interviews, collect and analyze survey data, etc. Student helpers can complete transcription at home and return the completed transcripts to the project team via email. Period of work: from as soon as possible until August 2027. Applicants who are interested in this part time job, please visit https://shorturl.at/KEIiO and complete the tasks below: 1. Translate part 1 into English; 2. Translate part 2 into Chinese; 3. Transcribe the soundtrack into written Chinese; 4. Write down the time taken of each task. Deadline of application: Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. & the completed tasks. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Sep 3, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537290 Part Time Student Research Assistant Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537290 Part Time Student Research Assistant Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
