    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537230/student-advising-officer-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537230 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Student Engagement and Leadership of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (Ref.: 537230) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary/ Renewal of contract is subject to the availability of project funding and mutual agreement.). Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree with at least 3-5 years' relevant post-qualification experience, preferably with some experience in database and online platform management. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); strong communication, organizational and problem-solving skills, and the ability to work independently with initiative and under pressure to meet tight deadlines. They should also be a good team player with the ability to multitask, be attentive to details, and have a strong sense of responsibility. The appointee will Oversee the administration and daily operation of two Amenities Centres, including financial administration, budget control, maintenance and improvement works, contractor and support staff supervision, venue utilisation, safety and security; Liaising with student societies, student leaders, hall/college representatives, University units, and external partners on matters relating to student activities, leadership development, and student support; Planning, coordinating, implementing and evaluating student leadership development, orientation, integration, cultural exchange, and campus-wide engagement programmes that promote students' holistic development and enrich campus life. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 2, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537230 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537230 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
