    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537212/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Administrative Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537212 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant II in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537212), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary basis or two- to three-year fixed-term basis, with possibilities to renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Applicants should have a Bachelor’s degree with at least 7 years’ relevant work experience in tertiary education institutions, including at least 3 years supervisory role. They should have outstanding administration and management skills, particularly in the areas of human resources and finance; excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese (including fluency in Cantonese); good organizational, interpersonal and problem-solving skills; and the ability to multi-task and work independently to meet strict deadlines. They should also be attentive to details, and self-motivated with strong sense of responsibility. The appointee will work for the “Jockey Club Health Programme for Adult Persons with Disabilities” under the supervision of Professor Kelvin Wang. He/She will work closely with various parties, including the funder, NGOs, internal and external stakeholders, and other teams to administer the Project. He/She will be responsible for overseeing a wide range of administrative functions including human resources, financial matters, project planning and management, secretarial work, supervising junior administrative staff; and performing other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Aug 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537212 Administrative Assistant II School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537212 Administrative Assistant II School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537227/administrative-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Professional & Management 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Administrative Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537227 Work type: Full-time Department: Curriculum Development and Quality Assurance Section of the Registry (60391) Categories: Professional & Management, Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Administrative Assistant I/II in the Curriculum Development and Quality Assurance Section of the Registry (Ref: 537227) We are looking for an Administrative Assistant I/II to join the Curriculum Development and Quality Assurance Section of the Registry. The Role The appointee will provide administrative support to curriculum development, and quality assurance and quality enhancement processes in teaching and learning, in addition to performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess a good Bachelor’s degree and at least 6 years’ administrative experience at supervisory or management level, preferably in the tertiary education sector. They should be able to work independently and demonstrate sound judgment and initiative.  An excellent command of both English and Chinese, as well as a high level of communication, interpersonal and organisational skills, is essential.  Relevant experience in higher education administration, particularly in taught programme administration, is highly desirable.  Experience in servicing committees and working groups, as well as in grants administration, would be an added advantage.  Strong computer skills and artificial intelligence literacy are definite assets. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a full-time fixed-term contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary or 10% of basic salary for Administrative Assistant II. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant II. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( http://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will commence from September 7, 2026 and continue until the post is filled.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536518) need not re-apply. Advertised: Aug 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537227 Administrative Assistant I/II Curriculum Development and Quality Assurance Section of the Registry (60391) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537227 Administrative Assistant I/II Curriculum Development and Quality Assurance Section of the Registry (60391) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
