    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537252/lecturer-senior-lecturer": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537252 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Materials and Energy (14900) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applicants are invited for appointment as Lecturer / Senior Lecturer in the Department of Materials and Energy (Ref.: 537252), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. We are looking for a highly motivated individual to support the newly established Department of Materials and Energy, under the Faculty of Engineering, as a University initiative to foster dynamic and cross‑disciplinary activities. The overarching aim of the Department is to foster closed-loop interdisciplinary collaboration in materials science and engineering, with a strategic emphasis on energy materials and energy engineering. We welcome candidates from the following areas of Materials or Energy Engineering: Advanced Manufacturing Materials Characterization Kinetics and Thermodynamics of Materials Materials Chemistry Nanomaterials and Nanotechnology Energy Materials Computational Materials AI for Materials Structural Materials Applicants should possess a PhD degree in Materials, Energy Engineering, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related engineering discipline, together with relevant tertiary-level teaching experience and a demonstrated track record in knowledge exchange, curriculum development, pedagogy and academic administration. The appointee will be responsible for delivering high-quality teaching and learning at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Key duties will include: Delivering high-quality teaching and contributing to course design for undergraduate and postgraduate modules; Supervising student capstone projects and other project-based learning activities; Providing academic advising and pastoral support to students; Leading and supporting curriculum development and actively engaging in knowledge exchange activities; Contributing to student recruitment, admissions and outreach events, and liaising with internal and external stakeholders to promote the Department; and Serving on departmental committees and undertaking other administrative duties as required. Applicants with more than five years of outstanding tertiary-level teaching experience (or equivalent professional experience) and a strong record of pedagogical excellence and leadership in curriculum design may be considered for appointment as Senior Lecturer. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Aug 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537252 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer Department of Materials and Energy (14900) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537252 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer Department of Materials and Energy (14900) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
