    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537157/assistant-registraradministrative-assistant-i-two-positions": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (two positions)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (two positions) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537157 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (two positions) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537157), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a good bachelor’s degree and have at least 10 years of relevant full-time administrative experience, preferably gained in a tertiary institution or public-sector organisation. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua. They will be mature, meticulous, self-motivated, and collaborative team players with strong organisational, interpersonal, and communication skills. They should be able to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and demonstrate initiative in handling a wide range of administrative responsibilities. A strong commitment to service excellence and results, together with excellent inter-personal, time-management, problem-solving, and multitasking abilities, is essential. They should also possess a professional work ethic and a high level of computer literacy. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant I. The appointees will lead a team of professional staff in providing comprehensive administrative support to the six Academic Areas under the unitary Faculty structure. Working closely with the Area Heads, they will oversee the day-to-day operations of the Academic Areas, encompassing human resources, financial administration, academic programme management (including the coordination of teaching and learning activities), research support, event and visiting scholar coordination, and general office administration. Key responsibilities include supervising and mentoring professional staff, ensuring effective service delivery, resolving operational issues, and maintaining efficient office processes and logistics. The roles require proactive and adaptable individuals with strong organisational, communication, and leadership skills, as well as the ability to think strategically and manage multiple priorities in a dynamic academic environment. Appointees will also perform other duties as assigned by the Dean in support of the Faculty’s mission and objectives. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Housing benefits will be provided for the Assistant Registrar rank. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the posts are filled. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Aug 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy 