    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537165/senior-technical-officer-technical-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537165 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Innovation (14800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer in the School of Innovation (Ref.:537165) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal). Applicants for the Senior Technical Officer position should possess a relevant higher diploma or bachelor’s degree, preferably with at least three years of relevant work experience. They should have extensive technical experience in at least two of the following areas: robotics; electronics; embedded systems programming in C or Python; and 3D modeling software, such as Fusion 360. Strong hands-on experience in developing rapid mechatronic prototypes is essential. Applicants should also have experience in operating and maintaining prototyping tools, including 3D printers, laser cutters, and basic electronic equipment. They should be self-motivated, able to work independently, and have a good command of written and spoken Chinese and English.  Candidates with less experience may be considered for appointment as Technical Officer.  Fresh graduates may also be considered. The appointee will be responsible for maintaining the School’s prototyping workshop; supporting teaching, research, and prototyping activities for project-based courses; conducting workshops; assisting students in developing innovative projects; and providing technical support for the School’s daily operations. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or a written test. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. together with a portfolio of previous creations or projects, if available. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Aug 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537165 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer School of Innovation (14800) Oct 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537165 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer School of Innovation (14800) Oct 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
