    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537112/professor-and-head-of-department-of-politics-and-public-administration": {
      "title": "Professor and Head of Department of Politics and Public Administration",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Professor and Head of Department of Politics and Public Administration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537112 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Professor and Head of Department of Politics and Public Administration Applications are invited for appointment as Professor and Head of the Department of Politics and Public Administration, Faculty of Social Sciences at The University of Hong Kong (Ref.: 537112).  We are seeking a distinguished scholar with the stature of a Full Professor at a research-intensive institution, a strong record of academic leadership, and a solid commitment to research, teaching, and community engagement to lead our world-class department. Candidates should hold a PhD in Political Science or related discipline. The appointment as Professor will be made on tenure terms, while the appointment as Head of Department will be for an initial three-year term, renewable subject to mutual agreement. Department of Politics and Public Administration The Department of Politics and Public Administration has played a leading role in the University and its global disciplines since its establishment in 1970. In addition to a competitive PhD research degree programme, the Department offers three highly successful taught postgraduate programmes – Master of Public Administration (MPA), Master in International and Public Affairs (MIPA), and Doctor of Public Administration (DPA) – as well as thriving undergraduate programmes. The Department’s faculty members are research active, diverse, international and highly collegial. Many have received training and work experience in the most prestigious departments and universities in North America, Europe and across Asia. Their expertise spans the fields of Comparative Politics, International Relations, Political Theory, and Public Administration. For more information about the Department, visit https://ppa.hku.hk/ . Position Description The Department is looking for a visionary leader who will be responsible for both strategic and operational leadership within the Department, and contribute a significant voice in the leadership structure of the Faculty.  Through effective leadership and coordination, he/she will champion the activities of the Department and will seek to align them with the Faculty’s strategic research areas.  We seek a scholar of the highest academic credentials who has a commitment to helping build a community of scholars.  The area of research expertise is open, but the appointee should have the experience and capability required to lead the Department.  The appointee will lead strategic planning within the Department to deliver positive outcomes across our research and teaching programmes.  He/She will bring energy, experience in leadership and administration, and strong interpersonal skills to the role. Compensation and Benefits A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  The University will contribute up to 15% of basis salary into the retirement benefits scheme.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. Application The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload (1) an up-to-date C.V. with contact information of three referees, (2) a cover letter, (3) a research plan, (4) a statement on teaching philosophy, and (5) an outline of the vision and mission as Head of Department.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Aug 18, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537112 Professor and Head of Department of Politics and Public Administration Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537112 Professor and Head of Department of Politics and Public Administration Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
