      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Research Assistant I/II (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537086 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Chemistry (25200) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II (several posts) in the Department of Chemistry (Ref.:537086) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a B.Sc. or M.Sc. degree in Chemistry or other relevant disciplines.  Preference will be given to those with a strong background and research experience in organic synthesis, particularly in the synthesis of photoactive and/or biologically active compounds.  They should be responsible and able to work independently as well as in a team.  They should also have good analytical skills and a good command of English and Chinese.  The appointees will work on projects on the synthesis of photo- or bioactive compound precursors.  The appointees will work under the supervision of Professor C. M. Che. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 (extended to January 31, 2027) , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Aug 6, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you