    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537064/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Administrative Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537064 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Administrative Assistant II in the Strategy and Operations of Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref.: 537064), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal. We are seeking a proactive, innovative, and results-driven candidate to join CEDARS. The appointee will play a key role in driving student development initiatives, leading signature university events, and building high-impact partnerships across internal and external stakeholders. Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership & Event Management : Lead and empower a small administrative team to design, execute, and evaluate a diverse portfolio of strategic initiatives and signature CEDARS events. Programme & Collaboration Development : Conceptualize, launch, and manage new student engagement programmes and cross-sector collaborations from initial ideation through to implementation. Stakeholder Engagement & Reporting : Prepare high-level proposals, presentations, and institutional reports; cultivate strong working relationships with students, university administrative units, external partners, vendors, and community organizations. Process Innovation : Identify opportunities to integrate new technologies, digital tools, and operational workflows to continuously enhance student support and departmental efficiency. Qualifications and Requirements Essential: Education & Experience : A recognized University degree with at least 5 years of relevant professional experience, ideally within the higher education sector, public, or quasi-public organizations, or international corporations. Language Proficiency : Excellent written and spoken command of English and Chinese. Digital Competence : High IT proficiency combined with practical AI competence and digital tool literacy. Project & Team Leadership : Proven track record in project/event management and institutional advancement; demonstrated capability to lead a small team to deliver quality outcomes under pressure. Core Skills : Exceptional communication, problem-solving, stakeholder management, and multi-tasking abilities with a proactive, innovative mindset. Desirable / Advantageous: Experience in strategic partnership development and outreach. Knowledge of or hands-on experience with database management, design/media applications, and the implementation of digital solution tools. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Aug 5, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537064 Administrative Assistant II Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537064 Administrative Assistant II Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
