    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537049/student-advising-officer-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537049 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre of Development and Resources for Students (50000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Student Advising Officer (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Centre of Development and Resources for Students (CEDARS) (Ref.:537049) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal). Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree with at least 2–5 years of relevant post-qualification administrative experience, preferably in event management, marketing, multimedia publicity, or tertiary education. Strong communication skill is essential, along with familiarity with social media platforms popular among international students. Fluency in Cantonese or Putonghua is a plus. Proficiency in publicity, digital marketing, and multimedia content creation is required. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a genuine passion for student support, cultural integration, and proactive engagement, with strong organizational and interpersonal skills. The appointee will join the International Student Support Team at CEDARS, dedicated to enhancing the experience and well-being of international students—including international and Chinese Mainland students—through comprehensive support and engagement initiatives. Key duties include but are not limited to: Student Engagement & Integration Develop and implement programmes that foster adaptation to local academic, social, and cultural environments. Organize orientation activities, cultural exchange events, and social integration programmes to build a sense of belonging. Well-being and Crisis Support Provide timely assistance and guidance to students facing challenges in adjustment, well-being or crisis. Publicity & Communication Plan and execute publicity strategies across digital and social media platforms to promote support services and events. Create engaging multimedia content tailored to diverse student communities. Revamp the website to better cater to the needs of international students, enhancing accessibility, relevance, and user experience. Leadership & Collaboration Recruit, train, and manage student ambassadors to assist in programme delivery. Collaborate with internal units and external partners to strengthen support networks for international students. Other duties Perform any other tasks as assigned to advance the objectives of the Global Student Support Team. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until September 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Aug 4, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy stateme