    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537024/senior-lecturerlecturer-in-the-school-of-future-media-several-posts": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in the School of Future Media (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in the School of Future Media (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537024 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Future Media (31200) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (several posts) in the School of Future Media (Ref.: 537024), to commence in Spring 2027 or from as soon as possible thereafter. The appointment rank will be determined according to qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. The initial appointment will be on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree or equivalent in journalism, media studies, computer science, artificial intelligence, data science or related fields of study, with a substantial track record of professional experience in the media industries. Proficient knowledge of digital media and AI applications is required. Knowledge of Asia will be a definite advantage. Priority will be given to those with experience in designing and teaching professional courses at the tertiary level. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Lecturer. The appointees will be responsible for teaching and leading curriculum design at the undergraduate and postgraduate level in one or more of the specialisations in the following areas, as well as undertaking administrative duties at the Division level. Journalism: News reporting and writing, journalistic practice, entrepreneurship, business journalism, AI applications in journalism practices; Global Creative Industries: animation and game design, immersive and interactive media, computer vision, digital humanities, museum and heritage studies, music and performing arts. Candidates who have responded to the job (Ref.: 534409) need not to re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary for Senior Lecturer and Lecturer. Housing benefits will be provided for Senior Lecturer as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should upload an up-to-date CV and teaching statement. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until February 28, 2027 , or until the position is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 31, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Feb 28, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537024 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in the School of Future Media (several posts) School of Future Media (31200) Feb 28, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537024 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in the School of Future Media (several posts) School of Future Media (31200) Feb 28, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
