intment as Certificated Dental Surgery Assistant I/II, applicants should have a Certificate of Proficiency in Dental Surgery Assisting issued by a recognised institute or equivalent, AND 5 passes in HKCEE, or min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE, with at least 5 year’s chairside assisting work experience in a dental clinic.  Those with less experience may be appointed as Certificated Dental Surgery Assistant II.  The appointees will assist the operators in the treatment of patients and teaching-related matters; facilitate patient care, administration, supplies, general cleanliness associated with clinics, and front desk patient care assisting functions; and perform other duties as assigned. For appointment as Dental Clinic Assistant (at the rank of Facilities Assistant) , applicants should have 5 passes in HKCEE, OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE, with at least 1 year’s work experience in a dental clinic including chairside assisting.  The appointees will assist the operators in the treatment of patients and teaching-related matters; facilitate patient care, administration, supplies and general cleanliness associated with clinics; and perform other duties as assigned. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536127) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits, if applicable.  The appointments on fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from August 10, 2026 and continue until October 27, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 28, 2026 