    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536969/professorassociate-professor-on-tenure-terms-or-tenuretrack-assistant-professor-in-global-iberian-empires": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Professor on tenure terms or tenure-track Assistant Professor in Global Iberian Empires",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Professor/Associate Professor on tenure terms or tenure-track Assistant Professor in Global Iberian Empires The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536969 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Humanities (05200) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Professor/Associate Professor on tenure terms or tenure-track Assistant Professor in Global Iberian Empires in the School of Humanities (History) (Ref.: 536969), to commence on August 1, 2027, or as soon as possible thereafter. Appointment as Assistant Professor will be made on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and with consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract. The Department of History at the University of Hong Kong (HKU) seeks dynamic candidates for this position, specializing in the early modern Iberian empires (1450-1800). Candidates should demonstrate a research profile that is intrinsically comparative and global in scope, highlighting connections forged by Spain and/or Portugal with the Americas, Asia, and Africa. We particularly welcome scholars working in social and cultural history, especially those whose research engages with slavery and dependency studies, women’s and gender studies, and/or indigenous studies. The successful candidate will be expected to teach broad surveys in Latin American history. Preference will be given to candidates whose current or future research also engages with maritime East Asia. HKU is consistently ranked amongst the world’s top universities: 11 th in QS World University Rankings 2026, 1 st in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026 and 33 rd in Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026. The Department of History nurtures a lively research-intensive culture in a vibrant global city. Our faculty specialize in international, transnational, and connective histories, with a particular strength in the intersections between Asia and the wider world. We offer a highly popular and expanding undergraduate Major in History and play a vital role in the Faculty of Arts, fostering interdisciplinary collaborations and innovations through conferences, workshops, and speaker series. All of the Department’s courses are taught in English. The Department is committed to advancing the careers of junior scholars and provides a range of funding to support research activities. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in History and demonstrate a strong research profile with a commitment to innovative, research-led teaching. The successful candidate will be expected to sustain world-class research output, secure competitive research funding, excel in undergraduate and postgraduate teaching (including thesis supervision), and contribute actively to departmental leadership and academic administration. HKU and the Hong Kong Research Grants Council (RGC) offer generous research funding across disciplines. For more details about the Department, visit http://www.history.hku.hk . Enquiries about the post may be directed to Professor Christine Walker, Chairperson of the Department (email: cwalker@hku.hk ). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and professional leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload a curriculum vitae, a cover letter (two pages maximum), a research statement, a writing sample, and syllabi of two courses. Applicants should also arrange three reference letters to be sent by their referees to sohappt@hku.hk . Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expressly encourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Jul 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536969 Professor/Associate Professor on tenure terms or tenure-track Assistant Professor in Global Iberian Empires School of Humanities (05200) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536969 Professor/Associate Professor on tenure terms or tenure-track Assistant Professor in Global Iberian Empires School of Humanities (05200) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536993/postdoctoral-fellow-inorganic-synthesis-several-posts": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow (Inorganic Synthesis) (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Post-doctoral Fellow (Inorganic Synthesis) (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536993 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Chemistry (25200) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointments as Post-doctoral Fellow (several posts) in the Department of Chemistry (Ref.:536993), to commence as soon as possible for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Chemistry with a strong background and demonstrated experience in inorganic synthesis, particularly in organometallic chemistry.  A strong sense of responsibility, good organizational skills, self-motivation, ability to work independently, and fluency in written and spoken English are required.  The appointees will conduct research on the synthesis of novel precious-metal complexes and their application in anticancer drug development or transition-metal catalysis under the supervision of Professor Chi-Ming Che.  Applicants with an outstanding academic record and relevant postdoctoral experience may be considered for appointment at a higher rank. Interested applicants may contact Professor Che directly at cmche@hku.hk with a C.V. and a brief description of their research background and interests.  Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Dr. Lihui Zhu at zhulihui@hku.hk. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536993 Post-doctoral Fellow (Inorganic Synthesis) (several posts) Department of Chemistry (25200) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536993 Post-doctoral Fellow (Inorganic Synthesis) (several posts) Department of Chemistry (25200) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
