    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536905/research-assistant-iii-in-the-department-of-medicine": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Medicine",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Medicine The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536905 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:536905) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will join an internationally active team of researchers working on the development studies of big data and simulation modelling in health service Assist in the application and validation methodology on electronic medical records-based cohort studies Conduct data manipulation and visualization Prepare scientific publications, grant proposals and reports Provide general administrative and operational support Perform other duties as assigned Enquiries about the duties of the post should be directed to Prof Li at sxueli@hku.hk and Ms Effie Cheung at effiec@hku.hk . Requirements A Master’s degree or above in Public Health, Epidemiology, Biostatistics, Health Economics or a related discipline A strong quantitative background; with experience in analysing statistical data using R, SAS, Stata, Python or other programming packages Demonstrated expertise in analysis of large and complex datasets A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese Excellent communication skills Able to work independently and in collaboration with a multidisciplinary team Relevant experience in big data manipulation or decision analytics, and a track record of publications would be advantageous What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start August 10, 2026 and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Jul 27, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536905 Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536905 Research Assistant I/II in the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536956/research-assistant-iii-in-the-school-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536956 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 536956) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree in Nursing, Social Sciences, Health Science, or a related discipline. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese); high proficiency in IT (e.g. MS Office and database); strong interpersonal, communication and organizational skills; and the ability to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently to meet tight deadlines. They should be attentive to details; self-motivated; responsible; able to work independently as well as in a team; and competent to perform administrative duties and collaborate with different stakeholders. The appointee will work under the research team led by Dr. Benjamin Ho. The appointee will assist in research projects relating to cancer/oncology research. He/She will assist in participant recruitment, tracking project progress, data entry, and perform other duties as assigned by the Principal Investigator. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 24, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536956 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536956 Research Assistant I/II in the School of Nursing School of Nursing (20800) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
