    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536819/tenuretrack-clinical-associate-professor-clinical-assistant-professor-several-posts": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536819 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 536819), to commence as soon as possible, on a four-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second four-year fixed-term contract, subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong and a specialist qualification in Obstetrics and Gynaecology, i.e. Fellowship of the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine (Obstetrics and Gynaecology).  Applicants should demonstrate proven capacity and potential for high-quality research, and excellence in teaching and student supervision at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels.  They must also demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, and be able to contribute to the enhancement and development of medical and health sciences courses in the Faculty.  Those with experience of having successfully developed and submitted research grants and worked effectively with major international partners and funding agencies; interacting effectively across multiple sectors; and establishing and managing studies involving colleagues from different disciplinary backgrounds may be favourably considered. The appointees will undertake teaching responsibilities, and organize and develop both undergraduate and postgraduate programmes.  They are expected to conduct high-quality scholarly research, provide clinical services and patient care at the University's teaching hospitals, and participate in services/administration at Departmental, Faculty and University levels.  They are also expected to play a key role in leading the development of academic scholarship and teaching programmes of the Department.  Information about the Department can be obtained at https://obsgyn.med.hku.hk/ . Applicants who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534424) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidate.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online, upload an up-to-date C.V. with an indication of research orientation and specialty of interest, and provide the contact information of at least 3 referees who can comment on his/her academic scholarship.  Review of applications will start from September 30, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536819 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536819 Tenure-Track Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Assistant Professor (several posts) Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, School of Clinical Medicine (20900) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536925/senior-research-assistant-several-posts-in-the-division-of-public-health-laboratory-sciences": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536925 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Senior Research Assistant (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences of the School of Public Health (Ref.: 536925) (to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary term or a two-year fixed-term contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Master’s degree with at least one year’s post qualification experience or a Ph.D. degree with a strong background in Microbiology, Immunology, Medical Laboratory Science, or a related discipline. Excellent skills and knowledge in virology and molecular biology is essential. Preference will be given to those with experience in conducting virology research using cell line in the biosafety level 2 laboratory. The appointees will work on research projects on influenza virus. They will participate in research planning and implementation, provide training and supervision to junior research staff and postgraduate students, and prepare reports. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Mr Eric Yip at yiperic@hku.hk . Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 534616) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 22, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536925 Senior Research Assistant (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences School of Public Health (22400) Oct 22, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536925 Senior Research Assistant (several posts) in the Division of Public Health Laboratory Sciences School of Public Health (22400) Oct 22, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536936/research-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536936 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 536936) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in Biological/Biomedical Sciences, Biotechnology or a related discipline. They should also have good communication skills in Cantonese, English and Mandarin. Experience in molecular diagnostics and Next Generation Sequencing library preparation would be advantageous. The appointee has to be able to troubleshoot problems found in molecular assays and NGS library preparation. The appointee will work on research projects related to viral/bacterial/fungi diagnostics and emerging infectious diseases under the supervision of Dr. Rosana Poon and Dr. Anson Lee Chung Ho. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. (preferably with an academic transcript). Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Jul 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536936 Research Assistant I Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536936 Research Assistant I Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
