    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536890/data-scientist-at-the-rank-of-assistant-research-officer-in-the-hong-kong-jockey-club-global-health-institute-hkjcghi-of-the-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Data Scientist (at the rank of Assistant Research Officer) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Data Scientist (at the rank of Assistant Research Officer) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536890 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Data Scientist (at the rank of Assistant Research Officer) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health (Ref.: 536890), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. HKU has partnered with the International Vaccine Institute (IVI) and The University of Cambridge to establish the HKJCGHI, with funding support from The Hong Kong Jockey Club Charities Trust. IVI is a non-profit international organization dedicated to vaccines and vaccination for global health. The Epidemiology, Public Health and Impact (EPIC) Unit of IVI coordinates HKJCGHI’s work streams in epidemiology, pandemic preparedness and capacity building. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Epidemiology, Biostatistics, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Public Health or a related field with a strong quantitative focus. A PhD degree in a relevant discipline would be desirable but is not required. Applicants should have 3-5 years of experience in mathematical modeling and/or statistical inference relevant to epidemiological studies of infectious diseases, with a proven track record of leading research projects and publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Applicants should have expertise in study design, as well as in the formulation and implementation of mathematical or computational models of infectious diseases. They should also have an interest in, or experience with, integrating climate change variables, sociodemographic factors, and other area-level covariates into disease modeling. Experience working with diverse datasets, including epidemiological, surveillance, demographic, and climate data, is essential. Proficiency in programming languages such as R, Python, MATLAB, or C++ for modeling and analysis is required. Familiarity with statistical methods, machine learning techniques, and tools for data visualization would be an advantage. Experience in using agentic artificial intelligence to facilitate analysis workflows is a plus, but is not required. The appointee will work closely with research scientists and the biostatistics team at IVI. IVI has an extensive global network of field sites and databases spanning 20 years of vaccine-related field studies. The appointee will be working with existing IVI EPIC databases from IVI projects and field sites, and will contribute to the design, development, and implementation of mathematical and computational models to simulate infectious disease transmission dynamics, progression, and intervention strategies, with a particular focus on the intersection of infectious diseases and climate change. The appointee will incorporate climate change variables, such as extreme weather events, temperature, precipitation, and environmental factors, into models to explore the impacts of climate variability on disease dynamics. He/She will be expected to integrate epidemiological, demographic, health systems, and climate data into modeling frameworks to inform public health policies and intervention planning. He/She will lead research projects, define objectives, manage timelines, coordinate internal and external collaborators, publish research findings in peer-reviewed journals, and present at conferences and stakeholder meetings. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Appointee on fixed-term contract will receive a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start from (2 weeks from posting) and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536890 Data Scientist (at the rank of Assistant Research Officer) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536890 Data Scientist (at the rank of Assistant Research Officer) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Global Health Institute (HKJCGHI) of the School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536804/data-scientist-data-coordinator-at-the-rank-of-senior-technical-officer-technical-officer-in-the-division-of-community-medicine-and-public-health-practice": {
      "title": "Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536804 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice in the School of Public Health (Ref.: 536804) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in data management, statistics, computer science, information systems, public health, or a related discipline; a master’s degree will be an advantage. They should have proven experience in data cleaning and quality assurance, as well as in preparing technical documentation and data reports while managing workflows in a multi-stakeholder environment. Practical expertise with data platforms and tools is highly valued, including SQL databases, Excel or Google Sheets, and data capture systems such as REDCap, ODK, SurveyCTO, or Qualtrics; familiarity with visualization/reporting tools such as Power BI or Tableau is advantageous.  Proficiency in programming or scripting languages commonly used for data processing, such as R, SAS, Stata and Python, is desirable. Knowledge of data protection principles and compliance frameworks, along with a foundational understanding of statistical methods and data analytics principles will be beneficial. Applicants should be highly organized, detail-oriented, proactive, and possesses strong problem-solving skills. Excellent communication abilities are required to convey technical information to non-technical audiences and to build trusted relationships across teams. Leadership, mentoring capabilities, and a commitment to ethical data practices are important in a fast-paced project environment. The appointee will assist the Data Manager in overseeing the end-to-end data lifecycle across multiple projects, ensuring that data collection, processing, validation, storage, and reporting meet high standard. This role is crucial in maintaining data integrity and ensuring compliance with organizational policies and regulations. Key responsibilities include: designing and refining data management workflows; monitoring data quality, running validation checks and troubleshoot discrepancies; maintaining comprehensive documentation (e.g., data dictionaries, operational procedures, instruction manuals, data capture guidelines) and establish audit trails; supporting database administration, coaching data entry and processing teams; providing training on tools and procedures; preparing operational dashboards and data summaries for various internal and external stakeholders; collaborating closely with IT or platform vendors to address technical issues, as well as with project managers, analysts, and researchers, convert data requirements into practical solutions while ensuring adherence to data protection and security standards. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Ms Cynthia Yau at cynthyau@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical/dental benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 535038) need not re-apply. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 21, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536804 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice School of Public Health (22400) Oct 21, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536804 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice School of Public Health (22400) Oct 21, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536805/assistant-registraradministrative-assistant-i-several-posts-in-the-division-of-community-medicine-and-public-health-practice": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536805 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health (Ref.: 536805), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Application should possess a good first Bachelor’s degree, with relevant academic and professional training related to the areas of duties and/or recognized professional qualifications, plus at least 8 to 10 year’s professional experience in a public/quasi-public organization or a related sector, preferably with a higher degree.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, be mature and meticulous, self-motivated, and a good team player with excellent organisational and interpersonal skills and be able to work on their own initiative.  Commitment to quality and results, excellent time management and problem-solving skills, professional work attitude and a high level of computer literacy are essential qualities for the post. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant I. The appointee will work to support a large team focused on population mental health projects and mental wellbeing in Hong Kong. He/She will play a central role in managing financial operations, and coordinating human resources activities, ensuring timely reporting, streamlining procedures, and maintaining strong stakeholder relationships. The role also involves managing procurement, budgeting, and financial reporting, handling grants and donations and collaborating with internal and external teams to support project execution. In addition to project and financial oversight, the appointee is responsible for HR administration, including recruitment, onboarding, promotions, and visa processing. The role requires mentoring junior staff, resolving operational challenges, and maintaining efficient office logistics. The position demands adaptability, strategic thinking, and strong communication skills to support the team’s mission and ensure smooth administrative operations. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Housing benefits will be provided for the Assistant Registrar rank. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 535039) need not re-apply. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until October 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jul 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536805 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice School of Public Health (22400) Oct 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536805 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice School of Public Health (22400) Oct 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
