    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536865/tenuretrack-associate-professor-assistant-professor-in-international-relations-in-the-department-of-politics-and-public-administration": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in International Relations in the Department of Politics and Public Administration",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Tenure-Track Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in International Relations in the Department of Politics and Public Administration The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536865 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in International Relations in the Department of Politics and Public Administration (Ref: 536865), to commence in August 2027 or at another mutually agreed time, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract, both subject to satisfactory performance. Exceptionally outstanding candidates at the Associate Professor level may be considered for appointment on direct tenure terms subject to the University's approval. The Department of Politics and Public Administration is an internationally oriented research-focused department that covers a broad range of fields in Political Science and Public Administration. The Department offers three highly successful taught postgraduate programmes - Master in International and Public Affairs (MIPA), Master of Public Administration (MPA) and Doctor of Public Administration (DPA) - as well as a thriving undergraduate programme. More information about the Department can be found at https://ppa.hku.hk/ . Applicants should hold a Ph.D. degree by the time of appointment and demonstrate excellence in research and teaching. The Department welcomes applications from excellent candidates who specialise in any field of International Relations and is eager to both consolidate its existing strengths and to diversify into new areas of research and teaching. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At the current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of the gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of the basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload (1) an up-to-date CV, (2) a letter of interest, (3) graduate transcripts where relevant, (4) a research statement, (5) a teaching statement, (6) teaching evaluations where available, and (7) the contact information of three referees.  Please also arrange for your referees’ letters of support to be sent directly to us at ppahr@hku.hk . We would be glad to receive these letters from Interfolio, your department administration or the referees themselves. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 Further inquiries may be made to the Head of Department, Professor Robert Thomson, rthomson@hku.hk . Advertised: Jul 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536865 Tenure-Track Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in International Relations in the Department of Politics and Public Administration Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536865 Tenure-Track Associate Professor / Assistant Professor in International Relations in the Department of Politics and Public Administration Department of Politics and Public Administration (30100) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536840/senior-research-assistant-research-assistant-iii-in-community-child-health-in-the-department-of-paediatrics-and-adolescent-medicine": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant/ Research Assistant I/II in Community Child Health in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant/ Research Assistant I/II in Community Child Health in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536840 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Senior Research Assistant/ Research Assistant I/II in Community Child Health in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine (Ref.:536840) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis or a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) The appointee(s) will work with a team of researchers on projects related to big data, large-scale population-based longitudinal studies, and electronic medical records-based cohort studies, particularly in the areas of special educational needs and mental health. The appointee(s) will conduct statistical data analysis and interpretation, prepare scientific publications, grant proposals and reports, prepare and manage IRB applications, provide general administrative and operational support, and perform other duties as assigned. Applicants should possess: (i) a Bachelor’s degree or above in Statistics, Biostatistics, Public Health, Epidemiology, Health Economics, Data Science, or related disciplines, with a strong quantitative background; (ii) experience and proficiency in statistical data analysis using R, STATA, SAS or other statistical packages; (iii) excellent written and oral communication skills; (iv) strong problem-solving, organisational and administrative abilities; and (v) attention to detail, with the ability to work independently and collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary team. Proficiency in big data manipulation, longitudinal analyses, and a track record of publications would be an advantage. On-the-job training will be provided. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. and academic transcripts. Review of applications will start on July 20, 2026 and continue until October 31, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Jul 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536840 Senior Research Assistant/ Research Assistant I/II in Community Child Health in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536840 Senior Research Assistant/ Research Assistant I/II in Community Child Health in the Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine Department of Paediatrics and Adolescent Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (21100) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
