    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536602/fulltime-research-assistant-ii-at-the-speech-language-and-reading-lab-in-the-faculty-of-education": {
      "title": "Full-time Research Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Education 1 Full-time Research Assistant II at the Speech, Language and Reading Lab in the Faculty of Education The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536602 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Education (10000) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Full-time Research Assistant II at the Speech, Language and Reading Lab in the Faculty of Education (Ref.: 536602) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) The Speech, Language and Reading Lab ( https://slrlab.edu.hku.hk/ ) at the University of Hong Kong is inviting application for a full-time Research Assistant II position. This is an exciting opportunity for highly motivated candidates who are passionate about child development, special educational needs, and advanced data analytical techniques. Our lab conducts cutting-edge interdisciplinary research at the interaction of psychology, cognitive neuroscience, AI, linguistics, and computational modeling. The appointee will contribute to impactful research that advances scientific understanding and supports children with and without special educational needs. The appointee will play an important role in ongoing research projects involving: (1) On-site psycholinguistic and cognitive assessments for children with special educational needs (SEN); (2) Cognitive-behavioral intervention and training for children with SEN; (3) Advanced quantitative analyses using statistical and computational methods. This position offers much more than a typical research assistant role. The appointee will have the opportunity to: (1) Work closely with an interdisciplinary team of educational and developmental psychologists, cognitive neuroscientists; speech-language pathologists, linguists, and computer engineers; (2) Receive hands-on systematic training in behavioral intervention, psycholinguistic assessment, acoustic analysis, and neurophysiological assessment; (3) Build research management, leadership, and communication skills through project coordination and student supervision. This role is especially suitable for candidates who are considering future postgraduate study or research careers in psychology, speech-language pathology, cognitive science, education, linguistics, cognitive neuroscience, data science, or related fields. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Psychology, Data Science, Psycholinguistics, Linguistics, Cognitive Science, Education, Speech and Language Sciences, or a related discipline. Applicants should also have: (1) Cantonese-English bilingual proficiency; (2) Experience with behavioral experiments and quantitative and/or qualitative data analysis; (3) Strong analytical, organizational, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills. Experience with Python, R, MATLAB, Praat, or related research and data-analysis tools would be a strong advantage. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, along with annual leave and medical benefits. The successful candidate will join a dynamic, supportive, and intellectually stimulating research environment at HKU, with excellent opportunities for professional growth, advanced research training, and meaningful contribution to SEN research. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online with an up-to-date C.V. and a cover letter outlining how their qualifications and experience align with the role. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 30 November 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Jun 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536602 Full-time Research Assistant II at the Speech, Language and Reading Lab in the Faculty of Education Faculty of Education (10000) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536602 Full-time Research Assistant II at the Speech, Language and Reading Lab in the Faculty of Education Faculty of Education (10000) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536261/research-assistant-professor-rap-postdoctoral-fellow-pdf-in-epidemiology-or-biostatistics-school-of-public-health-several-posts": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor (RAP)/ Post-doctoral Fellow (PDF) in Epidemiology or Biostatistics, School of Public Health (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant Professor (RAP)/ Post-doctoral Fellow (PDF) in Epidemiology or Biostatistics, School of Public Health (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536261 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant Professor (RAP)/Post-doctoral Fellow (PDF) in Epidemiology or Biostatistics , School of Public Health (several posts) (Ref.:536261), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis for RAP, or on a one- to three-year temporary basis for PDF. Applicants should possess a doctoral degree by research (Ph.D., D.Sc., Dr.P.H. or equivalent) in epidemiology, biostatistics, public health or related disciplines.  They should have a strong quantitative background; experience in analysing epidemiological data using R, STATA, SAS or other statistical packages; demonstrated expertise in the analysis of large and complex datasets; excellent written and oral communication skills; and the ability to work independently as well as in collaboration with a multidisciplinary team.  Proficiency in longitudinal analyses, multilevel modelling, data visualisation, and state-of-the-art statistical and epidemiological models would be an advantage. The appointees will be primarily responsible for applied and methodological work in epidemiological and/or statistical research, and will work with a large population-based cohort with over 46,000 participants in 20,000 households.  They will conduct power/sample size estimation; generate tables and figures for reports and presentations; write scientific publications, grant proposals and reports; and assist in general administrative, operational and other duties as assigned. The focus of one of the posts will include The World Health Organization World Mental Health Survey Initiative and the Composite International Diagnostic Interview (CIDI), which is one of the largest cross-national mental health studies in the world. Those with relevant post-doctoral work experience and an excellent publication track record may be considered for appointment as RAP, and the appointee is expected to take up a leading role to oversee the cohort team.  Enquiries about the duties of the posts should be sent to familyco@hku.hk. Information about the School can be obtained at http://sph.hku.hk . Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 533837) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  For RAP, the appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start June 25, 2026 and continue until December 9 , 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Jun 10, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 9, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536261 Research Assistant Professor (RAP)/ Post-doctoral Fellow (PDF) in Epidemiology or Biostatistics, School of Public Health (several posts) School of Public Health (22400) Dec 9, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536261 Research Assistant Professor (RAP)/ Post-doctoral Fellow (PDF) in Epidemiology or Biostatistics, School of Public Health (several posts) School of Public Health (22400) Dec 9, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
