    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536390/technical-assistant-field-data-collection-several-posts": {
      "title": "Technical Assistant (Field Data Collection) (several posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Technical Assistant (Field Data Collection) (several posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536390 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Social Sciences Research Centre (30700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for the position of Technical Assistant, carry the functional title of Interviewer (several posts) at the Social Sciences Research Centre (SSRC) within the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 536390) We now invite applications for the captioned post. Duties and Responsibilities Travel to or remain stationed at designated survey sites to conduct surveys with respondents, not limited to in-person, door-to-door or via telephone Strictly adhere to established survey protocols, sampling methodologies, and screening processes to ensure valid and unbiased data collection. Employ interviewing skills to create a safe, supportive, and non-judgmental environment for respondents sharing difficult experiences. Politely and professionally handle respondent questions, objections, or refusals while maintaining an empathetic tone. Ensure the strict confidentiality and secure handling of all respondent information and collected data. Meet daily/weekly productivity and quality assurance goals Requirements High school diploma or equivalent. Native fluency in Cantonese. Ability to listen to difficult or emotionally heavy accounts while maintaining professional boundaries and personal emotional well-being. Able to travel to and remain at designated survey sites for the duration of scheduled working shifts. Must be able to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, to accommodate the schedules of the respondents. Excellent verbal communication and interpersonal skills. Comfortable navigating deeply personal conversations with strangers. High level of accuracy in listening, following complex routing protocols, and recording information. Comfortable using mobile devices (tablets/smartphones) and basic data entry applications. Previous experience in counselling, social work, victim advocacy, healthcare, or conducting research with vulnerable populations would be an advantage What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible in temporary basis for 3 months. A competitive hourly rate commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The University will make a mandatory 5% MPF contribution in accordance with Hong Kong regulations. The appointment is project-based; subject to satisfactory performance, opportunities for participation in future data collection campaigns may be available. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the posts are filled, which ever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: May 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
