    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536241/vicepresident-and-provicechancellor-global": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Management / Officers 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Ref.: 536241 Work type: Full-time Department: President's Office (60100) Categories: Senior Management / Officers Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor ( Global ) The University Founded in 1911, the University of Hong Kong has attained its pre-eminence as a research-led comprehensive university through upholding the highest international standards of excellence in its research pursuits, scholarship, teaching and learning, and service to the community. The University is consistently ranked amongst the world’s top universities: 11 th in QS World University Rankings 2026, 1 st in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026 and 33 rd in Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026. In recent years, the University was ranked multiple times as the most international University in the world. Home to ten disciplinary Faculties (Architecture, Arts, Business and Economics, Dentistry, Education, Engineering, Law, Medicine, Science, and Social Sciences), the University is committed to fostering interdisciplinary exchange with an outlook for transformative breakthroughs, innovations and global impact. There are 42,330 undergraduate and postgraduate students from 97 countries, and more than 9,600 academic, academic-related and administrative staff. The University has embarked on a number of ambitious infrastructure and facilities projects for future expansion in the Northern Metropolis, Beijing, Shanghai and Europe. The Position The Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) (hereinafter referred to as VP(G)) will be a full member of the Senior Management Team of the University.  He/She will be the chief architect of the University’s global engagement, responsible for elevating our international presence, influence, and impact. Reporting to the President & Vice-Chancellor, the VP(G) leads the globalization strategy of the University by adopting an inclusive and integrated approach. He/She is responsible for strengthening the University's global networks of collaboration, building key relationships with relevant stakeholders in Chinese Mainland and overseas, maximizing opportunities across talent recruitment, teaching and learning, research, knowledge exchange and technology transfer, and deepening the University’s presence and engagement with Chinese Mainland and globally.  The appointment will be for a five-year term, subject to renewal and the position is accorded the status of University Officer. Key responsibilities include but are not limited to: Strategic Leadership: Develop and implement a comprehensive, forward-looking Mainland and global strategy aligned with the University’s vision and mission. Partnership Development: Forge and sustain high-impact strategic alliances and partnership with world-leading universities, research institutions, industry partners, and government bodies, and act as an ambassador and represent the University in major Mainland and global initiatives. International Reputation: Strengthen the University’s global brand and profile as a hub for cutting-edge research, talent, and cross-cultural integration. Global Student Experience: Enhance international student recruitment and exchange, provide support to facilitate student mobility, and to ensure a vibrant, diverse, and inclusive campus community. Geopolitical Navigation: Provide insightful guidance on global trends and geographical dynamics to inform university strategy and risk management. The Person The successful candidate should be an outstanding scholar at full Professor level or above, with distinguished international standing. Skills & Experience Possesses an international reputation for distinguished academic and research excellence, with a distinguished career in higher education, international relations, or a relevant global sector Demonstrates a proven track record of strategic leadership in global engagement, partnership building, launch of institutional partnership programmes, and complex international project management Exhibits a deep understanding of global higher education trends, geopolitical landscapes, and the role of the university in a connected world Brings an extensive global network and partnership, and inspires and motivates others to engage in international networking and partnership Has the ability to contribute to the leadership of a complex institution Personal Style and Characteristics Proactive and lateral thinker Leader with sound judgement, professional integrity, high levels of emotional intelligence, deep business insights and a pragmatic approach to financial management A team builder contributing to a positive team-oriented culture Good at mentoring and developing talent An entrepreneurial, target-oriented and delivery-focused mindset Outstanding communication skills with ability to negotiate, influence and finalize commercial agreements across organizational boundaries Performance-driven, motivated by purpose and the ability to “make things happen” Natural inclination to horizon scan and identify opportunities/challenges High level of ambassadorial skills and the ability to command respect and instil trust Aptitude for working across international borders, with a natural empathy with and interest in different cultures around the globe Someone of utmost integrity and who would prioritise building up the institutional capability and resilience of the University function Nominations and Applications Nominations, expression of interest and applications should be directed to Heidrick & Struggles via email at hkuvpg@heidrick.com in confidence. Review of nominations and applications will begin now and will continue until the post is filled.  The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency. Advertised: May 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536241 Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) President's Office (60100) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536241 Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) President's Office (60100) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/536259/professor-and-head-of-department-of-mathematics": {
      "title": "Professor and Head of Department of Mathematics",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Professor and Head of Department of Mathematics The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 536259 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Mathematics (25500) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Professor and Head of the Department of Mathematics, Faculty of Science, The University of Hong Kong (HKU).  This is an outstanding leadership opportunity for an eminent scholar to shape the future of one of Asia’s leading mathematics departments.  We seek an academic leader with a distinguished record of excellence in research, teaching, knowledge exchange, and academic administration, along with a strong commitment to advancing the Department’s and University’s missions and engagement with the wider community.  The successful candidate will drive the Department’s strategic vision, foster interdisciplinary and international collaboration, and further elevate its global impact.  Candidates should hold a PhD in Mathematics or a closely related field and possess the stature of a full Professor at a research-intensive institution.  The most highly qualified applicants may be considered for appointment as Chair Professor. The University of Hong Kong Founded in 1911, HKU is a research-led comprehensive university that upholds the highest international standards of excellence in research, scholarship, teaching, and service to the community.  The University is consistently ranked among the world’s top universities: 11 th in QS World University Rankings 2026, 1 st in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026, 33 rd in the Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026, and recognized as the 3 rd most international university in 2026. Department of Mathematics The Department of Mathematics at HKU is renowned for its tradition of excellence in mathematical research and education, with a vibrant community of scholars engaged in a broad spectrum of pure and applied mathematics.  The Department hosts internationally recognized research groups in areas such as algebra and number theory, geometry, computational mathematics, and optimization and operations research.  More information about the Department can be found at https://hkumath.hku.hk/web/index.php . Position Description The Department seeks a distinguished scholar to provide visionary leadership and strategic direction, ensuring continued alignment with the academic missions of HKU and its tradition of excellence.  The successful candidate will help the Department uphold the highest international standards of research and teaching, foster interdisciplinary collaboration and community engagement, optimize the deployment of departmental resources, cultivate an inclusive and vibrant intellectual community, and expand the Department’s international collaborations and networks. Qualifications and Qualities Ph.D. in Mathematics or a closely related field, and stature equivalent to full Professor or Chair Professor rank; Outstanding record of academic achievements and international recognition in research, scholarship, and teaching; Proven experience in leadership and university-level administration; Strong international network and demonstrated ability to secure research funding; Effective interpersonal communication skills and a high standard of personal integrity; and Commitment to representing the interests of the discipline and the Department in the broader community. Compensation and Benefits A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and professional leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries.  Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. Application The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  To ensure full consideration, applicants should apply online and upload: (1) a CV with publication list, (2) a cover letter, (3) an outline of strategic vision as Head of the Department of Mathematics.  Review of applications will begin as soon as possible and continue until Octo ber 31, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: May 11, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536259 Professor and Head of Department of Mathematics Department of Mathematics (25500) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 536259 Professor and Head of Department of Mathematics Department of Mathematics (25500) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/534975/clinical-professor-of-practiceclinical-associate-professor-of-practiceclinical-assistant-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 534975 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointments as Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) in Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 534975), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. Fractional appointments may be considered for suitable candidates. Applicants should possess a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong, and a higher professional qualification of Specialty Fellowship of the relevant Hong Kong colleges under the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine or equivalent. They should demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching, and be able to contribute to the enhancement and development of courses for the Faculty in the broad spectrum of medical and health sciences education. Proven capacity and potential in conducting research in their respective field(s) would be an advantage. Direct communication with patients is required and the languages employed are English, Cantonese and Putonghua. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointments will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidates. Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online, upload an up-to-date C.V. and provide contact information of at least 3 referees. Review of applications will start from July 7, 2026 and continue until November 7, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: May 7, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 7, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 534975 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Nov 7, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 534975 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice Department of Emergency Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (22700) Nov 7, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
