    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/531998/professorassociate-professorassistant-professor-in-materials-innovation-for-life-sciences-and-energy-miles": {
      "title": "Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor in Materials Innovation for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor in Materials Innovation for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 531998 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Chemistry (25200) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor in Materials Innovation for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) (Ref.: 531998) Founded in 1911, The University of Hong Kong (HKU) is a leading international university renowned for excellence in research and education. HKU is a highly international university ranked 17th in the world by QS in 2025, and it offers a comprehensive range of programmes across ten faculties. The University’s diverse community of students and staff — including Ph.D. students and postdoctoral fellows from top universities in the US, UK, China, and beyond — contributes to a vibrant, multicultural campus. Materials Innovation Institute for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) The Materials Innovation Institute for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) is a highly interdisciplinary research institute at HKU, housed in a state-of-the-art ~12,000 m² facility with cutting-edge laboratories and office spaces. MILES brings together around 20 faculty members from the Faculties of Science, Engineering, and Medicine, fostering a collaborative environment at the interface of these disciplines. It provides a unique platform for interdisciplinary research in chemistry, materials science, nanotechnology, biomedical science, and energy innovation. MILES faculty also enjoy the flexibility to recruit Ph.D. students year-round, which helps to rapidly grow and advance their research teams. The Positions We now invite applications for faculty positions at all levels of Full Professor , Associate Professor and Assistant Professor . Exceptional candidates may be considered for appointment as Chair Professor . Appointees will be based in MILES and jointly appointed with a relevant academic unit at HKU (for example, the Department of Chemistry, Faculty of Engineering, or School of Biomedical Sciences in the Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine). We are open to virtually all areas of the physical sciences, engineering, and biomedical sciences that are relevant to chemistry, materials, and nanoscience. Specific research focus areas of particular interest include: 1) Novel organic and inorganic molecular, polymeric or nanoscale materials with interesting properties and functions 2) Soft materials and biomaterials 3) Biophysics and biochemistry involving novel molecules and materials 4) Nanomedicine and bioengineering for new generations of medical imaging techniques, drugs and vaccines 5) Energy materials, catalytic materials, and electrochemistry 6) Electrocatalysis, gas storage and conversions 7) Optoelectronic devices, solar cells and novel optical materials 8) Renewable energy solutions, novel batteries, carbon neutrality approaches 9) Computational chemistry, theoretical chemistry, machine learning, artificial intelligence and robotics for chemistry, biology and materials science 10) Nanomedicine (broadly defined) Qualifications Applicants should possess the following qualifications and attributes: • A Ph.D. in a relevant discipline (physical sciences, engineering, or biomedical sciences) • A demonstrated ability to secure competitive research funding • A strong commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring of students • For senior positions, (1) an internationally recognized record of research excellence and scholarly achievement in an area related to chemistry, materials or nanoscience, and to lead a high-impact research programme. (2) A collaborative, interdisciplinary mindset and proven academic leadership experience. What We Offer For Assistant Professors, the appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 3 years initially with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of the second three-year fixed-term contract. Exceptionally outstanding candidates at Professor/Associate Professor level may be considered for appointment on tenure terms subject to approval. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. An internationally competitive start-up package, including dedicated new laboratory space at MILES, will be tailored to the appointee’s needs and experience to support their research and ensure a strong foundation for their research endeavours. How to Apply The University only accepts online applications for these positions. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload the following documents: (i) a cover letter, (ii) an up-to-date curriculum vitae (including a full list of publications), (iii) a teaching statement (maximum 2 pages), (iv) a research statement (maximum 2 pages) outlining current and future research plans, and (v) the contact information of at least three referees. Informal inquiries can be sent to Dr. T.L. Lee at tllee315@hku.hk. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the positions are filled. Only shortlisted candidates will be invited for an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: May 2, 2025 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 531998 Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor in Materials Innovation for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) Department of Chemistry (25200) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 531998 Professor/Associate Professor/Assistant Professor in Materials Innovation for Life Sciences and Energy (MILES) Department of Chemistry (25200) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/530520/it-officerit-manager-hku-jockey-club-enterprise-sustainability-global-research-institute": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 IT Officer/IT Manager, HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 530520 Work type: Full-time Department: HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute (07009) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong IT Officer/IT Manager, HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 530520) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute, a strategic collaboration between The University of Hong Kong (HKU) and The Hong Kong Jockey Club (HKJC), aspires to establish as a world-class hub for Environmental, Social, and Governance best practices for Hong Kong, Asia and beyond. Bringing together distinguished global scholars from diverse fields, our mission is to foster a multidisciplinary approach to ESG research and training, as well as to forge partnerships with private and public sectors for sustainability initiatives and responsible leadership advocacy. As a leading institute in ESG research, we are dedicated to creating meaningful, lasting impact through pioneering studies, actionable insights, ESG index development, start-up incubation and transformative projects. Our objective is to equip the next generation of ESG professionals and leaders with the knowledge and skills necessary to promote responsible and sustainable growth. In our pursuit of excellence, we recognise the importance of collaboration and knowledge exchange. We are committed to facilitating dialogues and cooperation among regulators, corporates, NGOs, and academics, to ensure the development and dissemination of best practices in ESG. Together, we aim to shape a more sustainable, equitable, and responsible future for all stakeholders. Applicants should hold a bachelor's degree or higher in Information Technology or a related discipline, along with a minimum of 5 years of relevant work experience. They should demonstrate a quick learning ability, possess strong interpersonal skills, a strong sense of responsibility, and the ability to work proactively with faculty members in a fast-paced environment. Besides, they should possess a strong technical background and be capable of providing expert-level support across various IT systems and applications. Applicants should have experience in managing research data. Solid experience in Linux (Red Hat/CentOS/Ubuntu) and Windows Server system administration, system shell scripting, database management, server hardware setup and maintenance, and peta-scale storage systems using distributed parallel file systems is essential Familiarity with high-performance computing clusters, VM/Container, cloud technologies, and Python would be advantageous. They should also have a proven track record of leading a team and successfully completing projects. Proficiency in scripting to automate tasks, strong problem-solving and decision-making skills, as well as the ability to prioritize and manage multiple tasks and projects, are essential. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills are necessary for effective collaboration with stakeholders at all levels. Experience in IT procurement, including vendor management and contract negotiation, is highly valued. The appointee will mainly be responsible for research data management and collaborate with the Faculty's IT Team to provide support in maintaining the overall IT infrastructure, server administration, and delivering high-quality IT services at the Institute. He/she will ensure  smooth functioning of all systems, providing guidance, training, and mentorship to deliver exceptional IT support and services. The appointee will play a crucial role in supporting various projects by coordinating IT requirements and ensuring seamless execution. They will also work in collaboration with stakeholders at the University and Faculty levels to ensure alignment of IT systems and processes. Furthermore, the appointee will provide technical support for events and functions and undertake ad hoc projects as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled. Advertised: Nov 14, 2024 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 530520 IT Officer/IT Manager, HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute (07009) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 530520 IT Officer/IT Manager, HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute HKU Jockey Club Enterprise Sustainability Global Research Institute (07009) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/519152/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Architecture 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 519152 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Real Estate and Construction (Ref.: 519152) We now invite applications for the Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Real Estate and Construction. The Department enjoys a world-class reputation for its research and teaching in real estate and construction fields. Under the QS University Rankings 2022, it is ranked in the 14th position in the subject of Built Environment globally. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will work on a project related to urban entrepreneurship. The appointee will employ mathematical modelling skills to specify the relationship between start-ups, developers, and planners under a framework of spatial equilibrium. The appointee will coordinate data collection and analysis. The appointee will assist in the preparation of reports. Requirements a Ph.D. degree in applied mathematics, urban economics, data science or related subjects from a world leading university. Applicants should have a research background in mathematical and computational modelling. Preference will be given to the applicants with specialised skills in calculus, spatial equilibrium model, and equilibrium sorting model. Applicants with an outstanding track record of publications and research project experience will be an advantage. What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post(s). Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The appointee will join a multidisciplinary team led by Prof. Kelvin Wong, Dr. Alex Shi, and Dr. Jintao Ke. Prof. Wong is the Head of Department of Real Estate and Construction and a leading scholar in real estate economics; Dr. Shi is an Assistant Professor in urban economics from Department of Real Estate and Construction; Dr. Ke is an Assistant Professor in transportation engineering from the Department of Civil Engineering. If you have any enquiry about the post, please contact Dr. Shi via alexshi@hku.hk . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Feb 2, 2023 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 519152 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 519152 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
