    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537223/clinical-professor-of-practiceclinical-associate-professor-of-practiceclinical-assistant-professor-of-practice": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537223 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Anaesthesiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20100) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice (several posts) in the Department of Anaesthesiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537223), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance.  Fractional appointment may be considered for suitable candidates. Applicants should possess a medical qualification registrable with the Medical Council of Hong Kong, and a higher professional qualification of Specialty Fellowship of the relevant Hong Kong colleges under the Hong Kong Academy of Medicine or equivalent.  They should demonstrate a commitment to clinical work, teaching, and research; with particular focus on clinical advancement and/or development of teaching for the department and Faculty.  Proven capacity and potential in conducting research in their respective field(s) would be an advantage.  Direct communication with patients is required and the languages employed are English, Cantonese and Putonghua. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  A monthly cash allowance will be offered to the successful candidates.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online, upload an up-to-date C.V. and provide the contact information of at least 3 referees.  Applicants should indicate clearly which level they wish to be considered for.  Review of applications will start from December 15, 2026 and continue until January 31, 2027 or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537223 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice Department of Anaesthesiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20100) Jan 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537223 Clinical Professor of Practice/Clinical Associate Professor of Practice/Clinical Assistant Professor of Practice Department of Anaesthesiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20100) Jan 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537576/clerk-iii-holding-the-functional-title-of-senior-executive-assistantexecutive-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537576 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537576) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis or a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability) Applicants should hold a Bachelor’s degree with at least three years’ relevant work experience. They should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; good communication, organizational and problem-solving skills; IT proficiency; the ability to prioritize multiple tasks efficiently to meet tight deadlines; and competence in performing administrative duties and collaborating with different stakeholders. They should also be attentive to details, a good team player with self-motivation and a strong sense of responsibility. Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience will be considered for the post of Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant). The appointee will provide administrative support to the new taught Master programme, including student recruitment and admissions, curriculum management, handling of student matters, examinations, event management; and perform other duties as assigned by supervisor(s). Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start October 29, 2026 and continue until December 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537576 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Dec 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537576 Clerk I/II (holding the functional title of Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant) School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Dec 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
