    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537493/lecturerassistant-lecturer": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Assistant Lecturer",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Lecturer/Assistant Lecturer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537493 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Engineering (14000) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer / Assistant Lecturer in the Faculty of Engineering (Ref.:537493), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. The Faculty of Engineering is committed to providing high-quality education in Artificial Intelligence (AI) for undergraduate students to keep status quo. These courses represent key initiatives to promote active learning and interdisciplinary mindset through hands-on and project-based pedagogy, inspiring students to engage with real-world engineering applications. We are seeking passionate educators to join our teaching team in designing and delivering lectures, tutorials, and project-based learning experiences in AI-related courses. To ensure the courses remain up to date and relevant, appointees are expected to regularly review and update teaching materials, incorporating the latest developments in AI. The appointed candidate will also supervise student-driven projects within the Faculty of Engineering and collaborative initiatives with external partners. Candidates with substantial practical experience in applying AI to solve engineering challenges are especially encouraged to apply, as we value professional insight alongside academic excellence. Successful applicants should be comfortable in teaching and supervising in a dynamic international environment. Qualifications and Requirements: A Master’s or Ph.D. degree in Computer Science or related engineering fields; Demonstrated expertise in Artificial Intelligence, including but not limited to computer vision, foundation models and agentic systems, embodied AI and intelligent robotics, or AI infrastructure and systems; Practical experience in applying or deploying AI techniques to engineering problems; and A strong record of, or clear potential for, excellence in teaching practice-oriented courses, mentoring students, and supervising projects. Based on the teaching experience and academic qualifications, suitable candidates will be considered for positions ranging from Assistant Lecturer or Lecturer. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary for Lecturer, or up to 10% of basic salary for Assistant Lecturer. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Applicants are highly encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537493 Lecturer/Assistant Lecturer Faculty of Engineering (14000) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537493 Lecturer/Assistant Lecturer Faculty of Engineering (14000) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537508/assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537508 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Engineering (14000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Engineering (Ref.: 537508) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a recognised Bachelor’s degree, with at least 3 years’ solid work experience, preferably in tertiary institutions. They should have an excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, and fluency in Putonghua. They should also have strong interpersonal, supervisory, organisational, problem-solving and communication skills; the ability to work independently and under pressure to meet tight deadlines; a strong sense of responsibility; and be a good team player with the ability of multitasking and attentive to details. Experience in undergraduate programme administration would be an advantage. The appointee will provide administrative support for undergraduate programmes, including the HKU-Cambridge Undergraduate Recruitment Scheme and flagship programmes. Duties involve managing student matters, planning events and enrichment activities, coordinating career-related programmes, and liaising with external parties. The appointee will also perform other duties as assigned and may occasionally be required to work outside normal office hours or travel outside Hong Kong. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 202 6 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537524/executive-assistant-at-the-rank-of-clerk-ii": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537524 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) in the Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) (Ref.: 537524) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) About Us Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) is an academic research-support centre embracing multi-omics and big data biomedical research under the LKS Faculty of Medicine.  CPOS core laboratories host state-of-the-art omics technology platforms with sophisticated equipment supported by our over 70 dedicated and trained members.  Welcome to visit us https://cpos.hku.hk to explore more. The Role Assist with daily office operations, including procurement, payments, reimbursements, and invoicing Manage and maintain databases, ensuring accuracy and consistency Handle service and payment enquiries from internal and external parties Provide customer service and support through effective written and verbal communication Support events, activities, and social media administration Perform various clerical and administrative tasks, such as filing, data entry, and correspondence management Carry out other duties as assigned Qualifications and Qualities Bachelor’s Degree/Diploma At least 1-2 years of relevant work experience Proficiency in advanced IT applications, including MS Office, particularly Excel Good command of spoken and written English and Chinese Good organizational and interpersonal skills Strong sense of responsibility, a fast learner, highly motivated and attentive to details A good team player with the ability to work independently Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview.  Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 537339) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537524 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537524 Executive Assistant (at the rank of Clerk II) Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
