    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537566/fulltime-multimedia-designer-at-the-rank-of-technical-officersenior-technical-assistant-in-the-division-of-neurology": {
      "title": "Full-time Multimedia Designer (at the rank of Technical Officer/Senior Technical Assistant) in the Division of Neurology",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Full-time Multimedia Designer (at the rank of Technical Officer/Senior Technical Assistant) in the Division of Neurology The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537566 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Full-time Multimedia Designer (at the rank of Technical Officer/Senior Technical Assistant) in the Division of Neurology of the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537566) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess 5 passes in HKCEE, including English Language (minimum Grade C for Syllabus A or Level 2 from 2007 onwards), Chinese Language (minimum Level 2 from 2007 onwards) and Mathematics, or a minimum of Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSE, including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, together with at least 5 years’ hands-on experience in graphic design, multimedia design or a related field; or a recognized Bachelor’s degree. They should be proficient in creative software such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator and Premiere. Experience in video production and website design is preferred. Experience in event coordination is an advantage. Those with lower qualifications or less experience may be considered for appointment as Senior Technical Assistant. The appointee will assist in: (i) content creation and distribution, including creative concepts layout, artwork and video productions for the distribution of various platforms such as websites, social media platforms and printed materials; (ii) UI design, digital marketing materials, social media content management, and website maintenance; (iii) campaign planning and execution, by developing and implementing media campaigns across digital, print and broadcast channels; and (iv) event coordination, including assisting in the planning, promotion, and preparation of all event materials based on the guidance and requirements provided by supervisors. He/She will mainly work on projects undertaken by the Stroke Research and Prevention Group of HKU (HKU Stroke). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits, if applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. and portfolio. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537566 Full-time Multimedia Designer (at the rank of Technical Officer/Senior Technical Assistant) in the Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537566 Full-time Multimedia Designer (at the rank of Technical Officer/Senior Technical Assistant) in the Division of Neurology Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
