    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537569/it-officer-in-the-school-of-computing-and-data-science-ref-537569": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 IT Officer in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537569) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537569 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as IT Officer in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537569) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.) The Role The appointee will be responsible for supporting the development, enhancement, implementation, and maintenance of in-house systems, websites, web applications, databases, and internal digital tools. The role will focus mainly on software development, system support, user requirement gathering, and IT project coordination.  The appointee will also be expected to take a leading role in assigned IT projects and oversee the project development cycle, from requirements analysis and solution design through development, testing, implementation, user acceptance, rollout, documentation, and subsequent enhancement. The appointee may occasionally be required to support for general IT, operations, events, facilities, and administrative duties as needed. The appointee should be proactive, responsible, detail-minded, and able to work independently and collaboratively with users and stakeholder. They should demonstrate a strong sense of project ownership and be able to deliver practical and sustainable IT solutions that improve operational efficiency. Key Responsibilities (include, but are not limited to): In-House System, Web & Application Development: Design, develop, test, and implement in-house systems, websites, web applications, databases, and internal digital tools to support daily operations and improve workflow efficiency. IT Project Leadership and Development Cycle Oversight: Take a leading role in assigned IT projects and oversee the project development cycle, including requirements analysis, solution design, development, testing, implementation, user acceptance, rollout, documentation, and post-implementation enhancement. Coordinate with users, stakeholders, vendors, and other relevant parties to facilitate timely and effective project delivery. User Requirement Gathering & Solution Planning: Liaise with users and stakeholders to gather and analyze requirements, translate operational needs into functional or system specifications, evaluate possible solutions, and recommend practical and sustainable approaches that support operational requirements. System Maintenance, Support & Enhancement: Maintain, support and enhance existing systems and digital platforms, including troubleshooting technical issues, fixing bugs, optimizing system performance, and supporting database queries, reporting functions, application programming interfaces, and system integrations. Qualifications and Qualities A recognized Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a related discipline. Relevant experience in software development, web application development, system support, database management, IT project coordination, or related IT functions is preferred. Proficiency in front-end and back-end development technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, PHP, Python, SQL , or other suitable programming languages. Experience with modern development frameworks, libraries, or platforms such as React, Vue.js, Angular, Next.js, Node.js, Express.js, Laravel, Django , or similar technologies, would be an advantage. Knowledge of relational databases such as MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server , or other database systems. Experience with database design, data management, and reporting would be an advantage. Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Fluency in Cantonese and Putonghua would be an advantage. Good interpersonal, communication, analytical, troubleshooting, problem-solving, and project coodination skills. A strong sense of responsibility and project ownership; self-motivated, well-organized, detail-minded, and service-oriented; and able to work independently as well as collaboratively with users and stakeholders. A positive mindset and willingness to learn and apply new skills and technologies to meet changing organizational and operational needs. Fresh graduates or candidates with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for appointment at a suitable level. The appointee may also be required to perform other duties as assigned. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 16, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 16, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537569 IT Officer in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537569) School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Nov 16, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537569 IT Officer in the School of Computing and Data Science (Ref.: 537569) School of Computing and Data Science (14700) Nov 16, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537592/lecturer-in-russian-and-turkish-global-and-area-studies": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Russian and Turkish (Global and Area Studies)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Lecturer in Russian and Turkish (Global and Area Studies) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537592 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Modern Languages and Cultures (05100) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer in Russian and Turkish (Global and Area Studies) in the School of Modern Languages and Cultures (Ref.: 537592), to commence on February 1, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in a relevant field and demonstrate expertise in teaching Russian and Turkish to non-native speakers. They should be native or near-native speakers of Russian and Turkish with excellent English proficiency. Familiarity with contemporary trends in pedagogy and assessment, including the use of AI tools for teaching and learning, is essential. The successful candidate will be expected to teach courses at various levels, develop new curricula, design assessment materials, and engage with stakeholders to support the programme’s activities related to Russian and Turkish culture. While the primary duties involve teaching and administration, research activities are also encouraged. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and professional leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V., proof of qualifications, a cover letter in English, Russian, and Turkish, and a portfolio of past teaching materials and evaluations.  Three reference letters should be sent directly by the referees to smlcsena@hku.hk . Closes November 20, 2026 . The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expressly encourages qualified persons of all genders to apply. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537592 Lecturer in Russian and Turkish (Global and Area Studies) School of Modern Languages and Cultures (05100) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537592 Lecturer in Russian and Turkish (Global and Area Studies) School of Modern Languages and Cultures (05100) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537597/senior-software-developer-software-developer-at-the-rank-of-it-officer-it-technician-for-student-information-systems-team-in-the-information-technology-services-several-posts": {
      "title": "Senior Software Developer / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) for Student Information Systems Team in the Information Technology Services (Several Posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Senior Software Developer / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) for Student Information Systems Team in the Information Technology Services (Several Posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537597 Work type: Full-time Department: Information Technology Services (40000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Software Developer / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) for Student Information Systems Team in the Information Technology Services (several posts) (Ref.: 537597) Information Technology Services (ITS) provides central IT services to support the University’s teaching, learning, research and administrative activities. ITS is transforming its organization to support its strategic development and adoption of new technologies. Information about ITS can be obtained at https://its.hku.hk/ . We are seeking high-caliber IT talent to join us in providing top-notch IT services for our Student Information Systems Team, leveraging their technical expertise to design, develop, integrate and support tailored solutions that contribute to the digital transformation of the University. The Role The appointees will be responsible for: Designing, developing, and deploying web and mobile applications, conducting unit tests and SIT, and supporting users during UAT and end-to-end integration tests; Modernizing systems, migrating legacy applications and integrating microservices; Supporting the adoption and integration of AI technologies (including LLMs and MCP frameworks) to enhance student experience and operational efficiency; Analyzing user requirements and producing student analytics and reports; Managing and maintaining cloud infrastructure and services on Microsoft Azure to ensure high availability, security, and performance; and Providing technical support and maintaining reliable, high-quality IT services that underpin student information management and University business processes. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology or a related field; Solid experience in software application development and system support; A good command of written and spoken English; and Strong communication, presentation, analytical and problem-solving skills, with a high degree of responsibility. Applicants should have good knowledge of, and relevant experience in, some of the following areas: Designing and developing microservices with Spring Boot and Java Servlets; Frontend web development using modern frameworks such as React, Next.js, and Vue.js, with Node.js for server-side development and tooling; Native or hybrid mobile app development (React Native, Swift, Objective-C, Cordova, Framework7); Database technologies (Oracle, MS SQL); System modernization strategies and legacy application migration; Cloud technologies (Microsoft Azure), including API Management (APIM) and hybrid cloud; API technologies and protocols, including RESTful APIs and SOAP, as well as integrations leveraging the Model Context Protocol (MCP) to enable large-scale AI adoption and consumption; AI and machine-learning integrations, particularly leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs); PeopleSoft Campus Solutions and Oracle BI Publisher; Power BI (Power BI Desktop and Power BI Report Builder); and IoT development including contactless smartcard systems and related technologies. Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for appointment as Software Developer (at the rank of IT Technician). High-caliber fresh graduates are also welcome to apply. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years and commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 1, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 1, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537597 Senior Software Developer / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) for Student Information Systems Team in the Information Technology Services (Several Posts) Information Technology Services (40000) Nov 1, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537597 Senior Software Developer / Software Developer (at the rank of IT Officer / IT Technician) for Student Information Systems Team in the Information Technology Services (Several Posts) Information Technology Services (40000) Nov 1, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537649/manager-knowledge-exchange-marketing-and-engagement-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Manager, Knowledge Exchange – Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537649 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Manager, Knowledge Exchange – Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537649) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and mutual agreement.) Qualifications and Qualities a bachelor's degree or above is required, preferably in Marketing, Communications, Public Relations, Journalism, Business Administration, or a related discipline; at least 5 years of relevant work experience is required, preferably  in higher education institutions, professional services firms, financial services firms, corporate communications units, international organisations, or agency environments; excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, with strong organisational and interpersonal skills; experience in bridging academia and policy/industry is highly desirable; a collaborative mindset and demonstrated ability to build effective working relationships; IT proficiency and attention to detail; self-motivated, with the ability to work independently as well as part of a team in a dynamic environment; and ability to multitask and prioritise multiple tasks efficiently and work under pressure to meet tight deadlines. Key Responsibilities Reporting to the Director / Assistant Director of Knowledge Exchange, the appointee will support the planning, implementation, promotion, and monitoring of the Faculty's Knowledge Exchange initiatives, with a primary focus on marketing, communications, stakeholder engagement, and public relations. The main duties include, but are not limited to: manage and execute the Knowledge Exchange unit 's marketing, communications, and public relations initiatives, including strategic projects, stakeholder engagement activities, meetings, events, outreach programmes, digital marketing campaigns, branding initiatives, and promotional efforts; develop and implement integrated communications and promotional strategies to enhance the visibility, reputation, and impact of KE initiatives, thought leadership activities, partnerships, and research dissemination; develop and maintain effective relationships with media organisations, industry partners, professional bodies, and other external stakeholders to maximise publicity opportunities and strengthen the Faculty's external engagement; manage all aspects of event management & event-driven collaborations, including project planning, stakeholder communications, vendor liaison, logistics arrangements, on-site operations, inquiry handling, post-event follow-up, and other related coordination activities; monitor and report on media coverage, publicity outcomes, digital engagement, and other key performance indicators (KPIs) to evaluate communications effectiveness; prepare and oversee the development of marketing and communication materials, including press releases, newsletters, website content, social media content, promotional collateral, presentations, reports, and other publications; and perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the function and Director, as well as cross-functional collaboration, including but not limited to the Office of Strategic Partnerships and the Faculty. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 5, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 5, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537649 Manager, Knowledge Exchange – Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 5, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537649 Manager, Knowledge Exchange – Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 5, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
