    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537657/executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537657 Work type: Full-time Department: Customer Services Unit of the Estates Office (66063) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the Customer Services Unit of the Estates Office (Ref.: 537657) We are looking for an Executive Officer to join the Estates Office. The Role The appointee will lead a team in managing the campus facilities services including event support services, function venue bookings, official car and shuttle bus services, customer services and fleet management.  The appointee will work closely with departments, contractors, in-house teams and the Integrated Facilities Management operator to provide high-level support to a spectrum of administrative processes associated with tendering exercises, service contracts, staffing, financial and reporting matters. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities A recognized Bachelor’s degree with at least 5 years’ work experience in the higher education sector or a related field, of which a minimum of 2 years should be at a supervisory or management level.  Possession of work experience in the customer services field would be an advantage; Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese; A high level of communication, problem-solving, multi-tasking and time-management skills with good computer literacy; Ability to prioritize work to ensure all competing deadlines are met to a high standard; Highly developed administrative and organizational skills with the capacity to work both independently and as part of a team; and Being self-motivated and attentive to detail, with the ability to develop effective working relationships. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.   A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 5, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 16, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 5, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537657 Executive Officer Customer Services Unit of the Estates Office (66063) Nov 5, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537657 Executive Officer Customer Services Unit of the Estates Office (66063) Nov 5, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
