takeholders; and ability to work independently as well as part of a team in a dynamic environment. Key Responsibilities Reporting to the Manager, Knowledge Exchange, the appointee will provide marketing, communications, and administrative support for the Faculty's Knowledge Exchange initiatives. The main duties include: assist in implementing marketing and communications plans to promote the Faculty's Knowledge’s Exchange activities, research impact, partnerships, events, and thought leadership initiatives; create and manage content for digital channels, including websites, social media platforms, and newsletters; support the production of reports, impact stories, brochures, event materials, presentations, and other communications collateral; coordinate the Faculty's social media and digital communications channels, including content scheduling, monitoring, and basic performance reporting; assist in organizing conferences, forums, seminars, workshops, networking events, and stakeholder engagement activities, including logistics, registration, venue arrangements, and on-site support; liaise with internal departments, academic staff, external vendors, media representatives, and partner organizations on marketing and event-related matters; maintain databases, mailing lists, event records, media contacts, and other administrative documentation; provide general administrative and clerical support to The Faculty’s Knowledge Exchange unit, including procurement, reimbursement, scheduling, meeting arrangements, and general office filing; and perform other duties as assigned by the Manager and the Director of Knowledge Exchange. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 4, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 4, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537648 Senior Executive Assistant, Knowledge Exchange - Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Clerk I) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 4, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537648 Senior Executive Assistant, Knowledge Exchange - Marketing and Engagement (at the rank of Clerk I) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 4, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
