    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537654/technical-manager-iii": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Technical Manager I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537654 Work type: Full-time Department: Project Division of the Estates Office (66062) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Technical Manager I/II in the Project Division of the Estates Office (Ref.: 537654) We are looking for a Technical Manager I/II in Site Safety to join the Estates Office. The Role The appointee will participate in campus expansion projects relating to quality and safety management. He/she will be responsible for the day-to-day monitoring and supervision of site works and interface works, quality control, carrying out site inspections, overseeing on-site and off-site testing as directed, and monitoring site housekeeping and safety.  He/she will liaise with project teams, maintenance and operations teams, Safety Office, external consultants and government authorities in relation to project quality and safety. The appointee may be required to work shifts, overtime and on public holidays, subject to prior arrangements. Enquiries about the post should be sent to eojobs@hku.hk . Qualifications and Qualities Applicants should possess: A Bachelor’s degree or above in Architecture, Mechanical/Electrical/Building Services Engineering or equivalent disciplines; At least 8 years’ post-qualification experience, of which at least 5 years must be in a supervisory/responsible position in project management, monitoring and site supervision; A valid Construction Industry Safety Training Certificate (Green Card) issued in accordance with Chapter 59 of the Factories and Industrial Undertakings Ordinance (i.e. by attending the relevant safety training courses which are recognized by the Commissioner for Labour) or equivalent; Good communication skills, self-motivation, a strong sense of responsibility, and the ability to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines; and Solid site supervision experience in large-scale, institutional, DfMA or MiC projects would be an advantage. Those with less experience or lower qualifications may be considered for appointment as Technical Manager II. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref: 536931) need not re-apply. What We offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.   A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s career site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 28, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537654 Technical Manager I/II Project Division of the Estates Office (66062) Oct 28, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537654 Technical Manager I/II Project Division of the Estates Office (66062) Oct 28, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
