    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537658/senior-technical-assistant-in-bioresearch-support-core": {
      "title": "Senior Technical Assistant in Bioresearch Support Core",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Technical Assistant in Bioresearch Support Core The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537658 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Assistant in Bioresearch Support Core of the Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) (Ref.: 537658) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) We are Expanding | Come and Join Us Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) is an academic research-support centre embracing multi-omics and big data biomedical research under the LKS Faculty of Medicine. CPOS core laboratories host state-of-the-art technology platforms with sophisticated equipment supported by over 70 dedicated members. Welcome to visit https://cpos.hku.hk to explore more. Career Prospects Excellent on-job training Long-term development opportunities Exposures and interactions with world-class research groups Expert technical and managerial career track The Role Provide training and technical support to users utilizing laboratory instruments Manage and maintain laboratory instruments Assist in procurement and stock management of laboratory consumables Handle documents and prepare reports Provide organizational support for events and seminars Perform administrative duties as assigned Qualifications and Qualities Bachelor’s degree or above in Biological or Biomedical research related is a plus Experience in administration and procurement is preferred Self-motivated, responsible, have good communication skills and enjoy teamwork Candidates with higher qualifications or more experience may be considered for the position of Senior Technical Officer/Technical Officer Fresh graduates will also be considered Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 537012) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits, continuing professional development, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537658 Senior Technical Assistant in Bioresearch Support Core Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537658 Senior Technical Assistant in Bioresearch Support Core Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537664/fulltime-research-assistant-i-and-parttime-student-research-assistant-several-posts-in-the-teaching-and-learning-innovation-centre-talic-for-seven-months": {
      "title": "Full-time Research Assistant I and Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) for seven months",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Full-time Research Assistant I and Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) for seven months The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537664 Work type: Full-time, Hourly-paid Department: Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Full-time Research Assistant I and Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) for seven months (Ref.: 537664) (to commence early December 2026 and end in May-June 2027) All appointees (Research Assistant I and Student Research Assistants) will provide support to a project which aims to investigate Muslim international students’ decision to study in HK, intention to work locally after graduation, and satisfaction with their study‑abroad experience. We warmly welcome applicants who are dedicated and passionate about fostering a more diverse and inclusive environment for teaching and learning to join us in this project. Full-time Research Assistant I Applicants for the Full-time Research Assistant I position should possess a Master’s degree or above in Public Policy, Higher Education, or relevant Social Sciences discipline. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, intercultural communication and interpersonal skills, organizational skills and experience in conducting qualitative and/or quantitative research (e.g. analyzing interview and questionnaire data). They should also have a strong sense of responsibility, be detailed-minded, be able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment. Preference will be also be given to those with experience in conducting higher education and/or public policy research. Part-time Student Research Assistant Applicants for Part-time Student Research Assistant(s) position should be current undergraduate students in social science and education disciplines, preferably in their final year of study. Given that this is a student-as-partner project related to international Muslim students, we will be recruiting 1 Muslim and 1 non-Muslim student. The applicants should be able to commit to working either one full weekday or two half weekdays per week during the employment period. The estimated working hours will be approximately 7 hours per week, and the hourly pay rates will follow the guidelines of the University. All appointees (Research Assistant I and Student Research Assistants) will assist in literature review, the collection, input and analysis of data for the project, as well as the drafting of project findings for layman reports. They will also contribute to the design and development of the project website and a Muslim‑friendly campus handbook. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Enquiries about the posts should be sent to Dr. Lillian Luk at lyyluk@hku.hk . The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 13 November 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 15, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537664 Full-time Research Assistant I and Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) for seven months Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537664 Full-time Research Assistant I and Part-time Student Research Assistant (several posts) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) for seven months Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
