    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537641/senior-research-assistant-research-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537641 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant I / Senior Research Assistant in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537641), to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Master’s degree in Cancer Biology, Cancer Immunology, Biomedical Sciences or a related field, and demonstrate exceptional experimental, writing, and communication abilities. Preference will be given to candidates with translational research experience in cancer immunology, antibody-based therapeutics, and/or antibody/protein engineering; as well as cell/organoid culture, cellular/molecular biology, antibody/protein characterization, flow cytometry, animal studies, and cancer-related research work. Applicants should have good communication skills, be self-motivated, have the ability to multi-task with attention to detail, be organized and be able to work independently as well as in a multidisciplinary team. The appointee will work under the supervision of Professor Stephanie Ma on translational research projects relating to novel cancer therapeutics development with a focus on targeting cancer stemness using hepatocellular carcinoma as a model system, that is part of a collaborative project. For further information, please contact Professor Stephanie Ma at stefma@hku.hk . Details of Professor Ma’s research can also be found at http://thesmalab.com/. Information about the School of Biomedical Sciences can be obtained at http://www.sbms.hku.hk/ . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ). Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start October 27, 2026 and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537641 Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537641 Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537645/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537645 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537645) (to commence as soon as possible, for one year in the first instance, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability) Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in synthetic biology, immunology, vaccinology, molecular biology, bioengineering, computational biology, artificial intelligence, or a related discipline. They should have strong experimental, analytical, writing, and communication skills. Experience in one or more of the following areas would be an advantage: mRNA/LNP vaccine development, cancer immunotherapy, bacterial infection models, mouse experiments, flow cytometry, cytokine profiling, single-cell RNA sequencing, bioinformatics, or AI-assisted biomedical data analysis. The appointee will contribute to collaborative research projects investigating synthetic biology approaches for vaccine development and cancer treatment. Relevant ongoing research includes the development and mechanistic study of mRNA-LNP vaccines, immune regulation by IL-10, vaccine responses against Staphylococcus aureus and other pathogens, and the use of single-cell and computational approaches to understand vaccine-induced immunity. The work is also aligned with broader developments in life and health technology, including the integration of artificial intelligence with life sciences and medicine. The appointee will be expected to conduct independent and collaborative research, including experimental design, molecular cloning or mRNA construct preparation, vaccine formulation and evaluation, cell-based assays, animal experiments, immune profiling, data analysis, manuscript preparation, and presentation of research findings. He/She may also assist in grant preparation, student supervision, and coordination with collaborators. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from October 27, 2026 and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537645 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537645 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537642/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537642 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537642, to commence as soon as possible for two years, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Cancer Biology, Cancer Immunology, Biomedical Sciences or a related field, and demonstrate exceptional experimental, writing, and communication abilities. Preference will be given to candidates with translational research experience in cancer immunology, antibody-based therapeutics, and/or antibody/protein engineering; as well as cell/organoid culture, cellular/molecular biology, antibody/protein characterization, flow cytometry, animal studies, and cancer-related research work. Applicants should have good communication skills, be self-motivated, have the ability to multi-task with attention to detail, be organized and be able to work independently as well as in a multidisciplinary team. The appointee will work semi-independently under the supervision of Professor Stephanie Ma on translational research projects relating to novel cancer therapeutics development with a focus on targeting cancer stemness using hepatocellular carcinoma as a model system, that is part of a collaborative project. For further information, please contact Professor Stephanie Ma at stefma@hku.hk . Details of Professor Ma’s research can also be found at http://thesmalab.com/. Information about the School of Biomedical Sciences can be obtained at http://www.sbms.hku.hk/. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ). Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start October 27, 2026 and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537642 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537642 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
