    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537643/research-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537643 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537643) (to commence as soon as possible for six months, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should possess a university degree with upper second-class honors or above in Biological/Biomedical Sciences or equivalent. Those who have interests in pursuing further postgraduate studies in the School are preferred. In addition, they should have a good command of written and spoken English, good communication skills, a strong sense of responsibility and commitment and be highly motivated. Previous experience in tissue culture, basic molecular biology work, and/or animal work will be a strong advantage. The appointee will participate in research projects relating to molecular studies to influenza A virus and innate immune responses. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Dr. Zi-Wei Ye via email (zwye@hku.hk). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from as soon as possible and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537643 Research Assistant I/II School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537643 Research Assistant I/II School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537644/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537644 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral fellow in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537644) (to commence as soon as possible for one year, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should have a PhD degree or above, preferably in Biological Science, Biochemistry, Biomedical Sciences, Biophysics or related disciplines. An ideal candidate should have excellent experimentation and communication skills. Preference will be given to applicants with a strong background in at least some of the listed fields: molecular biology, protein purification, cell biology, genome engineering, neuroscience, structural biology, or fluorescence microscopy. Experience in cell imaging or single-molecule fluorescence microscopy will be a plus. The appointee should be organized, self-motivated, highly committed, and be able to work independently as well as in a team. He/She will participate in a research project investigating the biochemistry, biophysics, structural biology, and cell biology underlying how microtubules form diverse cellular architectures. He/She will work in Prof. Jeff Ti’s lab, which employs single-molecule fluorescence and cryogenic electron microscopy (cryo-EM) to dissect the molecular basis that confers diverse human tubulin isotypes' unique and essential functions. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Prof. Ti at jeffti@hku.hk. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply on-line and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 27, 2026 and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537644 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537644 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537640/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537640 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537640), to commence as soon as possible for two years, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Biological/Biomedical Sciences or equivalent. They should have a good command of written and spoken English, good interpersonal and communication skills, high motivation as well as a strong sense of responsibility and commitment. Preference will be given to those with previous research experience in virus-host interaction, influenza viruses and animal models. Eligibility to work in Biosafety Level 3 facility is an advantage. The appointee will contribute substantially to research projects on molecular virology and immunology of emerging and re-emerging viruses (e.g coronaviruses and influenza viruses). Enquiries about the post should be sent to Dr Ziwei YE at zwye@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply on-line and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until January 13, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 13, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537640 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537640 Post-doctoral Fellow School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Jan 13, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
