    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537591/lecturer-in-hong-kong-studies": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Hong Kong Studies",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Lecturer in Hong Kong Studies The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537591 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Chinese (04100) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer in Hong Kong Studies in the School of Chinese (Ref.: 537591), to commence on January 1, 2027, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Hong Kong Studies is the first undergraduate programme to focus on Hong Kong in a comprehensive structure in any university, not only in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region but also overseas. As an interdisciplinary programme, it combines the perspectives and curricular strengths of a variety of disciplines - including literature, art history, history, sociology, politics, economics, and journalism - to give students a broad-based education on Hong Kong’s society, culture, creative industries, economy, politics, history and environment. The Programme adopts a “problem-based” approach where students engage with core issues in Hong Kong’s evolution, such as the interaction between citizens and rulers, the creation of a Hong Kong identity, the city’s global influence as a cultural and financial hub, and its role as a transition zone for ideas, capital and people. More information can be found on the School’s website at https://web.chinese.hku.hk . Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Hong Kong literature and culture or a related field, with at least 3 years’ post-qualification teaching experience at the tertiary level or equivalent professional experience preferred. A demonstrated capacity to develop and teach courses in one or more of the following areas would be favourably considered: Hong Kong literature, Hong Kong print media, Hong Kong food culture, and/or cultural studies. The appointee will be responsible for teaching undergraduate courses within the Hong Kong Studies programme, supervising capstone projects, and undertaking administrative duties as assigned by the Programme Coordinator. Fluency in English, Putonghua, and Cantonese, along with excellent communication and presentation skills, are required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave, medical benefits, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. and a portfolio of past teaching materials and evaluations. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expressly encourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537591 Lecturer in Hong Kong Studies School of Chinese (04100) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537591 Lecturer in Hong Kong Studies School of Chinese (04100) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537601/project-executive-site-management-at-the-rank-of-technical-officerresearch-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Project Executive, Site Management (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Project Executive, Site Management (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537601 Work type: Full-time Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Project Executive, Site Management (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.:537601) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies. HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession. Running a clinical study at a study site requires professional coordination and communication. HKU-CTC’s Site Management Unit (SMU) is a professional unit dedicated to facilitating the approval, logistics, financial management and administration for clinical studies at the project startup stage and throughout each project’s life cycle.  We are seeking a high calibre talent to join our SMU as a Project Executive, Site Management. Comprehensive on-the-job training will be provided.  Fresh graduates are welcome to apply. Main Responsibilities: Support project feasibility assessment; Perform project logistics planning and coordination; Coordinate research ethics applications and submissions, and facilitate communication with research ethics committees; Execute project budget preparation, negotiation and project financial management activities; Assist in administration of clinical study contracts; and Communicate with research teams and internal/external collaborators. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree or above in Biological/Life Sciences or related disciplines; Effective coordination and problem-solving skills; Detail-minded and good sensitivity to numbers; Able to handle multiple concurrent tasks; Good interpersonal and communication skills; and Good command of written and spoken English and Cantonese (proficiency in Putonghua is an advantage). Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 537313) need not re-apply. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Appointment on 2-year fixed term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from October 28, 2026 and continue until November 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537601 Project Executive, Site Management (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537601 Project Executive, Site Management (at the rank of Technical Officer/Research Assistant I/II) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537617/research-assistant-i-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-it-project-assistant": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/ II (holding the functional title of IT Project Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Research Assistant I/ II (holding the functional title of IT Project Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537617 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Chinese (04100) Categories: Research Staff, Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Research Assistant I/ II ( holding the functional title of IT Project Assistant) in the School of Chinese (Ref.: 537617) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Established in 1927, the School of Chinese at HKU holds a prestigious reputation as one of the University's earliest academic units and will celebrate its centenary in 2027. Visit our website at https://web.chinese.hku.hk for more information. To strengthen the School's technical support capacity, we are seeking a capable and proactive individual to join our administrative team. Applicants for the post of Research Assistant I should possess a Bachelor's degree or an approved qualification of equivalent standard. Applicants for the post of Research Assistant II should possess a Higher Diploma/Higher Certificate or an approved qualification of equivalent standard, or satisfy the University Entrance Requirements and have at least 3 years' relevant experience. The successful candidate should have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Cantonese and Putonghua, and relevant experience in website development (e.g. Wix and WordPress), photography and videography with editing skills, IT support, computer setup and troubleshooting, social media management, or related fields. Experience in website design and maintenance, desktop support, software and hardware configuration, and multimedia production will be an advantage. The candidate should be service-oriented, self-motivated, responsible, detail-minded, and able to work independently as well as collaboratively under tight deadlines. The appointee will support the School's IT operations in publicity, events, teaching and general administration. Duties include website development and maintenance, multi-media production and editing, audio-visual and videoconferencing support, digital content creation, user support and troubleshooting and maintenance of computers and related equipment. The appointee may be required to work outside normal office hours for events and will perform other duties as assigned. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written and/or practical test and an interview. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University's careers website ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 13, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. The Faculty of Arts expressly encourages qualified persons from all genders to apply. Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537617 Research Assistant I/ II (holding the functional title of IT Project Assistant) School of Chinese (04100) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537617 Research Assistant I/ II (holding the functional title of IT Project Assistant) School of Chinese (04100) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
