    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537659/postdoctoral-fellow-hku-stone-centre-on-socioeconomic-inequality-in-asia": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow (HKU Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Post-doctoral Fellow (HKU Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537659 Work type: Full-time Department: James M. and Cathleen D. Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia (30005) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow at the James M. and Cathleen D. Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia, jointly hosted by the Faculty of Social Sciences and the HKU Business School. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a one- to three-year temporary contract, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. About the Centre The James M. and Cathleen D. Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia at the University of Hong Kong is dedicated to the comparative study of income and wealth inequality in Asia. As the first Stone Centre in Asia, it connects researchers across disciplines and geographies to understand the nature, causes, and consequences of inequality, and to compare Asian experiences with those of North America and Europe. The Centre emphasises rigorous measurement, causal analysis, and clear communication of research findings. It is a joint initiative of the Faculty of Social Sciences and the Economics Department at HKU Business School, co-directed by Professor Tarani Chandola, Professor Uta Schönberg, and Professor Ming Wen. The Applicant We are seeking a highly motivated researcher with a PhD degree in economics or a related discipline, specialising in labour economics, trade, development, or political economy. The ideal candidate will have substantial experience working with large-scale datasets, including unstructured data such as LinkedIn data or job advertisements, as well as expertise in web crawling, large language models, and text analysis techniques. A strong understanding of causal inference methods is essential for developing rigorous research insights. Proficiency in both written and spoken English is required; proficiency in written and spoken Chinese is advantageous but not essential. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team is crucial. Key duties include conducting quantitative and qualitative data analyses, preparing manuscripts for publication in high-impact academic journals, and presenting research findings at research institutions and conferences. Fellows will be paired with a mentor from the Centre's leadership team for guidance and support. In addition, they will assist team leaders with project management tasks and contribute to the Centre's strategic planning and daily activities to ensure smooth operations. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, along with annual leave and medical benefits. Review of applications will begin as soon as possible and continue until January 15, 2027, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Inquiries about the post should be sent to stonecentre@hku.hk . The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 14, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 15, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537659 Post-doctoral Fellow (HKU Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia) James M. and Cathleen D. Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia (30005) Jan 15, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537659 Post-doctoral Fellow (HKU Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia) James M. and Cathleen D. Stone Centre on Socio-Economic Inequality in Asia (30005) Jan 15, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537611/executive-officer-in-the-division-of-periodontology-and-implant-dentistry": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Executive Officer in the Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537611 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer in the Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry of the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537611) We are looking for an Executive Officer to join the Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry of the Faculty of Dentistry. The Role The appointee will play a versatile role in leading junior clerical staff and providing comprehensive administrative support to the Division in a wide range of areas, including academic curriculum, research, clinical teaching, human resources management, financial administration, and secretarial support to the Division Chief and other professoriate staff, as well as performing other duties assigned by supervisors. Qualifications and Qualities A Bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years’ administrative experience, preferably gained in tertiary education institutions; Strong organisational, communication, analytical and problem-solving skills; A mature and proactive attitude with a strong sense of responsibility; Attentive to detail, self-motivated, and able to work independently; Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and other relevant software; An excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); Previous secretarial experience is preferred; and Experience in educational event management and a willingness to undertake related duties are advantageous. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University's careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 26, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 13, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537611 Executive Officer in the Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 26, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537611 Executive Officer in the Division of Periodontology and Implant Dentistry Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Oct 26, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537626/research-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537626 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref: 537626) (to commence as soon as possible for 6 - 12 months temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in psychology or any mental health-related discipline.  Previous research experience in clinical or health-related research projects and proficiency in statistical programming (e.g. R, preferably) are preferred.  The candidate should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Cantonese), proficiency in statistics, a strong commitment to high-quality research, strong organisational, communication, and interpersonal skills, strong analytical and problem-solving skills, and the ability to prioritise work and maintain a high level of effectiveness. Fresh graduates are welcome to apply. The appointee will coordinate psychiatric outreach services in response to a recent societal event and will work with Professor Eric TH Lai, social workers, and psychologists. He/She will also participate in research on electronic health care record studies on neurodevelopmental disorders, sleep research in youth with neurodevelopmental disorders and neuromodulation studies in internet gaming disorder. He/She will have access to clinical notes, conduct interviews, and recruit persons living with mental disorders. He/She will also assist with data analysis, proposal development, and research meetings, enhancing professional and communication skills. This is a full-time, onsite position. This position is ideal for those who want to gain research experience and clinical skills, gain exposure to both clinical and community settings, and contribute to serving survivors of a recent societal event and to academic research. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, along with annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. The review of applications will start on October 26, 2026, and continue until January 1, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 13, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 1, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537626 Research Assistant II Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Jan 1, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537626 Research Assistant II Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Jan 1, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537575/manager-student-outreach-masters-programmes-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Manager (Student Outreach), Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537575 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Manager (Student Outreach), Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537575) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a good bachelor’s degree, with at least 3 years of full-time work experience, preferably in tertiary institution, education sector or social service organization.  The ideal candidates should be a self-starter with a positive attitude; have a good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (fluency in Putonghua would be a definite advantage); and be able to multi-task, attentive to detail and work well both independently as well as in a team. Passion for working with youth and young adults would be an advantage. The appointee will provide support to the Faculty’s Masters Programmes Alumni and Student Services Team. This position is act as a Housemaster, working closely with the Assistant Director (Chief Housemaster) to cultivate an inclusive and engaged student community. The appointee will also be responsible for supporting and managing the Faculty’s AI Video Festival campaign, End of Module celebrations and related student engagement initiatives, including the planning and delivery of associated workshops in both online and physical formats. Key responsibilities include but not limited to: • overseeing daily operations, organizing outreach initiatives, and enhancing student bonding through collaboration with housemasters, vice housemasters, counsellors, and various stakeholders; • managing the overall Virtual House system, ensuring its effectiveness in promoting student engagement, cultural diversity, peer connection, and a strong sense of community among Master’s students; • planning, coordinating, and implementing the AI Video Festival campaign and related workshops (AI video production, digital storytelling, media creation), including promotion, recruitment, submission management, judging coordination, award arrangements, and post-event engagement; • planning and executing End of Module celebrations, regular house gatherings and  networking activities, to deepen connections among Master’s students; • supervising vice housemasters, providing support and guidance to help them achieve their goals and objectives; and • performing other duties as assigned. The appointee will work at the Faculty’s Cyberport campus, and may be required to work outside normal office hours and on weekends, and travel to overseas or Mainland China occasionally.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 2, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 13, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 2, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537575 Manager (Student Outreach), Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 2, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537575 Manager (Student Outreach), Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 2, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537602/research-assistant-iii-in-the-division-of-endocrinology-and-metabolism-of-the-department-of-medicine": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism of the Department of Medicine",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism of the Department of Medicine The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537602 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism of the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537602) We now invite applications for the captioned post. This post will provide an excellent opportunity to develop a research career involving advanced research in endocrinology and metabolism, on-the-job trainings will also be provided. Duties and Responsibilities Facilitate clinical research in the laboratory Handle various clinical specimens, coordinate biobank storages, and manage clinical database Perform other duties as assigned Requirements A Bachelor’s degree or above in Biomedical Sciences, Biology, Biochemistry, Public Health, Biostatistics or related disciplines A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese; ability to understand or communicate in Cantonese will be an advantage Familiar with MS Office application (including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.) Good organizational, communication and interpersonal skills Attentive to details, with a strong sense of responsibility, and self-motivated Able to work independently, and can contribute to a supportive team culture when working in a team environment Interest in pursuing postgraduate study (M.Phil. or Ph.D.) and/or with basic knowledge of biostatistics would be advantageous Those with lower qualifications or less experience may be considered for appointment as Research Assistant II, fresh graduates are welcomed What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 13, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537602 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism of the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537602 Research Assistant I/II in the Division of Endocrinology and Metabolism of the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
