    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537706/programme-manager-undergraduate-student-enrichment-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Programme Manager, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537706 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Programme Manager, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537706) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) The Undergraduate Student Enrichment team delivers a wide range of experiential learning opportunities that support students’ personal and professional development. These include student exchanges, case competitions, corporate partnerships, mentorship programmes, study trips, scholarships and prizes, and engagement with student associations. The team works closely with academic staff, external partners, and student bodies to enhance the undergraduate experience. Applicants should hold a good bachelor’s degree and have at least three years’ experience in programme management and/or development, preferably in a tertiary institution or the education sector. Excellent written and spoken English and Chinese (Putonghua and Cantonese) are essential. The successful candidate should be a collaborative team player with strong organisational and interpersonal skills, able to work independently and meet tight deadlines. Key attributes include a commitment to quality and results, excellent time management and problem solving skills, a professional demeanour, and high computer literacy. Experience in programmes/events management is an advantage. The appointee will be responsible for the coordination and delivery of the Faculty's undergraduate student enrichment and corporate partnership programmes. Duties include, but are not limited to, managing enrichment programmes, engaging and liaising with overseas institutions, corporate partners and other external parties; coordinating programmes and events with relevant stakeholders and students, supervising clerical staff, and performing any other duties as assigned. Occasional travel and work outside normal office hours may be required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537706 Programme Manager, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537706 Programme Manager, Underg