    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537732/clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-executive-assistant-in-the-graduate-school-of-the-research-services-of-the-registry": {
      "title": "Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537732 Work type: Full-time Department: Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry (60341) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry (Ref.: 537732) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should have 5 passes in HKCEE, including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, with at least 5 years’ relevant experience; OR a recognised Bachelor’s degree, with at least 1 year’s clerical/administrative experience preferably in tertiary institutions.  They should have a good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); IT proficiency; good interpersonal, communication, organisational and time management skills with initiative.  They should also have the ability to handle complex tasks; work independently; and be responsible, self-motivated and attentive to details. The appointees will provide clerical and administrative support to research postgraduate programmes including admissions, progress monitoring, thesis examinations, coursework, events, and any general administrative duties as assigned.  They may be required to work outside normal office hours.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537732 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry (60341) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537732 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry Graduate School of the Research Services of the Registry (60341) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
