    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537739/research-assistant-professor-in-the-department-of-social-work-and-social-administration-2-posts": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (2 posts)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (2 posts) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537739 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (Ref.: 537739), to commence as soon as possible, until 30 September 2028, on a temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. We are looking for someone with (1) a PhD in mental health, social work, psychology, health economics, or other related disciplines; (2) strong teamwork skills; (3) good leadership skills; and (4) good time management. Applicants should possess experience in postdoctoral research and project management within the field of mental health-related research, as well as an excellent academic publication record. Additionally, they should possess high proficiency in both written and spoken English and Chinese, including Cantonese. The position offers an excellent opportunity for academic publications, building research partnerships with international researchers and local mental health service providers, and learning the implementation of a mega mental health research project. The appointees will support the management of a large research team alongside the Project PI and managers. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV with supporting documents, a cover letter stating their background, and three references for the post applied.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 20 November 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537739 Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (2 posts) Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537739 Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Social Work and Social Administration (2 posts) Department of Social Work and Social Administration (30300) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537751/senior-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537751 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for the following post: Senior Research Assistant in the Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (to commence as soon as possible for two years, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in Biomedical Sciences, Life Sciences, Multi-omics, or a related discipline, with more than ten years of relevant research experience. A strong background in miRNA biology, circulating biomarkers, exosomes, and translational cancer research is essential. Applicants with at least five years of postdoctoral research experience, a proven publication record in peer-reviewed journals, and experience presenting research findings at major international conferences will have an advantage. The appointee will join a research team investigating cancer development and progression, with a particular focus on miRNA regulation, proteomic profiling, and circulating biomarkers for diagnosis, prognosis, and prediction of metastasis. He/She will conduct research on oncogenic and tumour-suppressor miRNAs and their downstream signalling pathways, investigate the functional roles of endogenous and extracellular (exosomal) miRNAs, perform proteomic profiling of oncogenes and tumour suppressors, and identify and validate circulating biomarkers associated with metastasis and clinical outcomes. The appointee will also assist in clinical sample collection and processing, maintain research databases and biobanking resources, support grant proposal preparation and laboratory management, contribute to manuscript preparation, and present research findings at scientific meetings. Applicants should possess strong organisational, coordination and problem-solving skills, be able to manage multiple concurrent tasks effectively, and demonstrate a high level of motivation and initiative. The ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a multidisciplinary research environment is essential. Opportunities for scientific authorship will be available where contributions merit. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on a two-year fixed-term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 20 November 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University places great emphasis on developing staff potential and has in place a variety of development opportunities and assistance for staff at different stages of their career. The University thanks applicants for their interest, but advises that only candidates shortlisted for interviews will be notified of the application result. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency. Advertised: Oct 26, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537751 Senior Research Assistant Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537751 Senior Research Assistant Department of Surgery, School of Clinical Medicine (21700) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
