    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537685/research-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Assistant Professor The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537685 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Research Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537685), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary basis or a two-to three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. We seek academic leaders and emerging scholars whose work advances the understanding and treatment of psychiatric disorders and improves mental and physical health outcomes. We welcome applicants from psychiatry and related fields, including psychiatric epidemiology, digital mental health, artificial intelligence and machine learning, and big data analytics. The shortlisted applicant(s) will be nominated for the Presidential Research Assistant Professor (RAP) Scheme of the University. Applicants should possess: (i) a Ph.D degree in psychiatry, psychology, public health, population health, data science, epidemiology, or a related discipline; and (ii) proven track record of impactful research, publications, external grants and leadership. Applicants are preferably within three years of their Ph.D graduation from top universities in the world and deemed to have almost reached the level of Assistant Professor. The appointee will join the team of Prof. Chang Wing Chung.  He/She is expected to conduct independent and collaborative research of high academic merit, and secure competitive external research funding (e.g., General Research Fund, Health and Medical Research Fund) to maintain an active research programme. He/She will contribute to supervising research postgraduate students. He/She will also undertake administrative and service duties as assigned. The Department offers a vibrant, collaborative environment with strong links to clinical services, community partners, and international research networks. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 15% of basic salary. In addition, the awardee of the Presidential RAP Scheme will be entitled to an annual research grant and annual conference support to be administered by the Faculty/Department. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload a one-page research abstract, a two-page research plan, including (i) background of research, (ii) research plan and methodology, and (iii) expected salary, and a two-page CV. Review of applications will start on November 6, 2026, and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537685 Research Assistant Professor Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537685 Research Assistant Professor Department of Psychiatry, School of Clinical Medicine (21500) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537710/project-executive-at-the-rank-of-technical-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Dentistry 1 Project Executive (at the rank of Technical Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537710 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Project Executive (at the rank of Technical Officer) in the Faculty of Dentistry (Ref.: 537710) We are looking for a Project Executive to join the Faculty of Dentistry. The Role The appointee will provide administrative and clerical support for the Faculty’s Continuing Professional Development (CPD) activities.  Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Managing and maintaining proper records of programme enrolment and participant attendance; Liaising with other CPD providers and accreditation panel members; Keeping abreast of the specific reporting mechanism of the Dental Council of Hong Kong for all CPD activities; Coordinating programme logistics and providing on-site support, including reception services, venue set-up, equipment arrangements and programme materials dissemination; Handling enquiries and following up on post-event matters with participants; Supporting the content management of apps, social media, websites and other Faculty communication platforms; Preparing budgets, processing payments and keeping accurate financial records; Preparing promotional materials to publicise CPD activities through websites, emails, posters and other Faculty channels; and Performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities A recognized Bachelor’s degree; OR 5 passes in HKCEE including English (minimum Grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics OR minimum Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSEE including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics, with at least 5 years’ relevant work experience, preferably gained in tertiary institutions or the education sector; A good command of spoken and written English and Chinese; Good computer literacy; Attention to detail and excellent organizational skills; Capability to prioritize multiple tasks and meet tight deadlines; Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a collaborative and self-motivated work ethic; and Experience in database and website management is preferred. Work outside regular office hours (including evenings and weekends) may be required for duty-related events/activities. What We Offer The appointment will be made on temporary full-time contract for 1 year, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered.  Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 5, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 5, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537710 Project Executive (at the rank of Technical Officer) Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Nov 5, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537710 Project Executive (at the rank of Technical Officer) Faculty of Dentistry (08000) Nov 5, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
