    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537573/clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-executive-assistant-clerical-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) /Clerical Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) /Clerical Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537573 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong 香港大學生物醫學學院 招聘 二級文員 （職銜為行政助理）／文員助理 ( 參考編號： 537573 ） （盡快到任，合約期為兩年；設合約期滿酬金及大學退休福利計劃提存，總額最高可達基本薪金的 10%；若資金充裕及工作表現令人滿意，可獲考慮續約） 本校生物醫學學院「知識交流及全球事務團隊」現誠聘一位具同理心、熱誠及主動積極的人士，為「香港大學『大體老師』遺體捐贈計劃」提供行政支援。若您待人誠懇有耐心，並具備自主靈活的工作態度，歡迎申請上述職位，共同推動這項充滿社會意義的大學計劃。 申請人須於香港中學會考（HKCEE）取得 5 科合格（包括英文科；2007 年前課程甲須達 C 級或 2007 年起達第 2 級），或於香港中學文憑考試（HKDSE）取得 5 科達第 2 級或以上（包括英國語文科），並具備最少兩年工作經驗。持有社會工作或社會科學文憑，或具備殯儀服務、火化服務或心理輔導經驗者獲優先考慮。資歷較低及／或經驗較少者，可獲考慮聘任為文書助理職位。 本職位主要於辦公室工作，惟因應公眾活動、參訪或傳媒採訪需求，受聘者偶爾須前往解剖實驗室，並能坦然面對生死議題以及接觸「大體老師」（遺體）與解剖標本。 申請人須具備優秀的中英文書寫及口語能力，能按不同情境靈活修訂及撰寫信件與電郵範本；並熟練掌握電腦及常用軟件（包括 MS Word、Excel、PowerPoint 及中文輸入法）。申請人亦須具備良好的溝通技巧與責任感，能根據既定指引，有條不紊地獨立處理日常運作及跟進個案。資歷或經驗較次者，可獲考慮聘任為文員助理。 受聘者須具備良好的電話禮儀及行政處理能力，並能展現高度主動性，密切跟進各個個案進度，預先評估營運需求並妥善完成各項行政程序。 受聘者主要負責本計劃的核心行政工作，包括：處理捐贈登記及相關行政手續；以耐心與關懷解答公眾及家屬的電話與電郵查詢（特別是引導長者及家屬了解捐贈程序與善後安排）；及時跟進具時效性的個案；協助舉辦「港大遺體捐贈日」等公眾教育活動，以及維護資料庫及相關紀錄。此外，受聘者亦須以尊重與同理心，與教學團隊、喪親家屬及殯儀業者等內部與外部持份者保持良好溝通與協調。 入圍申請人將獲邀參加筆試及面試。 本校將按受聘者的資歷及經驗提供具競爭力的薪酬，另設有薪年假及醫療福利。 本校只接受網上申請。申請人須登入大學招聘網站（ https://jobs.hku.hk ）提交網上申請，並上載最新履歷。申請審查將於2026年11月5日開始，並持續進行至 2026年12月22日 ，或直至職位填補為止（以較早者為準）。 Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) /Clerical Assistant in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537573) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) The Knowledge Exchange & Global team in the School of Biomedical Sciences is looking for a compassionate, dedicated, and proactive team member to provide administrative support for the HKU Body Donation Programme. If you approach people with warmth and empathy, while bringing a self-motivated, resourceful mindset to your work, we would love to welcome you. Applicants should possess 5 passes in HKCEE including English (min. Grade C if Syllabus A / Level 2 from 2007), OR min. Level 2 in 5 subjects in HKDSE including English Language, with at least 2 years’ work experience. Preference will be given to those with a diploma in Social Work or Social Sciences, or experience in funeral services, cremation operations, or counselling. Those with lower qualifications and/or less experience will be considered for the post of Clerical Assistant. While the post is primarily office-based, candidates must be comfortable with occasional visits to the Anatomy Dissection Laboratory during public education events, visits, or media activities, which involves handling life-and-death matters and exposure to anatomical specimens and cadavers. You should have an excellent command of written and spoken Chinese and English, including the ability to adapt template letters and emails to fit specific donor situations; strong communication and interpersonal skills; and proficiency in PC and various software applications including MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Chinese word processing. We seek a reliable team player who can independently handle daily routines and follow through on donor cases using good judgment and established guidelines. Candidates with less experience and/or lower qualifications may be appointed as Clerical Assistant. You are expected to handle administrative processes efficiently with good phone etiquette. You should demonstrate high initiative—anticipating operational needs, closely monitoring pending cases, and ensuring prompt follow-through to keep administrative procedures moving forward seamlessly. The appointee will handle core administrative procedures for the Programme, including managing donor records, handling phone and email enquiries with patience and care (particularly when guiding elderly callers and family members through donation procedures and post-death involvement), and ensuring prompt follow-through on time-sensitive donor cases. You will also assist with public education events (such as the annual HKU Body Donation Day), maintain accurate databases, and liaise with internal and external stakeholders, such as the School's Body Donation and Anatomy Education team, bereaved families, and funeral undertakers, with respect and empathy. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. You should apply online at the University's career site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start from November 5, 2026 and continue until December 22, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 22, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537686/marketing-manager-masters-programmes-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Marketing Manager, Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537686 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Marketing Manager, Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref: 537686) (to commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) HKU Business School Masters Programmes is seeking a high-calibre individual to join the team as Marketing Manager. The appointee will play a versatile role in planning, implementing, and executing marketing strategies for our specialised Master's Programmes including Accounting, Accounting Analytics, Artificial Intelligence in Business, Business Analytics, Economics, Family Wealth Management, Finance, Fintech, Global Management, Marketing, Sustainable Accounting and Finance, and Wealth Management. The ideal candidate holds a bachelor’s degree, preferably in Marketing, Communications, Journalism, or a related field, and possesses over five years of proven experience in brand building, marketing campaign management, digital marketing, content marketing, or external communications. They should have strong proficiency in both spoken and written English and Chinese, including Putonghua and Cantonese, and demonstrate a successful track record in managing social media channels. Hands-on experience with various digital marketing tools and platforms is essential. The candidate must be able to work independently as well as collaboratively in a fast-paced environment, effectively handling multiple tasks and prioritizing ad hoc requests. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills are required for working with cross-functional teams. Experience in a digital marketing agency is preferred, and familiarity with international tertiary education would be an advantage. The role involves leading the content planning and development process across multiple platforms, including but not limited to Facebook, Instagram, WeChat and Rednote, to ensure high-quality output and consistent brand messaging. The incumbent will manage website and brochure content to keep all materials up to date, while staying informed about the latest digital marketing trends, technologies, and best practices across relevant markets. This position requires close coordination with internal teams, external vendors, and partners to ensure timely and effective campaign launches. The candidate will also be responsible for managing digital marketing budgets and allocating resources across various campaigns and channels. In addition, they will take part in ad-hoc projects and other duties assigned by the Director. The appointee will work at the Faculty’s Cyberport campus, and may occasionally require working outside normal office hours, including weekends, and traveling outside Hong Kong when necessary. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 12, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 12, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537686 Marketing Manager, Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 12, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537686 Marketing Manager, Masters Programmes (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 12, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537704/senior-executive-assistantexecutive-assistant-undergraduate-student-enrichment-at-the-rank-of-clerk-iii": {
      "title": "Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk I/II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk I/II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537704 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk I/II) in the Faculty of Business and Economics (Ref.: 537704) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) The Undergraduate Student Enrichment team delivers a wide range of experiential learning opportunities that support students’ personal and professional development. These include student exchanges, case competitions, corporate partnerships, mentorship programmes, study trips, scholarships and prizes, and engagement with student associations. The team works closely with academic staff, external partners, and student bodies to enhance the undergraduate experience. Applicants should hold a bachelor’s degree and have at least 2 years’ full time work experience in administration or student affairs, preferably in a tertiary institution or the education sector. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (proficiency in Putonghua would be an advantage); strong interpersonal, organisational, communication and problem solving skills; good computer literacy; and the ability to multitask under pressure and work both independently and as part of a team, with a strong sense of responsibility. Attention to detail, particularly with data compilation, is essential. Candidates with lower qualifications and/or less experience may be considered for the post of Clerk II. The appointee will provide administrative and clerical support for the Faculty’s undergraduate student enrichment programmes. Duties include, but are not limited to, coordinating events, activities, and study tours; maintaining databases; liaising with students and internal/external stakeholders; performing data entry; and supporting general administration within the Undergraduate Student Enrichment Team. Occasional travel and work outside normal office hours may be required. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 12, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 12, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537704 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 12, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537704 Senior Executive Assistant/Executive Assistant, Undergraduate Student Enrichment (at the rank of Clerk I/II) Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Nov 12, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
