    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537724/parttime-research-assistant-iii-12-positions": {
      "title": "Part-time Research Assistant I/II (1–2 positions)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Part-time Research Assistant I/II (1–2 positions) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537724 Work type: Hourly-paid Department: Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part-time Research Assistant I/II (1–2 positions) in the Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (TALIC) (Ref.: 537724) (to commence as soon as possible for six months) We are looking for 1–2 Part-time Research Assistants (RA I/II) to support large-scale research projects related to teacher and student interviews in higher education. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will support the coordination and implementation of large-scale interview studies. Major responsibilities include: Coordinating teacher and student interview invitations, scheduling, and organization ; Supporting the recruitment, interview, and training of student research helpers ; Assisting with the development and administration of an interview management platform ; and Providing other research and administrative support as required. The appointee is expected to work approximately 7-15 hours per week . Requirements Applicants should: Be currently enrolled in a Master’s degree programme at The University of Hong Kong, preferably in Education, Psychology, or a related discipline; Have experience in research projects, preferably in the higher education sector ; Have an excellent command of written and spoken English ; Possess strong organisational, communication, and time-management skills ; Be proactive, outgoing, responsible, and self-motivated; Be able to work both independently and collaboratively as an effective team member; and Be proficient in commonly used productivity, scheduling, calendar, spreadsheet, and document-management software . This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to large-scale educational research in a supportive environment that values innovation, teamwork, and professional development . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until 20 November 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. For enquiries about the position, please feel free to contact Ms. Artemis Fung, at artemisf@hku.hk . Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537724 Part-time Research Assistant I/II (1–2 positions) Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537724 Part-time Research Assistant I/II (1–2 positions) Teaching and Learning Innovation Centre (47500) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537726/assistant-research-officerresearch-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537726 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537726), to commence as soon as possible on a one-year temporary basis or a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. We are recruiting an Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer to join an antiviral drug discovery project focused on developing small-molecule approaches to target conserved viral RNA elements. Requirements Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree and have at least 3 years of relevant postdoctoral research experience working on related projects. Prior experience in virology is preferred. They should demonstrate excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a proven ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in medicinal chemistry, chemical biology, RNA structural biology, RNA–small molecule interactions, computational chemistry, cheminformatics, or AI-assisted virtual drug screening. Experience in RNA-targeted therapeutics, molecular docking, RNA binding assays, structure–activity relationship analysis, or computational drug discovery would be highly advantageous. Duties The appointee will contribute to viral RNA target analysis, RNA structure modeling, virtual screening, compound prioritization, small-molecule design, assay development, and early-stage drug discovery. He/She will lead and execute end-to-end research projects in RNA-targeted therapeutics, antiviral drug discovery, medicinal chemistry, RNA structural biology, computational drug screening. He/She will design and implement translational research strategies and also conduct biostatistical analysis to interpret experimental data.  He/She will be expected to collaborate closely with colleagues, proactively share knowledge, and consistently deliver high-quality results in a fast-paced and deadline-driven research environment. The appointee will work mainly in the Hong Kong Science Park but occasionally in HKU. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 15% of basic salary for Research Officer; 10% of basic salary for Assistant Research Officer. Housing benefits will also be provided to Research Officer as applicable. How to apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start from November 9, 2026 and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537726 Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537726 Assistant Research Officer/Research Officer Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537729/research-assistant-ii-in-the-faculty-of-arts": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II in the Faculty of Arts",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Arts 1 Research Assistant II in the Faculty of Arts The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537729 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Faculty of Arts (04000) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant II in the Faculty of Arts (Ref: 537729) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term (fractional 60%) basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Faith and Global Engagement (FGE) is an initiative at the University of Hong Kong (HKU) which seeks to demonstrate the positive impacts and overall importance of faith in society, both locally and globally. While the FGE represents the Christian tradition in dialogue with the contemporary world, it also aids understanding of religion and spirituality in general, as the pluralistic setting of Hong Kong hosts the largely secular microcosm of HKU. Qualifications Applicants should have a recognised degree. Key Responsibilities The appointee will play a pivotal role in embedding professional career coaching and programme excellence into FGE's mentorship and student engagement portfolio. The role is designed with core objectives: deliver high-impact career and life coaching to students within the FGE community, supporting students' self-understanding, decision-making, and whole-person development; provide strategic leadership in programme design, quality assurance, and project management for FGE's flagship initiatives, including \"The Way To Success\" (TWTS) Mentorship Programme and Lead for Life; mentor the developing FGE career development team and facilitate succession planning to build long-term team sustainability; and carry out related administrative tasks for FGE programmes and courses as part of FGE's administrative team. The appointee will also be responsible for the following duties: provide professional coaching and student empowerment; design programs and manage projects; facilitate synergy and engage stakeholders; and mentor within FGE’s career development team and contribute to succession planning. What We offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment on fixed term will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will continue until October 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 29, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537729 Research Assistant II in the Faculty of Arts Faculty of Arts (04000) Oct 29, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537729 Research Assistant II in the Faculty of Arts Faculty of Arts (04000) Oct 29, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537731/part-time-senior-research-assistant-research-assistant-iii": {
      "title": "Part Time Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I/II",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Hourly-paid 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Education 1 Part Time Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I/II The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537731 Work type: Hourly-paid Department: Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Part Time Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I/II in the Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education. (Ref.: 537731) To commence as soon as possible until 30 June 2027. Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in Education, Psychology or related disciplines within Social Science. They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Cantonese), good communication, IT and organization skills, and experience in conducting qualitative and/or quantitative research. Preference will be given to those with foundational research skills (e.g. conducting interview, and analyzing qualitative data with N-vivo and quantitative data using R, SPSS, Mplus, etc.). Having relevant work experience in educational research projects or project management skills such as coordination, communication, and documentation, will be an advantage. Those with less experience may be considered as Research Assistant I/II. The appointee will assist the project team with conducting visits, literature review, surveys, interviews, data collection and analysis. They will also be expected to organize project events and perform other duties as assigned. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537731 Part Time Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I/II Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537731 Part Time Senior Research Assistant / Research Assistant I/II Centre for Information Technology in Education within the Faculty of Education (10001) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537736/ai-engineer": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Law 1 AI Engineer The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537736 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Law (18100) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong AI Engineer (at the rank of Research Assistant I or II) in the Faculty of Law (Ref.: 537736) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance) Note: Candidates who have previously applied for position ref. 537095 will automatically be considered and do not need to reapply. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree or above in Computer Science or a related field, along with: Proven experience as a full-stack Web Developer. Proficiency in TypeScript/JavaScript and Python (Flask). Hands-on experience with Vercel AI SDK, Model Context Protocol, and agent tool calls. Strong experience with PostgreSQL and Prisma ORM. Familiarity with Azure Cloud Services and Azure OpenAI API. Knowledge of web servers and deployment (Apache, Gunicorn). The appointee will join an interdisciplinary team from the Faculty of Law and the School of Computing and Data Science on a project integrating legal research, teaching and learning, community engagement, and AI development. Responsibilities will include: Design, develop, and deploy a next-generation AI application utilizing Vercel AI SDK, MCP, and agent tool calling. Model, query, and manage databases using Prisma ORM and PostgreSQL. Integrate and deploy cloud AI solutions via Azure Cloud Services (including Azure OpenAI API). Maintain and support existing web applications (Python/Flask). A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 30 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 23, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537736 AI Engineer Faculty of Law (18100) Oct 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537736 AI Engineer Faculty of Law (18100) Oct 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537443/fulltime-research-assistant-i-or-ii-senior-research-assistant": {
      "title": "Full-time Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Full-time Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537443 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Psychology (30200) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow, Research Staff Hong Kong We now invite applications for the captioned post. Full-time Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant in the Department of Psychology (Ref.: 537443) Applications are invited for the position of Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant in the Department of Psychology, for the Child and School Psychology Laboratory, to commence in November  2026, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. The Role The appointee will provide independent support to research projects and related academic activities. Key responsibilities include: Conducting literature reviews and synthesizing research findings Developing research materials, resources, and programme content Managing research data, performing statistical analysis, and preparing reports Monitoring project progress and ensuring timelines are met Supervising junior research staff (for Senior Research Assistant level) and coordinating day-to-day project operations Assisting in the preparation of manuscripts, presentations, and other research outputs Supporting other research-related activities as needed Requirements Applicants should possess: A Bachelor's degree in Psychology, Social Sciences, Education, or a related discipline. For Senior Research Assistant: at least 3 years of relevant post-qualification experience, or a Master’s degree with at least 1 year of experience, or a Ph.D. degree. Demonstrable ability to independently manage research tasks and supervise junior staff (for Senior level). Excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint). Familiarity with SPSS or other statistical analysis software is preferred. For Research Assistant I/II: relevant experience or skills in research support activities. For Research Assistant I/II: good knowledge of Microsoft Excel, with English word processing speed of at least 50 w.p.m. and Chinese at least 30 w.p.m. are preferred. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications . Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV and detailed academic transcripts. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537443 Full-time Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant Department of Psychology (30200) Nov 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537443 Full-time Research Assistant I or II / Senior Research Assistant Department of Psychology (30200) Nov 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
