    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537673/data-scientist-data-coordinator-at-the-rank-of-senior-technical-officer-technical-officer-in-the-division-of-community-medicine-and-public-health-practice-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537673 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537673) (to commence as soon as possible, on a one-year temporary basis or two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree in data management, statistics, computer science, information systems, public health, or a related discipline; a master’s degree will be an advantage. They should have proven experience in data cleaning and quality assurance, as well as in preparing technical documentation and data reports while managing workflows in a multi-stakeholder environment. Practical expertise with data platforms and tools is highly valued, including SQL databases, Excel or Google Sheets, and data capture systems such as REDCap, ODK, SurveyCTO, or Qualtrics; familiarity with visualization/reporting tools such as Power BI or Tableau is advantageous.  Proficiency in programming or scripting languages commonly used for data processing, such as R, SAS, Stata and Python, is desirable. Knowledge of data protection principles and compliance frameworks, along with a foundational understanding of statistical methods and data analytics principles will be beneficial. Applicants should be highly organized, detail-oriented, proactive, and possesses strong problem-solving skills. Excellent communication abilities are required to convey technical information to non-technical audiences and to build trusted relationships across teams. Leadership, mentoring capabilities, and a commitment to ethical data practices are important in a fast-paced project environment. The appointee will assist the Data Manager in overseeing the end-to-end data lifecycle across multiple projects, ensuring that data collection, processing, validation, storage, and reporting meet high standard. This role is crucial in maintaining data integrity and ensuring compliance with organizational policies and regulations. Key responsibilities include: designing and refining data management workflows; monitoring data quality, running validation checks and troubleshoot discrepancies; maintaining comprehensive documentation (e.g., data dictionaries, operational procedures, instruction manuals, data capture guidelines) and establish audit trails; supporting database administration, coaching data entry and processing teams; providing training on tools and procedures; preparing operational dashboards and data summaries for various internal and external stakeholders; collaborating closely with IT or platform vendors to address technical issues, as well as with project managers, analysts, and researchers, convert data requirements into practical solutions while ensuring adherence to data protection and security standards. Enquiries about the duties of the post should be sent to Ms Cynthia Yau at cynthyau@hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical/dental benefits. The appointment on fixed terms will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536804) need not re-reapply. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until January 22, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 22, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537673 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Jan 22, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537673 Data Scientist/ Data Coordinator (at the rank of Senior Technical Officer/ Technical Officer) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Jan 22, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537679/tenuretrack-associate-professorassistant-professor-2-posts-in-the-school-of-biological-sciences": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (2 posts) in the School of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Science 1 Tenure-Track Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (2 posts) in the School of Biological Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537679 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biological Sciences (26000) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-Track Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (2 posts) in the School of Biological Sciences (Ref.: 537679), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract. Applicants should be innovative scholars with a growing or established international record of research excellence in Marine Science and Conservation . They should possess a Ph.D. in Marine Science, Conservation Biology, Environmental Policy, Ecological Economics, or a closely related field, and demonstrate a strong research focus in contemporary marine conservation. Preferred areas include, but not limited to: marine restoration and bio-inspired coastal defense, blue carbon science and climate mitigation, marine natural capital and ecosystem services, conservation finance and the blue economy, sustainable mariculture and fisheries, marine spatial planning, and transboundary governance. A proven track record—commensurate with rank—of securing competitive research funding and publishing high-impact research is essential. Particular expertise and research experience focused on Greater China, East Asia, and/or Southeast Asia are required. Appointees will be key members of The Swire Institute of Marine Science (SWIMS) at the University, developing independent, world-class research programmes, mentoring students, and contributing to teaching at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Successful candidates will also engage with regional marine protection networks, cross-sector coalitions, and initiatives supported by the Swire Group Charitable Trust focused on marine conservation, restoration, and the sustainable use of marine resources across the region. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave, professional leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totaling up to 15% of basic salary. Housing benefits will be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V., a cover letter, a research statement, a teaching statement, and contact information of three referees. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until March 31, 2027 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Mar 31, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537679 Tenure-Track Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (2 posts) in the School of Biological Sciences School of Biological Sciences (26000) Mar 31, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537679 Tenure-Track Associate Professor/Assistant Professor (2 posts) in the School of Biological Sciences School of Biological Sciences (26000) Mar 31, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
