    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537691/postdoctoral-fellow-in-the-department-of-medicine": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Medicine",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Medicine The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537691 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the Division of Gastroenterology & Hepatology of the Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.:537691) We now invite applications for the captioned post. This post provides a good opportunity for professional growth by close collaboration with the Research Lead as well as excellent practical experience in the fields of medicine and biotechnology. Duties and Responsibilities Perform wet-lab experiments, coordinate projects, manage and analyse data, liaise and collaborate with various parties Perform administrative tasks and other duties as assigned Requirements A Ph.D. degree in a STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics)-related discipline A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese Excellent communication skills Ability to multi-task and work independently as well as in a team Previous clinical research experience will be preferable What We Offer The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a temporary basis for one year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will on start from November 5, 2026 and continue until November 21, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 21, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537691 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 21, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537691 Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Medicine Department of Medicine, School of Clinical Medicine (20600) Nov 21, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537697/assistant-manager-at-the-rank-of-executive-officer": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537697 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Social Sciences Research Centre (SSRC) of the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref: 537697) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance). The Social Sciences Research Centre (SSRC) advances methodological research and training within the social sciences through research, training and knowledge exchange. The Centre is seeking a highly organised, proactive and responsible individual to support its administration and operations, with particular responsibility for coordinating training programmes, seminars, workshops, conferences and other Centre activities. Applicants should possess a Bachelor’s degree, preferably with at least 4 to 6 years of relevant work experience in tertiary education institutions, research centres, training organisations or a similar setting. They should be effective communicators with an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, including Putonghua. The ideal candidate should demonstrate strong interpersonal, organisational and problem-solving skills, keen attention to detail, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively, manage multiple tasks, and meet tight deadlines. Experience in organising academic or professional training programmes, executive education, conferences, seminars, public engagement activities or study tours would be an advantage. The appointee will collaborate closely with the Co-Directors and management team to implement and oversee the operations of the Centre. They will serve as a versatile administrator, providing comprehensive support in human resources, financial management, committee secretarial duties, and general office administration. The appointee will also assist in organising the Centre’s research and knowledge exchange events and activities; liaise with and coordinate project collaborators and stakeholders; prepare event and promotional materials, including through the use of digital design and generative AI tools where appropriate; and perform any other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and written test. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 20, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 20, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537697 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 20, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537697 Assistant Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 20, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537700/research-nurse-at-the-rank-of-nurse": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537700 Work type: Full-time Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 537700) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies.  HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession. HKU-CTC’s Phase 1 Clinical Trials Unit (Phase 1 Unit) is a professional clinical trials facility located at the Queen Mary Hospital and dedicated to conducting phase 1 and early phase clinical trials.  We are seeking a high calibre talent who have the passion in promoting healthcare advancement through practising clinical research to join our Phase 1 Unit as a Research Nurse. Main Responsibilities: Be responsible to clinical trial coordination and operations; Conduct study planning and management; Recruit trial volunteers; Execute study procedures, data collection and documents management, medical emergency management, facilities management and quality management; Communicate with research teams and internal/external collaborators; and Perform other duties as assigned. Require to work outside normal business days or hours occasionally. Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Nursing; Registered with the Nursing Council of Hong Kong; A minimum of 1 year’s nursing experience is preferred; Holder of a Basic Life Support (BLS) / Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support (ACLS) certificate and a venipuncture certificate is an advantage; Experience in clinical trial operations and basic knowledge in Good Clinical Practice are added advantages; Experience in utilization of electronic devices (e.g., tablets, computers) for efficient and accurate clinical data capture are added advantages; Good interpersonal and communication skills; Good coordination and problem-solving skills, and commitment to quality and compliance; Detail-minded, able to multitask, and self-motivated; and Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (Both Cantonese & Mandarin). Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview.  Those who have responded to the previous advertisements (Ref.: 537292) need not re-apply. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on a 1-year temporary basis or 2-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Appointment on 2-year fixed term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Application Procedure: The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will begin from November 5, 2026 and continue until November 21, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 21, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537700 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 21, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537700 Research Nurse (at the rank of Nurse) Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 21, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537714/parttime-lecturer-in-geography-in-the-faculty-of-social-sciences-ref-537714": {
      "title": "Part-time Lecturer in Geography in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537714)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Part-time Lecturer in Geography in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537714) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537714 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Department of Geography (30900) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Part-time Lecturer in Geography in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537714) We now invite applications for appointment as Part-time Lecturer in the Department of Geography within the Faculty of Social Sciences. Duties and Responsibilities The appointee will be responsible for teaching an elective course themed at “Land and Housing in China” for the Master of China Development Studies (MChDS) programme. Requirements Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in geography, economics, urban planning, management, businesses studies or related discipline, with expertise in the context of China. Preference will be given to applicants with prior teaching experience in tertiary institutions and/or post-qualification working experience in relevant professional or academic settings. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a part-time basis for six months commencing either on 1 January 2027, renewable subject to mutual agreement and good performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. including the contact information of three referees. More information about the Department of Geography can be found at https://www.geog.hku.hk/ . Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until 30 November, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537714 Part-time Lecturer in Geography in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537714) Department of Geography (30900) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537714 Part-time Lecturer in Geography in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref.: 537714) Department of Geography (30900) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537727/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537727 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (Ref.: 537727), to commence as soon as possible for one to two years, with the possibility of renewal subject to funding availability and satisfactory performance. This post mainly works in Science Park but occasionally work in HKU. Requirements Applicants should possess a Ph.D. degree in medicinal chemistry, chemical biology, RNA biology, computational chemistry, or a related discipline. They should demonstrate excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a proven ability to work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate closely with colleagues, proactively share knowledge, and consistently deliver high-quality results in a fast-paced and deadline-driven research environment. We are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in medicinal chemistry, chemical biology, RNA structural biology, RNA–small molecule interactions, computational chemistry, cheminformatics, or AI-assisted virtual drug screening . Experience in RNA-targeted therapeutics, molecular docking, RNA binding assays, structure–activity relationship analysis, or computational drug discovery would be highly advantageous. Duties The appointee will join an antiviral drug discovery project focused on developing small-molecule approaches to target conserved viral RNA elements. He/She will contribute to viral RNA target analysis, RNA structure modeling, virtual screening, compound prioritization, small-molecule design, assay development, and early-stage drug discovery. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 22, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537727 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Dec 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537727 Post-doctoral Fellow Department of Microbiology, School of Clinical Medicine (20700) Dec 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537676/assistant-registraradministrative-assistant-i-several-posts-in-the-division-of-community-medicine-and-public-health-practice-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537676 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537676), to commence as soon as possible, on a two- to three-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Application should possess a good first Bachelor’s degree, with relevant academic and professional training related to the areas of duties and/or recognized professional qualifications, plus at least 8 to 10 year’s professional experience in a public/quasi-public organization or a related sector, preferably with a higher degree.  They should have an excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese, be mature and meticulous, self-motivated, and a good team player with excellent organisational and interpersonal skills and be able to work on their own initiative.  Commitment to quality and results, excellent time management and problem-solving skills, professional work attitude and a high level of computer literacy are essential qualities for the post. Applicants with less experience may be considered for appointment as Administrative Assistant I. The appointee will work to support a large team focused on population mental health projects and mental wellbeing in Hong Kong. He/She will play a central role in managing financial operations, and coordinating human resources activities, ensuring timely reporting, streamlining procedures, and maintaining strong stakeholder relationships. The role also involves managing procurement, budgeting, and financial reporting, handling grants and donations and collaborating with internal and external teams to support project execution. In addition to project and financial oversight, the appointee is responsible for HR administration, including recruitment, onboarding, promotions, and visa processing. The role requires mentoring junior staff, resolving operational challenges, and maintaining efficient office logistics. The position demands adaptability, strategic thinking, and strong communication skills to support the team’s mission and ensure smooth administrative operations. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. Housing benefits will be provided for the Assistant Registrar rank. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 536805) need not re-reapply. The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until January 22, 2027 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Jan 22, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537676 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Jan 22, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537676 Assistant Registrar/Administrative Assistant I (several posts) in the Division of Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Jan 22, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537698/postdoctoral-fellow": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow 1 Faculty Faculty of Engineering 1 Post-doctoral Fellow The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537698 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Civil Engineering (14100) Categories: Senior Research Staff & Post-doctoral Fellow Hong Kong Post-doctoral Fellow in the Department of Civil Engineering (Several Posts) (Ref.: 537698), to commence as soon as possible for 1 year, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. We now invite applications for the captioned posts. This post will provide an excellent opportunity to develop a research career involving advanced research in smart construction and transportation engineering. On-the-job training will also be provided. Duties and Responsibilities (1) Common Responsibilities All appointees will be required to conduct literature review, collect and analyze user requirements in safe and efficient transportation, and contribute to system engineering design. (2) Research Areas In addition to the common responsibilities above, each appointee will undertake research in one of the following four areas , selected according to their research interests and expertise: IoT research and development, including sensor integration and communication improvement. Mechanism research and algorithm development for real-time monitoring and early warning to enhance the transportation safety of large construction components. Mechanism research and algorithm development for cargo stability monitoring in the transportation of large construction components. Mechanism research and algorithm development for just-in-time fleet coordination in the transportation of large construction components. Requirements PhD degree in Civil Engineering, Transportation Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong publication and project experience in one or more of the research areas specified under Duties and Responsibilities. Ability to conduct field tests, undertake independent research and collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams. Attentive to detail, with a strong sense of responsibility, and self-motivated. What We Offer A leading research environment focused on real-time safe driving and fleet management for large construction components transportation. Opportunities to conduct internationally competitive research and applications. Support for publication, conference participation, and career development. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above posts. Applicants should apply online at the University’s Careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until December 31, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Sear