    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537636/fractional-clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-executive-assistant-in-the-joint-universities-computer-centre-jucc": {
      "title": "Fractional Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Fractional Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537636 Work type: Fractional / Part-time Department: Information Technology Services (40000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Fractional Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC) (Ref.: 537636) The Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC) Limited (http://www.jucc.edu.hk) is located in Information Technology Services.  Incorporated in 1970, the JUCC is a cooperative effort of the Computing/Information Technology Services Centres of the eight government-funded tertiary institutions in Hong Kong.  Being the consortium of the tertiary institutions of Hong Kong, the JUCC has a long history of inter-institutional collaboration in the development and application of IT in the higher education community, contributing to education and the development of IT in Hong Kong. The Role The appointee will provide administrative, operational and logistical support to the JUCC Office. The primary focus will be on committee operations, event coordination and cross-institutional liaison in a multi-institution higher-education environment. Key responsibilities include: providing administrative and logistical support for JUCC events, activities and committee meetings, including scheduling, registration, venue arrangements, attendance tracking, agenda preparation and on-the-day support; liaising with participating universities, vendors and other relevant stakeholders to coordinate arrangements and manage enquiries; supporting operations through the preparation, compilation, and handling of relevant documents, records, returns, and well-organised reports and summaries for management review; handling general enquiries and maintaining records and information using online systems and office tools; and performing other duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities A Higher Diploma or above, preferably with relevant experience in event management or administration A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) A strong sense of responsibility, with a self-motivated attitude and attention to detail Ability to handle multiple tasks and work under stress to meet tight deadlines Good interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work both independently and as part of a team Willingness to learn and take on new tasks as required Experience in providing event support and liaising with different universities would be an advantage Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term contract for 2 years on a fractional (50%) basis, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site (https://jobs.hku.hk) and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 4 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 4, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537636 Fractional Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC) Information Technology Services (40000) Nov 4, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537636 Fractional Clerk II (holding the functional title of Executive Assistant) in the Joint Universities Computer Centre (JUCC) Information Technology Services (40000) Nov 4, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537693/research-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Research Assistant I",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Architecture 1 Research Assistant I The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537693 Work type: Full-time Department: Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Categories: Research Staff Hong Kong Research Assistant I in the Department of Real Estate and Construction (Ref.: 537693) We now invite applications for the captioned post. The candidate will work with a team of researchers led by Professor Arnab Dutta, which includes Dr Sahil Gandhi (University of Manchester) and Professor Jan Brueckner (UC Irvine), on a project that investigates regulatory changes in Indian cities. The position will require processing large survey datasets and executing standard quasi-experimental research designs like difference-in-difference. The candidate will report directly to Professor Arnab Dutta. Duties and Responsibilities Processing large survey datasets; Creating visuals (figures and charts) for descriptive statistics; Executing applied econometric models, such as difference-in-difference; and Using geospatial techniques to integrate observational data with survey datasets. Requirements Bachelor’s degree with at least 2 years of experience or a master’s degree, preferably in Urban Economics, Urban Studies or Planning, Real Estate, or Finance; Expertise in Stata; Working knowledge of statistical tools and econometric models; and Excellent command of written and spoken English. Bonus skills Working knowledge of geospatial methods, like ArcGIS. Basic understanding of principles in economic theory, such as demand-supply mechanisms and pricing in markets, analysis of market interventions, etc. Experience with Python and LaTeX. What We Offer The appointment will commence in January 2027 on a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered.  Benefits include annual leave, medical benefits and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537693 Research Assistant I Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537693 Research Assistant I Department of Real Estate and Construction (01200) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537709/postdoctoral-fellow-in-transport-urban-environment-and-spatial-data-science": {
