    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537712/executive-officer-clerk-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-programme-manager-executive-assistant": {
      "title": "Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537712 Work type: Full-time Department: Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (60380) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) in the Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (several posts) (Ref: 537712) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, and with the possibility of renewal) The Academic Liaison Office, encompassing the International Affairs Office, Mainland Affairs Office, and HKU Summer Institute, is dedicated to fostering academic excellence, international collaboration, and cross-cultural exchange.  As our team continues to expand, we are excited to recruit multiple talented and dedicated Programme Managers and Executive Assistants to support the management of our growing programmes. Applicants should hold a good Bachelor's degree, preferably with at least 3 years' work experience in tertiary institutions.  They should also have a strong command of spoken and written English and Chinese (fluency in Putonghua is an advantage); strong organisational, communication, and problem-solving skills; as well as an outgoing personality.  They must be able to work independently with initiative and under pressure.  Flexibility to work outside normal office hours and on weekends is necessary, along with the willingness to undertake occasional travel.  Applicants with less experience may be considered for the post of Executive Assistant. The appointees will play a key role in overseeing the development and implementation of HKU Summer Institute programmes.  This includes liaising with internal departments, international partners, and external organisations to ensure seamless coordination.  The role also involves coordinating student recruitment and managing administrative duties such as programme logistics, budgeting, documentation, reporting, and other duties as assigned by the Office Head. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref. 537242) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 21, 2026 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 21, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 21, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537712 Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (60380) Nov 21, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537712 Executive Officer / Clerk II (holding the functional title of Programme Manager / Executive Assistant) Academic Liaison Office of the Registry (60380) Nov 21, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537614/lecturer-in-bioinformatics-in-the-school-of-biomedical-sciences": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Bioinformatics in the School of Biomedical Sciences",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Lecturer in Bioinformatics in the School of Biomedical Sciences The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537614 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Lecturer in Bioinformatics in the School of Biomedical Sciences (Ref.: 537614), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal. Applicants should have a PhD degree in bioinformatics, computational biology, genomics, biomedical data science, or a related discipline, with at least 3 years of relevant experience. Excellent motivation in teaching and learning should be demonstrated in teaching bioinformatics and related disciplines. The appointee will contribute to the bioinformatics, biomedical sciences, biochemistry, medicine, nursing and pharmacy undergraduateand postgraduate programmes. Applicants should also have strong communication and organisational skills, the ability to work independently and as a team, and be able to multitask. The appointee will be responsible for teaching, conducting tutorials and demonstrations, supporting curriculum design, and developing teaching materials. He/She will work closely with a team of colleagues dedicated to the development and delivery of innovative pedagogical approaches to improve student learning across the undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. At current rates, salary tax does not exceed 15% of gross income. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary. The University only accepts online applications for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. together with a teaching statement. Review of applications will start from November 2, 2026 and continue until 30 November 2026, or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537614 Lecturer in Bioinformatics in the School of Biomedical Sciences School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537614 Lecturer in Bioinformatics in the School of Biomedical Sciences School of Biomedical Sciences (22600) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
