    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537570/senior-it-assistant": {
      "title": "Senior IT Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior IT Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537570 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Nursing (20800) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior IT Assistant in the School of Nursing (Ref.: 537570) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with a contract-end gratuity and University contributions to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology, or a related discipline, with preferably at least 2 years of post-qualification work experience.  Experience in a tertiary institution or the education sector would be an advantage.  They should have sound knowledge of Microsoft Windows, macOS and Office applications, as well as experience in helpdesk support, photography and videography.  Excellent communication skills and a strong sense of responsibility are essential.  Solid experience in web application development using CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, PHP, ASP.NET, PL/SQL and HTML5 is required.  Competence in troubleshooting and maintaining computers and AV equipment would be advantageous.  They should also be a good team player, self-motivated and able to work under pressure. The appointee will provide IT technical support, photography, videography and audiovisual assistance for various academic programmes, events and workshops; assist with venue setup; troubleshoot and maintain computing and AV facilities; provide technical support to staff members; and perform other duties as assigned.  He/She may occasionally be required to work on weekends. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Review of applications will commence on November 3, 2026 and continue until December 15, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537570 Senior IT Assistant School of Nursing (20800) Dec 15, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537570 Senior IT Assistant School of Nursing (20800) Dec 15, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
