    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537577/clerical-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerical Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Clerical Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537577 Work type: Full-time Department: Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Clerical Assistant in the Clinical Trials Centre (Ref.: 537577) The Clinical Trials Centre (HKU-CTC) is a leading clinical trials management platform established under The University of Hong Kong LKS Faculty of Medicine (HKUMed) and is dedicated to managing and facilitating international-standard clinical trials on new drugs, medical devices and medical technologies. HKU-CTC offers long-term development opportunities to passionate talents who are devoted to a career in the clinical trial profession. HKU-CTC’s Phase 1 Clinical Trials Unit (Phase 1 Unit) is a professional clinical trials facility located in the Queen Mary Hospital and dedicated to conducting phase 1 and early phase clinical trials in a clinical setting. The Phase 1 Unit is seeking talents who have the passion in promoting healthcare advancement through practising clinical research. Main Responsibilities: Provide administrative and reception support for daily unit operations; Coordinate equipment and facility maintenance; Assist with petty cash, allowances, invoice processing, and payment verification; Support staff roster management and inventory control; and Assist in vendor evaluation and procurement to support clinical operations. Requirements: Completed Form 5 or above; Extensive administrative experience, preferably in a clinical setting; Familiarity with ward and clinical operations is preferred; Proficient in Microsoft Office and Windows; Strong communication, problem-solving, and multitasking abilities; Self-motivated, detail-oriented, and a team player; and Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. The appointment will commence as soon as possible on 2-year fixed-term basis or a 1-year temporary basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance.  A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  Appointment on 2-year fixed term basis will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary. Application Procedure: The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will start from November 3, 2026 and continue until November 19, 2026 or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 19, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537577 Clerical Assistant Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 19, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537577 Clerical Assistant Clinical Trials Centre (21180) Nov 19, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
