    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537651/parttime-teaching-assistant": {
      "title": "Part-time Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Hourly-paid 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Part-time Teaching Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537651 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Hourly-paid Department: Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong The Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (IHSS) invites applications for the position of Part-time Teaching Assistant (Ref. 537651) for the Common Core course CCHU9096: From Malthus to Modernity: A Global History of Economic Growth , for Semester 2 of the 2026-27 academic year. The appointment period is between January and May 2027. The course outline can be found here: https://commoncore.hku.hk/cchu9096/ Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in economic history, economics, history, or a related discipline. Postgraduate students (MPhil or PhD) would be particularly welcome. Good communication skills and proficiency in English are essential. Applicants should also have the ability to facilitate discussion-based learning among undergraduate students. Experience in teaching, grading assignments and presentations, providing academic feedback, and/or working with historical and quantitative evidence will be an advantage. The appointee will assist the course instructor in delivering CCHU9096: From Malthus to Modernity: A Global History of Economic Growth . He/she will assist with the preparation of teaching materials, class logistics, marking and grading assignments, and other teaching-related duties as assigned. Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants should submit a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae alongside their application via the system. Review of applications will commence immediately and continue until November 14, 2026 , or until the post is filled. Shortlisted candidates may be invited to attend an interview. For enquiries about the position, please contact Professor Sijie Hu, at sijiehu@hku.hk. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 14, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537651 Part-time Teaching Assistant Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Nov 14, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537651 Part-time Teaching Assistant Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Nov 14, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537652/parttime-teaching-assistant": {
      "title": "Part-time Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Fractional / Part-time 1 Hourly-paid 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Part-time Teaching Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537652 Work type: Fractional / Part-time, Hourly-paid Department: Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong The Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (IHSS) invites applications for the position of Part-time Teaching Assistant (Ref. 537652) for the Common Core course CCGL9069: Multinationals and the Global Economy , for Semester 2 of the 2026-27 academic year. The appointment period is between January and May 2027. The course outline can be found here: https://commoncore.hku.hk/ccgl9069/ Applicants should possess a Bachelor's degree or above in History, Economics, Business, Global Studies, International Political Economy, Social Sciences, or a related discipline. Preference will be given to current or recent postgraduate students or candidates with prior experience in teaching, tutoring, student assessment or research experience in areas related to globalization, multinational corporations, international business, economic history, global capitalism, or related fields. Applicants should also have excellent communication and interpersonal skills, a strong command of written and spoken English, and the ability to facilitate discussion-based learning among undergraduate students. Experience in grading coursework and providing academic feedback will be an advantage. The appointee will assist the course instructor in the delivery of CCGL9069: Multinationals and the Global Economy . Duties will include: Conducting and facilitating tutorial classes; Leading discussions on course themes and readings; Marking and providing feedback on student assessments, including tutorial presentations, reflective journals, group projects, and class participation; Assisting in the preparation of tutorial materials and learning activities; Holding consultation sessions and providing academic support to students as required; Assisting with course administration and other teaching-related duties assigned by the course instructor. Remuneration will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants should submit a cover letter and an up-to-date curriculum vitae alongside their application via the system. Review of applications will commence immediately and continue until November 14, 2026 , or until the post is filled. Shortlisted candidates may be invited to attend an interview. For enquiries about the position, please contact Professor Ghassan Moazzin, at gmoazzin@hku.hk. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 14, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537652 Part-time Teaching Assistant Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Nov 14, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537652 Part-time Teaching Assistant Hong Kong Institute for the Humanities and Social Sciences (45400) Nov 14, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537661/clerical-assistant": {
      "title": "Clerical Assistant",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Clerical Assistant The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537661 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Clerical Assistant in the Faculty of Social Sciences (Ref: 537661 ), to commence as soon as possible on a two-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Qualifications 5 passes in HKCEE including English Language (min. Grade C if Syllabus B/Level 2 from 2007) and Chinese Language (Level 2 from 2007), OR min. Level 2 or equivalent in 5 subjects in HKDSE including English Language and Chinese Language, preferably with at least 2 years’ relevant work experience. A fair command of English and Chinese (including Putonghua). Basic skill in English and Chinese word processing. Proficiency in MS Word and Excel. Good manners with strong communication and interpersonal skills. Punctual, with a strong sense of responsibility, self-motivated, and attentive to detail. Able to multitask, work independently, and as part of a team. Responsibilities Support the daily operation of the Faculty Office, including managing the reception counter and answering enquiries. Perform clerical duties such as data entry, collating and filing documents, updating databases, maintaining the office calendar, scheduling meetings, and coordinating appointments. Manage the room booking system and handle other venue-related requests for meetings and events. Support meetings and events by preparing venues, serving refreshments, and providing onsite logistics support. Monitor and replenish office supplies, report issues related to office equipment and facilities to relevant parties and coordinate maintenance orders. Submit procurement requests for purchases or service engagements. Maintain a tidy and professional office environment, and coordinate cleaning tasks. Perform other duties as assigned by supervisors to support the overall office operations. When necessary, work outside normal office hours or on weekends to support special events. What We Offer A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of the basic salary. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV. Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 13, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier.  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and/or written test. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537661 Clerical Assistant Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537661 Clerical Assistant Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537662/辦公室服務員-office-attendant": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories General Support Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 辦公室服務員 (Office Attendant) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537662 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Categories: General Support Staff Hong Kong 全職辦公室服務員 ( 檔案編號： 537662) 應徵者須具備中三或以上程度學歷，能操流利廣東話，並具備簡單英語及普通話溝通能力；能閱讀及書寫簡單中、英文更佳。應徵者須主動積極、守時盡責、具工作效率，能同時處理多項職務，並具良好服務態度及團隊合作精神。具相關辦公室支援、清潔、場地支援或雜務工作經驗者將獲優先考慮。 受聘者須負責提供學院辦公室及場地支援服務，主要職責包括： 執行日常清潔及整理工作，保持辦公室、會議室及公共地方整潔； 協助分派及跟進清潔員工的工作； 預備會議茶水及提供會議支援； 接聽一般查詢電話及協助處理日常事務查詢； 送遞及分派信件、文件及其他物品及協助文件歸檔； 協調及安排維修事宜，並跟進相關進度； 張貼海報、通告及宣傳物品； 協助活動及會議的場地佈置、整理及還原工作； 點算、搬運及整理物資、設備及用品； 執行其他由主管指派的職務；及 如有需要，於正常辦公時間以外或週末工作，以支援特別活動。 受聘者須能適應體力勞動工作，包括搬運物品、整理場地及支援不同活動安排。入職薪酬將按受聘者之學歷及相關工作經驗釐定。僱員福利包括有薪假期及醫療福利。 職位以兩年合約形式聘用，合約期滿時可獲約滿酬金及大學按強積金計劃所規定的供款，合共為薪金總額的百分之十；若工作表現滿意，可獲考慮續約。 大學只接受透過網上系統遞交的申請。應徵者請到大學人才招聘網站遞交網上申請及上載最新個人履歷。遴選程序將盡快開始，直至截止申請日期 2026 年 11 月 13 日 ，或至空缺填補，以較早者為準。 Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 13, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537662 辦公室服務員 (Office Attendant) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 13, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537662 辦公室服務員 (Office Attendant) Faculty of Social Sciences (30000) Nov 13, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537668/accounting-executive": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Accounting Executive The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537668 Work type: Full-time Department: Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Accounting Executive, Capital Estate Projects Team in the Finance and Enterprises Office (Ref.: 537668) The Role The appointee will assist in the following areas: preparation of journal entries, data input, budgetary control matters; submission of expenditure claims of capital projects to funding bodies; reconciliation of expenses reports and final accounts for capital projects; handling claims of government rent and rates for the University; preparation of bank reconciliations for month-end closing; preparation of accounting schedules for year-end audits; and undertaking any other ad hoc duties as assigned. Qualifications and Qualities 5 passes in HKCEE including English Language (minimum grade C if Syllabus A/Level 2 from 2007), Chinese Language (Level 2 from 2007) and Mathematics, OR minimum Level 2 or equivalent in HKDSEE in 5 subjects including English Language, Chinese Language and Mathematics; at least 1 year of work experience, preferably in the accounting and auditing field; hands-on knowledge of MS Office applications; good command of both written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua); good communication and interpersonal skills; and ability to work both independently and collaboratively as a team member in a fast-paced environment. What We Offer The appointment will be made on fixed-term full-time contract for 2 years, to commence as soon as possible with the possibility of renewal. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, together with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme at 10% of basic salary. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 19,2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 19, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537668 Accounting Executive Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Nov 19, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537668 Accounting Executive Finance and Enterprises Office (60500) Nov 19, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537675/programme-manager": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Non-Faculty Units 1 Programme Manager The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537675 Work type: Full-time Department: Admissions Office of the Registry (60381) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Programme Manager (at the rank of Executive Officer) in the Admissions Office of the Registry (Ref.: 537675) ( to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, and with the possibility of renewal) Applicants should hold a good Bachelor's degree with at least 3 years of work experience, preferably in the education sector.  Previous experience in programme design, operations, promotions, event management, and international student admissions in tertiary education institutions would be a plus.  They should be good team players with excellent organisational and interpersonal skills, and able to work independently on multiple tasks.  Commitment to quality results, excellent time and detail management, good problem-solving skills, and a proactive work attitude are essential qualities for the position. The appointee will be responsible for designing and executing year-round programmes for international secondary students in collaboration with university faculties, departments, and external vendors.  They will plan and initiate various student activities and perform any other duties as assigned by the Head of the Office.  They may be required to work outside normal office hours and on weekends. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online applications for the above post.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V.  Closes November 8, 2026 .  Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a written test and an interview. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 8, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537675 Programme Manager Admissions Office of the Registry (60381) Nov 8, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537675 Programme Manager Admissions Office of the Registry (60381) Nov 8, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
