    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537688/dean-of-business-and-economics": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Senior Management / Officers 1 Faculty Faculty of Business and Economics 1 Dean of Business and Economics Ref.: 537688 Work type: Full-time Department: Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Categories: Senior Management / Officers Dean of Business and Economics The University Founded in 1911, the University of Hong Kong has attained its pre-eminence as a research-led comprehensive university through upholding the highest international standards of excellence in its research pursuits, scholarship, teaching and learning, and service to the community. The University is consistently ranked amongst the world’s top universities: 11th in QS World University Rankings 2027, 1st in the QS Asia University Rankings 2026 and 33rd in Times Higher Education World University Rankings 2026. In recent years, the University was ranked multiple times as the most international University in the world. Home to ten disciplinary Faculties (Architecture, Arts, Business and Economics, Dentistry, Education, Engineering, Law, Medicine, Science, and Social Sciences), the University is committed to fostering interdisciplinary exchange with an outlook for transformative breakthroughs, innovations and global impact. There are 45,303 undergraduate and postgraduate students from 104 countries and regions, and more than 10,000 academic, academic-related and administrative staff. The University has embarked on a number of ambitious infrastructure and facilities projects for future expansion in Hong Kong’s Northern Metropolis, Beijing, Shanghai, Shenzhen and Europe. The Faculty The Faculty of Business and Economics, known as HKU Business School, is one of Asia’s foremost business schools and a globally recognised centre for research and education in business and economics. Since its establishment in 2001, the Faculty has grown rapidly in scale, reach and academic standing. It is ranked 1st in Asia and 6th globally in the 2025 UTD Top 100 Business School Research Rankings, and 1st in Asia and 11th globally for research in the Financial Times Global MBA Ranking 2026. The Faculty holds AACSB International and EQUIS accreditation. There are 9,493 undergraduate and postgraduate students, and more than 840 academic, academic-related and administrative staff in the Faculty. The Faculty brings together an internationally distinguished and diverse academic community across six academic areas — Accounting and Law, Economics, Finance, Innovation and Information Management, Management and Strategy, and Marketing. Its scholars produce rigorous and impactful research that advances academic knowledge and informs business practice and public policy. The Faculty offers a comprehensive portfolio of undergraduate, taught postgraduate, MBA, EMBA, DBA, executive education and research postgraduate programmes. Its research centres and institutes, together with the Wealth Management Academy, promote interdisciplinary scholarship and knowledge exchange across a broad range of fields, including Asian business and case research, economic policy and strategy, the Chinese economy and quantitative history, financial innovation and wealth management, entrepreneurship, the digital economy and innovation, sustainability, socio-economic inequality, and behavioural and decision science. Deeply rooted in Hong Kong, closely engaged with the Chinese Mainland and internationally connected, the Faculty has established an extensive network through its centres in Beijing, Shanghai and Shenzhen and its representative office in Vietnam. It is further extending its global footprint through HKU Europe in Barcelona, HKU’s first European campus. The incoming Dean will lead the Faculty at an important stage of its development, including overseeing its phased transition to the new Pokfield Campus and advancing its continued growth in research, education, global engagement and societal impact. Further information about the Faculty is available at www.hkubs.hku.hk . The Position The Dean will provide academic and strategic leadership to the Faculty.  He/She will provide a supportive research environment, commit to excellence in education, foster a collegial culture in the Faculty, and have a vision for developing and implementing new strategies for the Faculty.  He/She will be responsible for building a close and extensive network with the business community, attend to the students’ experience, fund-raising, and furthering the mission of the Faculty and the University.  The position carries the status and title of Professor.  The successful candidate is expected to assume the position in the summer of 2027.  The appointment will be for a five-year term, subject to renewal. The Person The successful candidate should be an outstanding scholar at full Professor level or above, with distinguished international standing. Qualifications and Qualities A doctoral (Ph.D.) or equivalent degree in Business, Economics, or a closely related discipline Record of distinguished scholarship and professional excellence Active engagement with business and government for teaching, research and service Proven administrative experience, with demonstrated capacity in strategic planning, financial stewardship, talent development, and stakeholder engagement Global outlook combined with a commitment to excellence in business education and high-impact research for the University and Hong Kong as a whole Deep understanding and appreciation of the higher education landscape in Hong Kong, the Chinese Mainland, the Asia-Pacific region, and globally Excellent leadership, interpersonal, communication and team-building skills Demonstrable success in fostering interdisciplinary cooperation, fundraising, knowledge transfer, and partnership development. Nominations and Applications Nominations, expression of interest and applications should be directed to Odgers via email at HKU_DeanFBE@odgers.com in confidence. Review of nominations and applications will begin now and will continue until the post is filled.  The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency. Advertised: Oct 20, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Back to search results Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537688 Dean of Business and Economics Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537688 Dean of Business and Economics Faculty of Business and Economics (07000) Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537519/senior-technical-officer-technical-officer-in-proteomics-and-metabolomics-core": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer in Proteomics and Metabolomics Core The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537519 Work type: Full-time Department: Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Categories: Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer in Proteomics and Metabolomics Core of the Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) (Ref.: 537519) (to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance) We are Expanding | Come and Join Us Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (CPOS) is an academic research-support centre embracing multi-omics and big data biomedical research under the LKS Faculty of Medicine. CPOS core laboratories host state-of-the-art technology platforms with sophisticated equipment supported by over 70 dedicated members. Welcome to visit https://cpos.hku.hk to explore more. Career Prospects Excellent on-job training Long-term development opportunities Exposures and interactions with world-class research groups Expert technical and managerial career track The Role Operate sophisticated scientific instruments (HPLC, GC, QQQ, Q-TOF, Orbitrap, QTRAP, etc.) to support core services and research Liaise with users to coordinate service logistics Provide technical advice to users Evaluate and validate new technologies Qualifications and Qualities Master’s degree or above in Analytical Chemistry, Biomedical Sciences, Biological Sciences, Biochemistry or a related discipline At least 2-3 years of relevant laboratory experience in proteomics Experience in operating and maintaining state-of-the-art equipment (HPLC, GC, QQQ, Q-TOF, Orbitrap, QTRAP, etc.) that facilitate cutting-edge translational research Working knowledge of MS-based technologies and previous work experience in a core facility with strong analytical and problem-solving skills is a definite advantage Self-motivated, responsible, conscientious, meticulous and capable of working collaboratively in a team environment Proficient in both written and spoken English and Chinese Competent in MS Office applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) Candidates with higher qualifications or more experience may be considered for appointment as Senior Technical Officer Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview. Those who have responded to the previous advertisement (Ref.: 537237) need not re-apply. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave, medical benefits, continuing professional development, and free access to on-campus gyms and libraries. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online at the University’s careers site ( https://jobs.hku.hk ) and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until October 31, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 1, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Oct 31, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537519 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer in Proteomics and Metabolomics Core Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537519 Senior Technical Officer / Technical Officer in Proteomics and Metabolomics Core Centre for PanorOmic Sciences (22200) Oct 31, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537541/it-support-technician-at-the-rank-of-research-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "IT Support Technician (at the rank of Research Assistant II)",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Executive / Technical / Support 1 Research Staff 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 IT Support Technician (at the rank of Research Assistant II) The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537541 Work type: Full-time Department: The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Categories: Research Staff, Executive / Technical / Support Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as IT Support Technician (at the rank of Research Assistant II) in the Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention, Faculty of Social Sciences, to commence as soon as possible, on a temporary basis for up to one year, with University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, and with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. Duties and Responsibilities Provide day-to-day technical support to Centre staff and assist in resolving IT-related issues; Assist in the maintenance of IT systems, platforms and equipment used for data collection and project implementation; Support the procurement, setup, inventory management and maintenance of IT equipment; Assist in liaising with vendors on system support, survey platforms, website maintenance and other IT-related services; Provide support for website updates, database maintenance, data storage, data security and server-related matters; Assist in IT project implementation, including system upgrades, data migration, web application testing and user support; Help maintain procedures, guidelines and documentation relating to data management and IT security; Provide technical support for research projects, events and meetings when needed; and Perform other ad-hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science or a related discipline; Relevant work experience in IT support, system maintenance, web support, database management or related areas; Knowledge of computer hardware, software, networking, web applications and database systems; Experience in website maintenance, survey systems, data management, server support and/or IT equipment procurement would be an advantage; Experience in photography, photo editing, and/or video editing is advantageous; Relevant work experience in the higher education sector, preferably in a university setting, would be a definite advantage; Good problem-solving skills and the ability to provide timely technical support; Good communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain technical matters to non-technical users; A responsible, detail-minded and service-oriented attitude; The ability to work independently and as part of a team; and A good command of written and spoken English and Chinese. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend an interview and written test. What We Offer The appointment will be made on a temporary basis for up to one year, to commence as soon as possible, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability. University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme will be provided. A competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered. Other benefits include annual leave and medical benefits, where applicable. How to Apply The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date C.V. Review of applications will start as soon as possible and continue until November 3 0 , 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. The University is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to equality, ethics, inclusivity, diversity and transparency Advertised: Sep 30, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537541 IT Support Technician (at the rank of Research Assistant II) The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537541 IT Support Technician (at the rank of Research Assistant II) The Hong Kong Jockey Club Centre for Suicide Research and Prevention (30002) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537728/tenuretrack-professor-associate-professor-assistant-professor-several-posts-in-the-division-of-epidemiology-and-biostatistics-school-of-public-health": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professoriate Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 Tenure-Track Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537728 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Public Health (22400) Categories: Professoriate Staff Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Tenure-track Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health (Ref.: 537728), to commence as soon as possible, on a three-year fixed-term basis, with the possibility of renewal, and consideration for tenure before the expiry of a second three-year fixed-term contract, subject to satisfactory performance. Exceptionally outstanding candidates may be considered for appointment on tenure terms. Applicants should possess (i) a Ph.D. degree or equivalent in epidemiology, biostatistics, public health, or a related discipline; (ii) prior research experience in infectious disease modelling and epidemiology; (iii) a strong track record of high-quality research as indicated by publication record and external grants; (iv) evidence of international recognition with a demonstrated ability to work across disciplines towards new research initiatives; and (v) a strong commitment to teaching students at both undergraduate and postgraduate levels. The appointees are expected to conduct independent and collaborative scholarly research, publish research articles in high-impact journals, and attract competitive grants to maintain active research programmes; take part in teaching undergraduate and postgraduate programmes, and supervise research postgraduate students; and perform administrative duties. The appointment rank will be determined based on qualifications and experience of the successful candidate. The School of Public Health is committed to protecting and enhancing the health for all people, through the synthesis of state-of-the-science research, the dissemination of knowledge through education and training and effective evidence-based public health advocacy. The School is structured into six academic divisions: Behavioural Sciences, Community Medicine and Public Health Practice, Epidemiology and Biostatistics, Health Economics, Policy and Management, Kinesiology, and Public Health Laboratory Sciences. To learn more about the School, please visit http://sph.hku.hk . A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits.  At current rates, salaries tax does not exceed 15% of gross income.  The appointment will attract a contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 15% of basic salary.  Housing benefits will also be provided as applicable. The University only accepts online applications for the above posts.  Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV, a research statement, and a teaching statement. Please state in the application form the position you are applying for, and provide contact emails of three referees. Please include in the CV your ORCID website link, H-index (as per Scopus), total number of international peer-reviewed publications, and the number of senior-authored papers. Review of applications will start from December 28, 2026 and continue until April 28, 2027 , or until the posts are filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 27, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Apr 28, 2027 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537728 Tenure-Track Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Apr 28, 2027 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537728 Tenure-Track Professor/ Associate Professor/ Assistant Professor (several posts) in the Division of Epidemiology and Biostatistics, School of Public Health School of Public Health (22400) Apr 28, 2027 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537435/高級講師講師": {
      "title": "HKU Careers",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Teaching Staff 1 Faculty Li Ka Shing Faculty of Medicine 1 高級講師／講師 The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537435 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Chinese Medicine (22100) Categories: Teaching Staff Hong Kong 香港大學中醫藥學院現誠聘 高級講師 / 講師 (檔案編號：537435) (以兩年合約形式聘用，若工作表現滿意，可獲續約) 應徵者須具備: (一) 認可中醫藥大學頒發之全日制中醫本科學歷及中醫學或相關學科博士學位；(二) 香港註冊中醫資格；及(三) 十五年或以上於高等院校從事中醫教學和臨床工作的經驗。 應徵者須 能主講相關中醫課程，並承擔各科中醫基礎和臨床教學工作。具備內科、外科、婦科、兒科或腫瘤科等的教學和臨床經驗者將獲優先考慮。 於相關學科或專業領域上有突出學術成就者可獲考慮聘任為高級講師。 受聘者主要負責本科及碩士課程教學、臨床和帶教工作。受聘為高級講師者需領導學科、設計及統籌課程。 入職薪酬將按受聘者的學歷及相關工作經驗釐定。受聘者於合約期滿可獲約滿酬金及大學按退休計劃所規定之供款，合共薪金總和的百分之十五。其他僱員福利包括有薪假期及醫療福利，合資格的高級講師可享有房屋福利。 大學只接受透過網上系統遞交 的申請。應徵者請到大學人才招聘網站遞交網上申請及上載最新的個人履歷。截止申請日期為 2026 年 12 月 15 日 。大學感謝應徵者的申請，唯只有獲甄選參加面試的應徵者才會收到通知。 Advertised: Oct 27, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Dec 15, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537435 高級講師／講師 School of Chinese Medicine (22100) Dec 15, 2026 Featured jobs Provost and Deputy Vice-Chancellor Vice-President and Pro-Vice-Chancellor (Global) Dean of Business and Economics Chief Information Officer and University Librarian Director of the Development & Alumni Affairs Office HKU Global Professoriate Recruitment Campaign Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537435 高級講師／講師 School of Ch