    "https://jobs.hku.hk/cw/en/job/537721/administrative-assistant-ii-holding-the-functional-title-of-school-manager-in-the-school-of-future-media": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of School Manager) in the School of Future Media",
      "description": "HKU Careers - Career Opportunities Skip to content HKU Home Home Start main Content Career Opportunities Home Explore Careers at HKU Career Opportunities Applicant login Job alert Internal openings Job Search e.g. Professor Refine Search Work type Full-time 1 Categories Professional & Management 1 Faculty Faculty of Social Sciences 1 Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of School Manager) in the School of Future Media The University of Hong Kong Apply now Ref.: 537721 Work type: Full-time Department: School of Future Media (31200) Categories: Professional & Management Hong Kong Applications are invited for appointment as Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of School Manager) in the School of Future Media (Ref: 537721), to commence as soon as possible, on a two-year fixed-term basis, with contract-end gratuity and University contribution to a retirement benefits scheme, totalling up to 10% of basic salary, with the possibility of renewal subject to satisfactory performance. Applicants should possess a good Bachelor’s degree in social sciences, accounting, finance, or equivalent, with at least 8 years of relevant work experience, including at least 3 years in a supervisory role, preferably in tertiary education institutions. They should have excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills, as well as excellent time management, multitasking, and problem-solving abilities, and the ability to work independently and under pressure. The appointee should have excellent command of written and spoken English and Chinese (including Putonghua) and possess strong human resources, accounting, budget management, and financial data analysis skills, as well as strong IT capabilities in Microsoft Office.  They should also have a good sense of tact in dealing with sensitive and confidential issues, including discreet handling of personal and confidential matters. The appointee will play a versatile role in managing the administrative work related to human resources and finance, and special projects management.  He/She will provide general administrative and secretarial support on a wide range of matters, including recruitment and appointment, budget monitoring, financial data organisation, data analysis, report preparation, committee support, office management, team supervision, and perform any other duties as assigned. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to attend a written test and an interview. A highly competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience will be offered, in addition to annual leave and medical benefits. The University only accepts online application for the above post. Applicants should apply online and upload an up-to-date CV.  Review of applications will commence as soon as possible and continue until November 30, 2026 , or until the post is filled, whichever is earlier. Advertised: Oct 28, 2026 (HK Time) Applications close: Nov 30, 2026 (HK Time) Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537721 Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of School Manager) in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Nov 30, 2026 Featured jobs Current opportunities Ref. Posting Title Department Closing Date 537721 Administrative Assistant II (holding the functional title of School Manager) in the School of Future Media School of Future Media (31200) Nov 30, 2026 Powered by PageUp Copyright © 2026\n                Human Resources Office,\n                The University of Hong Kong. All Rights Reserved."
